The wife of a police officer in Kandal province shot herself because of a physical illness, leaving three letters describing her suffering
(Kandal): The wife of a police officer in Lvea Em district, Kandal province, shot herself with her husband's gun because she was upset and had three children left orphaned. The suicide occurred on the evening of May 20, 2019 at Kampong Teuk Tonle, Khsach village, Arey Ksat commune, Lvea Em district, Kandal province.
Kandal Provincial Police Commissioner Major General Eav Chamroeun confirmed that the victim who shot her husband with a gun was Nop Vanny, 34, a shopkeeper in Tuol Meas village, Arey Ksat commune, Lovea Em district, Kandal province, while her husband Ouk Chiva, 43. Occupation: Police Officer: Office of Investigation and Procedure of the General Department of Immigration.
The General Commissioner described that before the incident, the victim went to bathe in the Mekong River at Koh Khsach with her husband and 3 children (2 girls) and 2 nieces. While taking a bath in the river, the victim did not take a bath, but rested in the car. On the right flower petal, with a bullet attached to the forehead.
The victim's husband immediately took his wife home and went to complain to the police.
According to the victim's sister, Nop Srey Roth claimed that the victim had undergone surgery and was suffering from chronic illness and wanted to commit suicide several times.
According to Him Mean, the abbot of Wat Areyaksat claimed that the victim must have had a chronic illness and had been hospitalized for about half a month before intending to hang himself and take his own life.
However, for the suicide, the victim also left three letters describing her medical condition and the suffering at the time of the illness. Now, after examining all the bodies of the victims, the authorities have handed them over to their families for a traditional ceremony.
