(Phnom Penh): Mr. Pa Socheatvong, Member of the Central Committee of the Cambodian People's Party and Chairman of the Committee of the Cambodian People's Party in Phnom Penh, claimed that the massacre during the Khmer Rouge regime was the murder of the brutal Khmer leaders in In that regime, it was not because of Chinese influence as a reference.
The Khmer Rouge regime was one of the deadliest in Khmer history. More than 2 million Cambodians died under the regime in just 3 years, 8 months and 20 days. The Khmer Rouge regime is known to have close ties to the Chinese government.
Due to the close relationship between the Khmer Rouge regime and the Chinese government at that time, some Cambodians, including anti-government politicians, blamed the Khmer Rouge massacre on the Chinese government. .
Starting from the image of past relations between the Khmer Rouge leaders and the Chinese government led to such massacres, and only then did some citizens and politicians tend to oppose, dragging and fussing that the close relationship between the current Khmer government and The Chinese government may face the same traces of history as during the Khmer Rouge regime.
On the occasion of the National Day of Remembrance on May 20, a day commemorating the brutal actions of the Khmer Rouge, Pa Socheat acknowledged that under the Khmer Rouge regime, Cambodia was influenced by the Chinese government in geopolitics. But the massacre under the Khmer Rouge regime was a massacre between Cambodians and Cambodians, not because of orders or because China was the backbone of the Khmer Rouge.
