After recalling the tragedy that took place during the brutal regime, Mr. Thong Khon further introduced the electorate as follows:
* All constituencies - all communes must maintain good health, keep safe in commuting to work. During this time, voters do not have to travel far.
Voters must know the party number well, must be able to draw and vote for the party correctly.
* The electorate must check their election documents (such as ID card) to be able to vote.
* Must have good internal unity and solidarity.
* Strive to prevent any activities that attempt to divide the internal affairs of commune councilors or within the ranks of candidates or within the party.
Must be responsible for timely response to all propaganda, slander and incitement of the opposition in all its forms at the local level.
* Strive to review and address any necessary challenges and suggestions at the local level.
Working groups and parties at all levels must create conditions for commune councilors who are the electorate to go to the polls and vote for the CPP.
According to the National Election Committee (NEC), the opening ceremony of the election campaign for the Capital-Provincial Council and the Municipal-District-Khan Council of the third mandate will last for 8 days, starting from the 17th. May 24, 2019 and this by-election will be officially held on Sunday, May 26, 2019.
