(Preah Sihanouk): On the morning of May 20, 2019, Preah Sihanouk Provincial Administration celebrated the National Day of Remembrance on May 20 by inviting monks to pay their respects to the victims of the Pol Pot genocide. . The ceremony also included a memorial service for the victims of the brutal black-shirt era.
On that occasion, Mr. Yon Min, Governor of Sihanoukville Province, called on all Cambodians to participate in maintaining peace, rights and freedoms that Cambodia is fully enjoying today for a long and lasting future. He said that every year on May 20, the Royal Government of Cambodia designates the National Day of Remembrance for the genocidal regime of Democratic Kampuchea, which killed millions of innocent Cambodians.
