(Phnom Penh): Chip Mong organized a study tour for 16 second generation Chip Mong scholarship students to 3 large Chip Mong factories and other business ventures last weekend.
The two-day visit aims to provide an opportunity for the 16 students to learn about the business activities of the factory production chain and social activities of Chip Mong.
The first day of the tour includes a study tour of the production line at the Khmer Breweries factory, which produces Cambodian beer, Cambodian pure water, Cambodian orange juice, ice cream, juices, energy drinks, which is the largest beverage and beer factory in Cambodia. Area. The students also continued to visit the tile and pipe factory of Chip Mong Industries and received knowledge from experts in the production of pipes as well as high quality tiles.
The second day visit took place at the cement factory of Chip Mong Inc. Cement Corporation, located in Banteay Meas district, Kampot province.
In addition to financial support, Chip Mong regularly organizes educational programs to enhance the ability and leadership of the two generations of Chip Mong scholarship students, who are the future human resources for the nation's development.
It should also be noted that Chip Mong Company provides 15 scholarships with a scholarship amount of $ 6,000 to students who have just graduated from high school every year.
