It should be noted that Vesak is the most important religious festival among many other festivals because it commemorates the three major events of the time of Samma Samputa, the day on which the Buddha Birth is enlightened and is also the day of Nirvana.
And these three events occur on the 15th day of the full moon, which has a full moon in the same month Pisak, only different years.
On the occasion of the Vesak festival, a large number of people came to participate in this festival with happy faces accompanied by appropriate clothing in accordance with this religious festival.
In addition, during the celebration, people were observed praying for peace and lighting lanterns at night and meditating for 10 minutes.
