The National Bank of Cambodia sets out four monetary policies to maintain price stability and sustainable economic growth in Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): In order to maintain price stability and sustainable economic growth, the National Bank of Cambodia, through the Monetary Policy Committee, has decided to continue to implement four monetary policies. This is according to the announcement of the National Bank of Cambodia on "Results of the 47th Monetary Policy Committee Meeting".
The 47th Monetary Policy Committee meeting was attended by Mr. Chea Chanto, Governor of the National Bank of Cambodia and Chairman of the Monetary Policy Committee.
The meeting discussed the economic situation and the implementation of monetary policy in the first quarter and the direction for the coming quarter. In the first quarter of 2019, key macroeconomic indicators showed good progress. Inflation was low at an average of 1.9%, the exchange rate was 4,017 riel per US dollar, and the international dollar reserves increased, which could guarantee the import of goods and services for the next five months.
In order to maintain price stability and sustainable economic growth, the Monetary Policy Committee has decided to pursue the following monetary policy:
1: Continue to adopt a stable exchange rate regime by making the necessary interventions based on economic changes to further strengthen the public's trust in the riel.
2. Maintain a stable LPCO interest rate and supply liquidity in the amount of 800 billion riels per month or according to the assessment of economic needs.
3. Continue to promote the widespread use of the riel by increasing public awareness of the importance and role of the riel in the economy and society.
4: Continue to regularly monitor and evaluate the implementation of the Prakas of the National Bank of Cambodia on requiring banking and financial institutions to have a loan of at least 10% in KHR.
