Minister of Agriculture Inspects Durian Crops to Farmers and Inspects Nursery Stations in Kampong Cham Province
(Kampong Cham): Mr. Veng Sakhon, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, on May 17, 2019, inspected the durian planting of farmers and inspected two local nursery stations in Kampong Cham province.
The inspection took place after the completion of the opening ceremony of the provincial-municipal-district-district council election campaign for the third mandate in 2019 at the Tbong Khmum Provincial Party Office.
The Minister and his colleagues inspected Mr. Siv Phanny's durian plantation in Ar: Tnaot commune, Stung Trang district, Kampong Cham province. On that occasion, he asked about the health, livelihood, cultivation and durian crops that are popular in the market today.
Ms. Siv Phanny, the owner of the durian plantation, said that currently cultivating durian on an area of 4.5 hectares, harvesting 10 tons per hectare per season, there is a good market, the wholesale price is 20,000 riels per kilogram. Yields fluctuate according to the actual season, this year the weather is too hot, yields fall.
She added that plantation owners face climate problems and high interest rates.
In that, the Minister explained to the plantation owners four important issues, including:
1. Planting techniques, diseases and durian harvesting. 2. Procedures for exporting Cambodian agricultural products to international markets. Contract 4: Instruct the Director of the Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries of Kampong Cham Province to contact the Agricultural Bank of Vietnam, which is cooperating with the Ministry to study low-interest loans.
Mr. Veng Sakhon requested the Ministry of Mines and Energy to consider and implement the recommendation of the Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen on reducing the price of electricity for pumping water, the current price greatly affects the value added of agricultural products and this area has not been implemented. No.
On the same day, Mr. Veng Sakhon visited a nursery station in Prey Chhor district, Kampong Cham province.
Keo Omalis, the Royal Government of Cambodia's delegate in charge of the Forestry Administration, said the station now covers an area of 68 hectares, covered with teak trees planted in 1997, and a wedding garden with beng thnong and rosewood trees, which are being managed and preserved by officials. Sangkat Section and Khan Forestry Administration of Kampong Cham Province.
After inspecting the general condition of the station, the Minister praised the efforts and sense of responsibility of the Forestry Administration, especially the staff in the station.
Mr. Veng Sakhon advised all forest administrations to take care to maintain and preserve this area in a sustainable manner in order to preserve the forest, water source for the next generation, especially for farmers, to improve the administrative infrastructure and nursery. The saplings will be re-activated to attract tourists, create a source of income to serve the needs of the station and turn this area into an eco-tourism area in the future.
