All three events take place on the 15th day of the full moon, which has a full moon in the same month, but different years. All the countries that practice Buddhism in our Southeast Asian region, in the whole world, always celebrate Vesak Day, which all Buddhists have been celebrating for a long time.
Not only that, the Vesak festival is also considered by the United Nations to be remarkable, the United Nations on December 15, 1999 announced the recognition of Vesak as an international holiday with a request. From countries around the world that practice Buddhism, including Cambodia and named UN-Visak or Visak Bochea of the United Nations.
Why Buddhism can make the Vesak festival can be considered by the United Nations as an international festival.
Thus the emergence of the Buddha is seen as the birth of a great person in the world, because he is aware of things that science can not find, such as the psychic mind, Nirvana, which means that the enlightenment of God is Enlightenment by nature, true nature exists in the world, so God reveals these truths.
Of course, other religions are not insignificant, but he centrally states that when the Eight Noble Truths are in place, you follow them and make you happy. "Because the Dharma of the Buddha seems to bring peace to the world, the United Nations has decided to incorporate the Vesak festival into the world."
Of course, on the occasion of Vesak, in addition to the holidays from the work of the Cambodian people, all pagodas also celebrate this great religious festival. Including the counting of bowls and many other rituals, some pagodas have organized short-term initiation programs for Buddhists who want to build a shrine but do not have much time.
Traditionally, the Vesak festival is held at night in accordance with the word "Bon Mi", which means the full moon of Bon Mi. And on the night of Vesak, they light lanterns, burn incense to light the radiance, and also to open the opportunity for Buddhists to gather to perform meritorious deeds happily at night.
