A spokesman for the Ministry of Cults and Religions said that the Vesak Festival was held under the presidency of Samdech Vibol Sena Pheakdey Say Chhum, President of the Senate, along with a large number of government officials, Buddhists and students.
Vesak is one of the most important religious festivals in the world, as it commemorates three major events of the time of the Buddha's birth, the day he was born. Enlightenment and also the day of Nirvana. These three events occur on the 15th day of the full moon, which has a full moon in the same month of Pisak, except for the year.
