Preah Sihanouk: Dr. Seng Nong, director of Preah Sihanouk Provincial Referral Hospital, said that one of the five female patients died after being sent to the hospital on the evening of the 17th. May 2019.
He said that the relatives of the five patients were sent to the emergency room at the Sihanoukville Provincial Referral Hospital, each with full body pain and severe.
Dr. Seng Nong said that the patients were residents of the Sihanoukville Special Economic Zone and were likely to have mushroom poisoning, because according to relatives, after they ate food cooked from vegetables and mushrooms, there were no symptoms. Feeling sick, vomiting, nausea and pain in the body, difficulty breathing and so on.
Doctors at the Sihanoukville Referral Hospital added that most of the five people were in critical condition. After being sent to the hospital for treatment, a female patient died on the evening of May 17, 2019.
Doctors said the woman who was killed was among the five critically ill. He died after being taken to Sihanoukville Provincial Referral Hospital, but unfortunately doctors were unable to save his life due to his serious condition or he was sent too late.
