(Phnom Penh): On the afternoon of May 16th, 2019, Lt. Gen. Rath Sreang, Deputy Commander of the National Gendarmerie and Commander of the Phnom Penh Municipal Gendarmerie, held a meeting to disseminate professional work to officers of the Office of Specialization and Base of the Gendarmerie. The 12 districts to remind and strengthen the procedures for law enforcement, as well as to launch a plan to prevent and suppress crime more effectively.
Lt. Gen. Rath Sreang also reminded all officers and deputies to pay attention to the family economy, maintain good health, exercise regularly, especially to see at least one doctor. Or twice a year.
During this outreach meeting, Lt. Gen. Rath Sreang initiated 10 ideas, approaches and recommendations of the Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen and distributed them to the 12 military bases as well as the Phnom Penh Capital Command. To be displayed as a symbol to remind and remind them of their daily work, which includes the following content:
First, ready to defend the independence, national sovereignty, continue to strictly implement the people's national defense, because the army was born from the people and do everything for the well-being of the people.
Second, together with other forces to maintain peace, political stability, security, social order, participate in the implementation of safe village and commune policies, fight against theft, drugs, human trafficking and other inactions, to make our country a truly peaceful country. At all costs, do not let anyone undermine the hard-earned peace.
Fourth, let all the troops join other forces to help the people, especially when there is a disaster, the army, the children of the people, wherever they are, look after the well-being of the people, help the people who are having a hard time Do what we can to help the people, especially the poor, and not to make people cry because of the misconduct of our army.
Fifth, support law enforcement to ensure the protection of forests, fisheries and other natural resources. All troops must participate in preserving the forest, not become loggers or protectors of loggers. Contribute to the conservation of our rare fisheries, not to engage in illegal activities related to the fisheries sector that engage in illegal fishing. Must contribute to the conservation of other natural resources available in Cambodia.
Sixth, support the collection of national budget revenue at both the national and sub-national levels, and strive to prevent tax evasion and cross-border crime. Being together is not a separate task of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, the customs or tax authorities, but must be supported by all and each of us must fulfill the same tax obligations.
Seventh, strive to strengthen the discipline of the army, increase the capacity in all areas, training must be done regularly in all disciplines, more modern equipment, if people are not modern, it is equivalent to not having those equipment. Sweating on the training ground is better than bleeding on the battlefield, which means that sweating on the training ground reduces bleeding and death on the battlefield, and take this opportunity to try to lose weight.
Eighth, take care of all kinds of equipment that is the equipment for our army and check it regularly, must be maintained to ensure that our weapons can be used and targeted when available. Being on target.
Ninth: Pay attention to the life of the army so that our army has all the qualifications and health care, shelter, places, food, continue to pay more attention to the life of the army, and each unit is self-employed In addition to the state-provided regime, address the treatment thoroughly. At the same time, pay attention to the troops in the ranks, pay attention to the soldiers who have retired through the Veterans Association.
And 10th, the military must play the role of diplomat in building good relations with neighboring countries and building good relations with all friendly countries in the world. Through good relations with neighboring countries, which improves state-to-state relations, trade, investment and tourism relations are improved.
