Mr. Theng Sothol said that there should always be regular communication between the authorities and the law enforcement forces in their work, and visiting and visiting each other now or today is to get to know each other. And to better link the work of the authorities and the police force on security and law enforcement.
While meeting with the district police force, he urged Inspector Yin San to pay more attention to local security, management and law enforcement, especially street vendors. Distribute gifts to young children, pregnant women and minors at the 2nd Correctional Center in Phnom Penh
The visit was chaired by Ms. Nhep Sopheap, Secretary General of the General Secretariat of the Cambodian National Council for Children, Ms. Chham Mary, Director General of the Cambodian Human Rights Commission, and Ms. Som Sereyvath, Deputy Director General of the Human Resources Department of the Cambodian Red Cross, as well as many relevant officials. .
On that occasion, Ms. Nhep Sopheap also warned women detained in all educational centers to strive to change after serving their sentences and to be good people in society to be a shadow to all children and In particular, provide opportunities for these young children to go to school like other children.
She also added that through this education, repentance will give their children the opportunity to go to school outside through the child support team of the National Council of Cambodia for children in orphanages or organizations. To receive education, care and training in various skills as well.
Before concluding the visit, the representatives of the three institutions also urged all women detainees to abide by the internal regulations of the Correctional Center, try to stay away from drugs and other evils that harm society. The nation, in particular, must strive to study the knowledge and skills available in the training courses at this educational center for the benefit of themselves and their families.
General Ith Sarath told a delegation from the Bangladesh Army College that the defense sector was growing steadily under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen.
(Phnom Penh): General Ith Sarath, Deputy Commander-in-Chief and Joint Chief of Staff of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, confirmed to a delegation from the Faculty of Command of Bangladesh that the Cambodian defense sector has made steady progress under the guidance and guidance of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces. In the presence of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
This statement was made by General Ith Sarath on May 17, 2019, on the occasion that General Md Eneayet Ulah, Commander-in-Chief of the Staff College of the People's Republic of Bangladesh, led the delegation. Courtesy and discussion at the General Command of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces.
The General said that under the leadership of the head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the country has been peaceful and developed in all areas, including the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces has successfully fulfilled its role, especially defense. Territorial integrity, peacekeeping, according to the strategy of the Royal Government, the work of building the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces.
The General confirmed to the delegation that the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces (RCAF) has trained at all levels and in all fields, which makes every soldier capable enough to carry out the task of communication between the two countries. The two armies and the two governments have also exchanged visits. Mutually, as a result, the relationship between the two armies must also be strengthened.
In addition, the General also mentioned the cooperation between the two countries and the two armies to strengthen the diplomatic and military relations, which the two governments have done together in the past.
Training and cooperation on demining, disaster management, the possibility of cooperation between the two countries in preparation for natural disasters, especially rehabilitation and post-disaster reconstruction. Anti-terrorism is a special force of the Bangladesh Army that can train and conduct joint exercises with the Cambodian Anti-Terrorism Unit.
Kratie Cambodian People's Party Leaders Launch Third Mandate Council Election Campaign
(Kratie): Mr. Pich Bunthen, Member of the Central Committee of the Cambodian People's Party and Chairman of the Central Working Group for Kratie Province, led the provincial leadership and thousands of member officials to participate in the election campaign of the Municipal / District Council / Capital Council. Province The first day of the campaign this morning, May 17, 2019.
During the opening ceremony of the campaign, Mr. Pich Bunthen conveyed greetings and wishes from Samdech Techo Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian People's Party, Samdech Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin, Honorary President of the Krala Hom Sar Kheng Party, and Samdech Vibol Sena Pheakdey Say Chhum, Vice President of the Party. To party officials, party members, including all voters.
On the first day of the campaign, it was observed that only the Cambodian People's Party had launched a large-scale campaign with thousands of people participating with various means and equipment from all districts and cities throughout the province, with thousands of people participating. The procession.
Agriculture official: Throughout Preah Vihear province, there are 34 companies investing in economic land concessions on an area of nearly 200,000 hectares, today a company launched the first rubber plantation
(Preah Vihear): Mr. Peng Trida, Director of Preah Vihear Provincial Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries also confirmed that there are 34 companies investing in economic land concessions in Preah Vihear province on an area of 199,488 hectares. Of which, 15 companies invested in rubber plantations on a total area of 64,860 hectares planted 25,198 hectares of rubber and 3,454 hectares of family rubber.
Today, hundreds of hectares of Rithy Granite (Cambodia) rubber plantation in Romney commune, Rovieng district, Preah Vihear province, was inaugurated for the first time after nearly eight years of cultivation.
The ceremony was held in the presence of Mr. Peng Trida, Director of the Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries of Preah Vihear Province, and was attended by Mr. Oknha Leng Rithy, Director of Rithy Granite (Cambodia) and representatives of VRG member companies and rubber plantation investment staff. Many other workers.
Mr. Peng Trida said that Rithy Granite (Cambodia) Company has been approved by the Royal Government to provide 1,646 hectares of economic land concessions for investment in the development of agro-industrial crops, including rubber, acacia, cashew and many other crops.
The director of the Provincial Department of Agriculture said, "As for the rubber crop, which we are holding the opening ceremony for rubber now, it has been planted since 2011 on an area of 193 hectares. And the company has opened a rubber band on about 10% of the land. The company will expand the rubber plantations in the coming years to 100% of the total rubber plantation area and can absorb labor for about 400 workers.
Some companies grow agro-industrial crops such as sugar cane, corn, beans, pepper, cashew nuts, mango, turmeric and so on. He said the average price of rubber for dry rubber is about 3,800 riel per kilogram, while water for rubber is 1,300 riel per liter. People to continue development
On the morning of May 17, 2019, Mr. Oum Seiha, on behalf of Mr. Kong Vibol, presided over the opening ceremony of the 2019 Provincial Council Election Campaign for the 3rd Mandate District Council at the school. Lvea Em district.
The ceremony was also attended by Mr. Phim Phira, Chairman of Lvea Em District Party Committee, Ladies and Gentlemen, Permanent Members of the District Party Committee, Candidates of the District Council, Commune Council, as well as the Commune Party Committee and nearly 500 village party branches.
He added that with this peace, the CPP has greatly reduced poverty in Cambodia, and as of 2019, poverty in Cambodia is only around 10 percent. With this peace, the Cambodian economy has grown at around 7% every year, while in the world, the countries with economic growth at around 7% are not many.
He added that under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Lvea Em district, for the past three years, more than 70 kilometers of roads have been built, 12 schools (80 rooms) have been built, 6 bridges have been built and 4 more are under construction. In addition, 4 commune halls and 4 others are under construction, 2 kingdoms have been built, and these are not enough, the CPP will continue to build and develop more.
The Central Working Group to assist Lvea Em District also requested the authorities at all levels, including the three types of forces and the people to participate in maintaining security and order, especially to maintain the polling station by making it safe during the election and security. To all candidates and Commune / Sangkat Councils so that you can all go to the polls.
Ms. Khuon Sodary: Members of the Cambodian People's Party at all levels must maintain and continue to succeed in the 2023 election and beyond.
This statement was made by Ms. Kittisangkhab Dr. Khuon Sodary during a meeting with members of Commune / Sangkat Councils in Leuk Dek District, Kandal Province on Friday, May 17, 2562. 2019 with 170 members of the 3rd Mandate District Council Election Committee and the Central Working Group.
Ms. Kittisangha Bandith urged voters that under any circumstances, CPP members must dare to sacrifice everything to keep the party stable and continue to be the core of leading the country towards building a national society. Which ensures peace, social stability and sustainable development.
