(Koh Kong): A drug-addicted son did not show gratitude to his father, but burned his father's property, burning only the pillars of the house, but did not cause any harm. This incident happened at 10:00 on May 17, 2019 in Village 1, Sangkat Dang Tong, Khemarak Phoumin Municipality, Koh Kong Province.
The owner of the house, Uy Sopheak, 73, described at the scene that the incident was caused by his son setting himself on fire, as his son was addicted to drugs and could not control himself. He knows him. Every day he was not with.
He confirmed that his son, Kim Sambo, 43, who set fire to the house, lived in the house.
Fire officials said at the scene that in this case, three fire trucks ran out of water and prevented from spreading to the nearby house and took about 30 minutes.
According to a source from the authorities, it is very difficult to put out the fire because his people built houses almost all the way, making it impossible for cars to reach their destination. The fire brigade also asked residents to build houses near the road, please leave the road a little wider to facilitate cars in and out when something happens in the village.
Koh Kong CamControl Officers Seize Some Outdated Goods at Pak Klang Market, Mondul Seima District
(Koh Kong): In order to ensure food safety, CamControl Branch, Koh Kong Province, together with subordinates and trade officials, on May 17, 2019, inspected all items displayed by traders in Pak Klang Market, Mondul Seima District, Koh Kong Province. By focusing on any beverage product beyond the production date.
Mr. Sam Chentra, Deputy Chief of CamControl Branch in Koh Kong Province, said that the operation was based on the Law on Quality Management, Safety of Products and Services and Trade Facilitation through Risk Management. General Exterior of food to labels, packaging, dates, cans, rotten cans.
At the same time, the quality and compliance are checked by preliminary analysis of the product using a test kit to find banned chemicals such as porcine and formalin. In case of doubt, samples are sent to the laboratory for further analysis. General Department of CamControl to identify risks.
Mr. Sam Chentra continued that as a result, CamControl officers and professional officers inspected the beverages sold by the vendors at the stalls in Pak Klang market, Mondul Seima district, CamControl officers confiscated 1 bottle of soy sauce, 3 bottles of cooking oil and spray. 4 cans found by professional officers.
In this regard, the professional officers continuously and responsibly inspect and guide the traders have a higher understanding of this issue as well, and for the expired exhibits, the professional officers have kept them to wait for the demolition. Prudential Cambodia sponsors exercise equipment in Svay Rieng
(Svay Rieng): People in Svay Rieng can now exercise in a comfortable and fun environment after Prudential Cambodia, a leading life insurance company, sponsored a venue and gym equipment in a public park. Located in the provincial town.
In addition, Prudential Cambodia has sponsored more than 300 public park seats in eight provinces to encourage people to spend more time breathing in the fresh air outside their homes.
Mr. Nutman added, “The facilities and equipment we have sponsored in Svay Rieng now include bicycles, treadmills, treadmills, weight training equipment. "We are pleased that people in the community can come and use the equipment at this new gym and increase their recreational activities to help improve their health and well-being."
Mr. Nop Chamroeun, Governor of Svay Rieng City, also said: “By donating this gym equipment, Prudential is helping us to try to make (people) healthy. And the installation of safe and appropriate exercise equipment here will make it easier for people in Svay Rieng to use as they need.
For a resident of Svay Rieng City, Kong Sophon, these public exercise equipment are an incentive for her to start developing good exercise habits.
"The Prudential-sponsored gym allows seniors like me to exercise, which helps us relax and reduce stress, which makes us feel good," she said. When exercising every day for half an hour or more.
Laos ready to implement new policy to promote sustainable economic growth and high environmental considerations
(VOVworld) - The Central Committee of the Lao People's Revolutionary Party (LPRP) has approved a resolution requiring the Lao government to adhere to maintaining sustainable national economic growth and environmental considerations. This was quoted from the Chinese news agency Xinhua on Friday afternoon, May 17, 2019.
The committee, which makes policy decisions in Laos, approved the decision on the occasion of the closing session of the eighth session of the 10th party congress, which took place this week. According to the decision, one of the paths the Lao government must take is to improve the business and investment environment, which is considered a prerequisite for Laos to maintain its economic growth.
At the same time, while maintaining strong national economic growth is essential, the Lao Central Committee also stressed that this goal must be based on principles that are environmentally friendly and sustainable.
Deputy PM Aun Porn Moniroth Asks US Power Company to Help Solve Cambodia's Electricity Shortage
Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Economy and Finance, warmly welcomed Mr. John Chiray and his working group and emphasized that electricity plays an important role in the economic process through assurance and improvement. Increase business competition.
The Deputy Prime Minister said that cooperation with John Chirai's team is important, while the Ministry of Economy and Finance is cooperating with the Ministry of Mines and Energy, Electricite du Cambodge and other relevant institutions to address shortages. Electricity of Cambodia now and for the future.
The Deputy Prime Minister also requested Mr. John Chiray to continue to provide support on other important issues, including: 1. Continue to support the health and well-being of the people, 2. Solve the problem of electricity supply and 3. Help build capacity and learn more about lowering electricity prices in Cambodia.
Mr. John Chiray stated that he was very pleased to meet and discuss with the General Secretary, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Economy and Finance. He agreed and accepted the request of the Deputy Prime Minister, and his team will commit to continue to cooperate with the working group of the Ministry of Economy and Finance and relevant ministries to study these work and proposals.
The Deputy Prime Minister also thanked the GE Working Group for its contribution to strengthening Cambodia's economic sector, ensuring economic growth and sustainable development, livelihoods and environment, and wished the GE Working Group Collaborate with the inter-ministerial working group successfully as planned.
