The Royal "Plowing Ceremony" will be held at Kirivong Sok Sen Chey Stadium, Takeo Province on May 22, today the authorities are ready to protect security and order
(Takeo): On May 17, 2019, Takeo Provincial Police Commissioner, Major General Sok Samnang, organized a security force to inspect the geographical location and product booths in the province to celebrate the "Plowing" under the presidency. Most High, His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, King of the Kingdom of Cambodia.
The Royal "Plowing Ceremony" will be held at Kirivong Sok Sen Chey Stadium in Trapeang Ang Village, Rokar Krao Sangkat, Daun Keo City, Takeo Province, which will take place on May 22, 2019.
Please note that last year, the Royal "Plowing Ceremony" was held in Svay Rieng province.
The Royal Plowing Ceremony is held every year at the beginning of the rainy season, which is the King's tradition, and also to announce to the people that the rainy season has arrived and to see the omen. Of the district, especially the smoke from the cultivation and cultivation of the people.
The Royal Plowing Ceremony was originally held only at Veal Preah Meru near the Royal Palace, but in recent years the Royal Ceremony has been held in the provinces to provide opportunities for people in The province participated and learned about this royal ceremony.
Royal Academy of Cambodia and Jiujiang University Organize First Scientific Forum on Sino-Cambodian Relations
(Phnom Penh): The Royal Academy of Cambodia, in collaboration with Jiujiang University of the People's Republic of China, organized the first Scientific Forum on China-Cambodia Relations for the purpose of mutual learning and mutual understanding between peoples and peoples. Inter-cultural people have also made the perspectives of the two countries more open.
The purpose of organizing this program is three main points, including: First: the strengthening of Sino-Cambodian relations and the achievements of building a belt and a road, Second: Promoting the development of the community of destiny Joint between Cambodia and China and the sustainability of the Confucius Institute of the Royal Academy of Cambodia; and third, the promotion of cultural exchanges between Cambodia and China.
Through in-depth study of Cambodia-China relations is discussed in the context of globalization, and the achievements of China-Cambodia relations will be discussed in the fields of politics, economy, military, culture and diplomacy.
Dr. Sok Touch, President of the Royal Academy of Cambodia, said: "We should talk about diplomacy, culture, economy, education between China and Cambodia, as well as how the Cambodian people are ready to embrace the 'One Belt and One Road' initiative in both areas. Recently, we talked about the role of the Confucius Institute.
The Confucius Institute, co-organized by the Royal Academy of Cambodia and Jijiang University of China, focuses on human resource training in cultural exchange, education, language translation, book publishing and more.
"At the same time, Cambodia is also translating important Chinese books into Khmer, such as Xi Jinping, Governance of China, Part 1, currently preparing to translate the second part. "Many books from Khmer to Chinese to promote cultural change between the two countries, and we are currently translating books such as the Red Roses of the Mekong River and Samdech Techo Hun Sen born from a peasant family."
Today, the Confucius Institute at the Royal Academy of Cambodia has many branches in state institutions, including the Armed Forces, the Legislature, various ministries, and many educational institutions with about 30,000 students. To 25 branches throughout Cambodia. The vision of the Institute is to continue to contribute to the strengthening of relations between Cambodia and the People's Republic of China in the fields of education, language and cultural exchange.
