In 2017, the Constitutional Court of Taiwan ruled that LGBT people have the right to marry legally. However, the National Assembly has two years to approve and amend some constitutions before this deadline expires on May 24, 2019.
Hundreds of LGBT people gathered outside the parliament building in Taipei to hear the results and the historic announcement of the legality of same-sex marriage. The crowd cheered and others cried in the middle of a romantic rain as the results were announced.
