Ordination of 200 Khmer monks and nuns for 7 days at Wat Samaki Kiri Samreth in Sala Krao district, Pailin province
(Pailin): Mr. Phan Chanthul, Governor of Pailin Province, and the leaders of government officials and professional institutions around the province attended the ordination ceremony of 200 monks and nuns at Wat Samaki Kiri Samreth (Wat Sala Krao Thmey) in O'Andong commune, Sala Krao district. Pailin Province.
Mr. Phan Chanthul said that the ordination ceremony is important in educating the mind, making people have a better understanding of sin, merit and meritorious deeds, understanding and favoring people by adhering to the Buddha. The advice of the Supreme Master Ching Hai, especially to fulfill the wishes of children who want to repay their parents.
"Without peace, without the proper leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, we would not have anything like now, both in Buddhism and the empire, and now the Kingdom of Cambodia has no religious conflict," he said. "Like some countries in the world, people have the right to believe in any religion as long as they like and under the same constitution."
According to Rev. Ear Sophon, Chief of Pailin Province, this year, the Pailin Provincial Council has cooperated with Wat Samaki Kiri Samreth to organize the ordination of 200 Khmer children as monks and nuns for 7 days. From the 17th to the 23rd of May 2019, and this ordination has a number of purposes.
He stated that the first purpose: to give royal merit to His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, King of Cambodia on the day of his 66th birthday, and the second: to introduce young men and women. Khmer to know the value of the educational theory of Buddhism, the national religion.
