(Germany): Social protection, rural development and decentralization remain key activities for Cambodia-Germany cooperation for development. This is according to the press release of the results of the Cambodia-Germany talks in Berlin, Germany, which was received by Fresh News this morning, May 17.
Germany will provide loans (loans) for the construction of rural infrastructure, provide grants for the nutrition sector and social accountability system, and will expand efforts to build the capacity of public health centers and rural development sectors. All of these are the results of bilateral talks between the German government and the Royal Government of Cambodia in Berlin, the Federal Republic of Germany.
The new loan (loan) for rural infrastructure is a joint project between the French Agency for Development (AFD) and the European Union. The total amount for the project will exceed 80 million euros (in this multilateral project, Germany will contribute 30 million euros in loans). This genuine European joint effort will help make a positive difference in the lives and livelihoods of rural people.
