On May 14, 2019, His Majesty the King of Cambodia met with Chinese President Xi Jinping at the Great Hall of the People in Beijing, China. Cambodian King Norodom Sihamoni has told Chinese President Xi Jinping that the Cambodian people will stand with the Chinese people under all circumstances.
The president went on to say that China cherishes the special friendship with the royal family of Cambodia, and that generations of Chinese leaders have established close ties with His Majesty King Norodom Sihanouk. Cambodia-China must take care of this heritage and continue to strengthen the good relations to leave the Cambodian-Chinese friendship to be passed down from one generation to the next.
Until the night of May 14, 2019, Chinese President Xi Jinping and his wife held a birthday celebration for His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni. The ceremony was held at a banquet hosted by senior international guests attending the Asian Civilization Forum at the Great Hall of the People in Beijing, China. On May 14, 2019, the King of Cambodia was 66 years old and 67 years old.
On the morning of May 15, 2019, His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, King of Cambodia, the Most Revered King of Cambodia, attended the First Asian Civilization Forum. During the ceremony, His Majesty the King of Life on the Stone gave some royal speeches.
He praised the President for initiating the Common Destiny Community of Mankind, which is the ideal and conscience for building a common destiny community between developed and small economies and the People's Republic of China, a heroic country. Gentleness, respectable and highly appreciated.
He added that Cambodia was one of the countries in Asia that received the light of Buddhism and Hinduism in the early days of its history and had served as a meeting place between Indian diplomats and business diplomats. China for centuries. This relationship greatly contributed to the enormous growth of Khmer culture until the creation of the world-famous Angkorian civilization.
According to the King, the nations of Asia all have their own unique national culture, and some nations have built centuries-old civilizations to this day.
True, the cultures, religions, and civilizations of the Asian nations are different, but they are very similar, and have a common color that can uniquely identify the Asian civilization as a civilized nation. They live in a continent rich in resources and wisdom and the birthplace of the world's major religious founders.
After completing the Royal Mission, at 4 pm on May 16, 2019, the King of Cambodia returned to Cambodia.
