Is the United States using the Vietnam War scenario to use military force against Iran?
* Is the United States using the Vietnam War scenario?
Several US groups on Monday told the Associated Press that Iran or pro-Iranian militants in the region may have been behind the attack on four ships in the Gulf of the United Arab Emirates. The attacks on these tankers, which took place at a time when the United States is stepping up military action in the Middle East, are reminiscent of the beginning of the Vietnam War.
In early August 1964, a similar incident occurred in the Tonkin Bay of North Vietnam (at that time), when the United States accused North Vietnamese warships of launching attacks on ships. America. The accusation prompted the US Congress to allow Washington at the time to declare war on North Vietnam.
However, in 2005 a leaked US National Security Agency (NSA) leaked document confirmed that no North Vietnamese warships were present at the time of the attack.
