Cambodia is negotiating to export mangoes directly to China (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): After the success of exporting fresh bananas to China, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries Veng Sakhon confirmed. That Cambodia is preparing to negotiate with the Chinese side to achieve the signing of a joint protocol on the export of mangoes directly from Cambodia to the Chinese market.
Currently, five Cambodian agricultural products are allowed to be exported directly by the Chinese side: rice, cassava chips, cashew nuts, rice and bananas, which have just been achieved.
Each year, Cambodia harvests nearly 1 million tons of mango, while Cambodia exports mangoes to neighboring countries, including Vietnam and Thailand.
"The Cambodian ambassador to Beijing has informed me that the Chinese side will invite Cambodia to negotiate a protocol on mango exports from Cambodia in July," he said. We also want to pack as we do not want to lift one at a time, first exporting rice, then exporting cassava, cashew nuts, rice and bananas. "And this time it's about mangoes, but we want to pack as a package, including mangoes, dragon fruit with saliva."
The Minister stated that the package to make it easier for the people of Cambodia, especially farmers can have a larger production capacity for the benefit of the people.
In 2018, Cambodia exported a total of more than 4.3 million tons of official agricultural products, and not less than 7 million tons of informal exports.
