After overcoming many difficulties, the first drop of fresh milk in "Techo Sen Russey Trip National Park" will be available this July
(Preah Vihear): After overcoming many difficulties and obstacles, Mr. Sok Touch, President of the Royal Academy of Cambodia has finally achieved his wish, with fresh milk will be produced for the first time in "Techo Sen National Park. Russey Trip ”in Preah Vihear province to supply national and foreign consumers from next July.
In one part of the park, sheds and pastures, as well as grasslands, are technically organized with the help of a team of experts from Thailand, while 10 young Cambodian experts have studied in Thailand. Also completed this work.
Milk presses, ports and storage machines are imported from Japan to produce fresh milk that is hygienic and of good quality according to food specifications.
Dr. Sok Touch said that the team of the Royal Academy of Cambodia Techo Sen Russey Trip Park is actively working on this, claiming that a cow is worth more than 2,000 US dollars.
He said that by 2020, a total of 500 cows will be in the park and up to 10,000 liters of milk will be produced per day to supply consumers, especially tourists in Siem Reap.
He said that once the milk is produced from the park, that will reduce the import of fresh milk from abroad, and later the park will also set up a cow bank for farmers, especially those living around the area.
It should be noted that in the "Royal Academy of Cambodia Techo Sen Russey Trip Park" with an area of 14,334 hectares, which was established by Royal Decree in 2014, there is a research center for monitoring, conservation and development of agriculture, forestry and wildlife and pond animals. Stockpile water for wildlife to drink, plant trees, breed flowers, and do some agricultural work, training cows, raising and storing milk.
The park, located in Chhep 1 and Chhep 2 communes in Chhep district, Preah Vihear province, also preserves traditional steel mills, as the area was formerly a place of iron production during the Angkorian period from the 11th to the 13th century.
Please be reminded that the Royal Academy of Cambodia and a Japanese company on July 28, 2018 signed a memorandum of understanding to bring rare animals such as dolphins or endangered freshwater dolphins in the world to raise in This park because there is O Dalas, which is an ancient stream.
The Royal Academy of Cambodia is seeking about $ 10 million from South Korea to restore the ancient stream for wildlife and rarelife conservation, as well as for farmers' agriculture near the park.
In another memorandum of understanding between the Royal Academy of Cambodia and a Japanese company on July 28, 2018, the Royal Academy of Cambodia will bring rare animals such as dolphins or endangered freshwater dolphins to the world. Go to raise in this park because there is a stream called Odalas that the Royal Academy of Cambodia wants to prepare there to be a dolphin.
Meanwhile, the Royal Academy of Cambodia will find endangered tigers and elephants to conserve in the park so that all nations can visit the endangered species.
Director General of Customs and Excise of Cambodia highlights the reform and modernization of the customs system at the Asia-Pacific Customs Director General Conference
In his opening remarks, Pranab Kuma Das said that in response to the evolution and rapid growth of international trade, the Fourth Industrial Revolution and e-commerce in the context of the digital economy, Asia-Pacific countries need to develop reform strategies. It focuses on security and trade facilitation, compliance and law enforcement, and capacity building.
He highlighted the important role of technology in streamlining customs procedures and highlighted key areas of work covered under the WCO theme for 2019 "Smart Borders for Trade, Travel and Transportation Facilitation". .
At the same time, Secretary-General Kunio Mikuriya highlighted the new strategies and initiatives of the World Customs Organization, including: security and trade facilitation, outcome measurement, automation of customs procedures and customs cooperation, risk management system. , And the use of technology in customs procedures and customs operations, especially the use of big data, data collection, data analysis, data sharing.
Dr. Kun Nhim was also invited to present the results of the discussion on cross-border e-commerce.
Regarding the priority areas of the Asia-Pacific region, the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia has also launched the Customs Reform and Modernization Strategy 2019-2023, using information technology in customs procedures as the core strategy to support four other strategies. These include: improving revenue collection efficiency, strengthening compliance and law enforcement, customs cooperation, and developing human and institutional resources.
It should be noted that on the occasion of attending this conference, the delegation of the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia also met bilaterally with the customs administrations of some major trading partners such as India, Korea, Thailand, etc. to strengthen cooperation. On customs work.
