Legal Awareness: Types of Criminal Penalties
(Phnom Penh): According to the spirit of the Penal Code, punishment is referred to as a punishment declared by the court to apply to any person who commits an offense as stated in the law, and the sentence is announced on the basis of harm. Of an offense that causes damage to the victim. What are the types of penalties of the Penal Code of the Kingdom of Cambodia?
So for this week, our Legal Awareness Program brings up the topic of "Types of Crimes!" To present to the public as follows:
Penal Code of the Kingdom of Cambodia 2009 Punishment is divided into 3 (three) categories:
1. Convictions In accordance with Article 43 of the Penal Code, penalties include imprisonment and fines, and fines shall be in KHR. Please also note that the fine received is paid into the state budget, that is, this fine is not a civil compensation that the parties pay compensation to the victim.
2. Additional sentence is a minor sentence that the judge decides to add to the sentence and until the court decides that the person is guilty, then the court can decide to impose an additional sentence on that sentence. The punishment shall be appropriate to the offense committed by the individual or guarantee the implementation of the principle of individual punishment.
Example: "A" is a doctor and he has misused his profession, causing the patient more serious injuries. Accordingly, according to Article 53, the court may impose additional penalties by prohibiting the profession committed during the profession or suspending his license.
In short, according to the spirit of the penal code, the categories of punishments are clearly aimed at identifying and carefully considering the harm or seriousness that causes harm or harm to individuals and society.
In addition, each sentence is designed to ensure that the punishment of the perpetrators is appropriate to the crimes committed by the individual. However, the sentence can only be announced if the person has violated the law.
