Minister of Commerce Leads a Delegation to Inaugurate a Cambodian Business Center and Meets with Chinese Officials to Promote Bilateral Trade
(Shandong, China): Minister of Commerce Pan Sosak cut the ribbon to inaugurate the Cambodian Business Center in Yantai, Shandong Province, People's Republic of China, with the participation of a high-level delegation of the two countries. 20 people. This ceremony will be held on May 10, 2019.
This business center is a gateway to provide information related to trade, investment, tourism and culture of the Kingdom of Cambodia to Chinese investors in Shandong and other provinces of China who wish to visit or do business and invest in Cambodia.
On that occasion, Mr. Pan Sosak asked Ms. Zhang Yami, President of the Cambodian Business Center, to exhibit Cambodian products to the maximum to attract orders from the Chinese market and promote the export of national products.
Mr. Pan Sosak thanked Mr. Zhang Tailing for supporting the establishment of the Cambodian Business Center in Yantai and informed the Deputy Mayor about the potential of Cambodia as well as the business opportunities and investment protection policies of the Royal Government of Cambodia. At the same time, the Minister also requested the Deputy Mayor to encourage more Chinese investors to invest in Cambodia.
In the afternoon of the same day, Minister Pan Sosak continued to meet with Ms. Rin Iron, Deputy Governor of Shandong Province at Shandong Hotel in Jinan.
During the meeting, the Deputy Governor welcomed the Cambodian delegation and briefed on the history of Shandong Province and the number of Shandong companies doing business in Cambodia. Ms. Rin Irong also asked the Minister to support Shandong Investment Project on the establishment of an industrial park and machinery in Cambodia.
In response, Minister Pan Sosak expressed his full support for the above investment project and thanked Ms. Rin Irong for her efforts to encourage investors in Shandong Province to invest in 112 companies in Cambodia.
The Minister promised to facilitate business for all investors in Shandong Province and requested the Deputy Governor to encourage Chinese traders to buy as much as possible agricultural products from Cambodia, such as rice, mango, cassava, lentils, bananas and other products to increase trade volume. Bilateral Cambodia-China.
