According to the report of the Third Commission of the Anti-Drug Campaign, the types of crimes include: 11 trafficking cases, 22 arrests and 6 use cases, 12 arrests.
According to the report, the results of the nationwide drug crackdown from January 1 to May 10, 2019 totaled 2,811 cases, detaining 6,006 people (480 females). 140 foreigners, 31 females of 7 nationalities). More than 100 kilograms of damaged chicken meat and chicken knees were burnt down by customs officers at O'Rumduol checkpoint in Battambang province.
(Battambang): Officers from the O'Rumduol Customs and Excise Office of the Battambang Provincial Customs and Excise Department, including border guards, arrested and burned a total of 127 kilograms of defective chicken meat and chicken knees that were smuggled in through O'Rumduol This morning, May 10, 2019.
According to the customs official, he also called on all people before buying to eat to check carefully to avoid harm to health and advise all traders to stop selling and distributing all these defective goods if not. Therefore, the authorities will enforce the law.
He added that it is often observed that Trumanny always has new reforms, but all of these changes are beneficial.
A group of Japanese mobile phone thieves in Beong Salang commune, Tuol Kork district, now the police force can crack down
(Phnom Penh): The crime prevention and suppression operation team of the National Police General Commission in Phnom Penh on May 10, 2019, investigated and cracked down on one of the two suspects who acted A Japanese mobile phone failed in Sangkat Boeung Salang, Khan Toul Kork.
According to the authorities, so far, the specialized police force is continuing to search for and arrest another suspect who is a fugitive. The suspects are currently being interrogated to prepare a case to be sent to court for further proceedings.
(Phnom Penh): After the trial on the afternoon of May 10, 2019, the Phnom Penh Municipal Court decided to postpone the hearing on the case of Ms. Yin Mana without setting a time related to the case of driving a car and hitting the victim. Died immediately at the scene.
Today's hearing is chaired by Mr. Ouk Sovannarith and chaired by Ms. Ser Vanny.
It should be noted that on the afternoon of March 29, 2019, Mr. Bunthy, Investigating Judge of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court, issued an order to bring Ms. Yin Mana, who drove a luxury car and hit a dead student, to the Phnom Penh PJ Prison to wait. The trial will be held in accordance with the law.
The victim, 22-year-old Dum Rida, was born in Kampong Damrey village, Prek Tamak commune, Khsach Kandal district, Kandal province.
In connection with this traffic accident, the family of Miss Dum Rida on the evening of April 3, 2019, agreed to accept $ 70,000 in civil damages from the family of the perpetrator, Mr. Yin Ngich, who drove the car and hit Ms. Dum Rida, causing her death. Immediately at the scene in Toul Kork, Phnom Penh a few days ago.
This agreement was made without any coercion in the office of Samdech Techo Sen at the Office of the Council of Ministers and in the presence of lawyers on both sides as witnesses. National Committee for Promoting One Village, One Product asks all sellers of raw materials to turn to recycling to increase income and increase employment
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Suong Noy, Deputy Secretary General of the National Committee for the Promotion of Village 1, Product 1 of the Council for Agricultural and Rural Development, requested all artisans and traders who sell raw materials to turn to processing raw materials. Those are to increase income and increase employment and knowledge for the next generation.
Dr. Suong Noy said this on the morning of May 10, 2019, when he was invited as a speaker in the forum "Business Initiatives for Food Processing and Agricultural Products Enterprise" at Himawari Hotel.
The event was also attended by Mr. Nuon Sophorn, Director of the Department of Planning and Small and Medium Enterprise Development of the Ministry of Industry and Handicrafts, Mr. Pech Bolen, Vice President of the Cambodian Young Entrepreneurs Association, Mr. Oknha Chhin Ken, Chairman of the National Public Relations Committee of the Association. Small and Medium Enterprises of Cambodia, Mr. Lek Sin Rithy, Executive Director of FACMEC, as well as many other participants.
Dr. Suong Noy said that all artisans and traders who sell raw materials should turn to processing those raw materials, because when we know how to process, we will be able to increase income and increase employment and knowledge for children. The next generation will also enhance our own livelihoods and enable migrants to return to this skill and refinement to support their livelihoods as well.
He added that for this processing, there is no market, because we know that today we Cambodians eat and use this product is our market, our traders today are importing only products. Instead of exporting raw materials, so if we process the products well, we use all the products, we will get more profit.
He added that the Ministry of Industry and Handicrafts will accept all cooperation, provide scientific opinions, technical assistance and innovation from national and international organizations and development partners to update or develop the relevant regulatory framework. A food business activity in a new phase by the handicraft factory as well.
It should be noted that the Business Matching Forum for Food and Agricultural Products Processing Enterprise 2019 is designed to create communication opportunities and build business networks for local food and agricultural processing enterprises to expand knowledge and information on innovative products and services for As an input to the production work of the enterprise to strengthen the production capacity and competitiveness of the product.
(Phnom Penh): Forces of Po Sen Chey District Unity Command led by Mr. Preap Manel, Deputy Governor under the coordination of Mr. OU Sopheak, Deputy Prosecutor of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court, inspected the wood processing and cigarette production of Ligun brand. Crush the wood.
The action of the authorities came after the people reported the theft.
The unbranded handicraft is located in Tuol Sam village, Sangkat Kampol, Khan Por Senchey, Phnom Penh. The owner is Leang Tong Leng, 35 years old, and was inspected by the joint police force at 10:15 am on the 10th. May 2019.
After inspecting, it was found that the site was operating without a license, and the wood was mixed with tobacco to make cigarettes, according to the information received. Not only that, the illegal and unlicensed business has been leaked for a long time now, but while the force arrived, did not see the cigarette production line in operation, while the wood processing machine in Process.
Meanwhile, the owner of the handicraft site said that he had previously rented the place to a Chinese man to run the handicraft, but only rented it for one month, so the Chinese man stopped renting it. Meanwhile, the production of cigarettes was also suspended, while the wood processing handicraft after the Chinese stopped working, he, who owns the location, continued to open until now, which is only three months.
After inspecting the actual situation, the above-mentioned police force temporarily suspended this handicraft business by asking the owner of the location to apply for the right permit to allow the wood processing to continue, but at the same time, the police did not Take away any material from this craft.
Cambodia expects to export 120,000 tons of yellow bananas directly to China this year!
(Kampot): Mr. Veng Sakhon, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, on May 10, 2019 stated that in 2019, Cambodia expects to export 12 yellow bananas directly to China. Ten thousand tons with five companies licensed by China to export directly.
This statement was made on the occasion of Minister Veng Sakhon presiding over the inauguration ceremony of Long Met Aggregate Co., Ltd. in Chhouk District, Kampot Province on the morning of May 10. This year 2019.
Minister Veng Sakhon also stated that China is the country with the largest demand for bananas, accounting for 40% of the world, with about 4 million tons per year, and the export of yellow bananas to China, the Chinese side can not. Set the banana export quota of Cambodia.
At the same time, the Minister said that the Ministry of Agriculture has been working to strengthen cooperation with development partners and the private sector to support and invest in all agricultural value chains from point A to Z by increasing product productivity. In accordance with the standards of the export market, meet the needs of both domestic and foreign markets.
To achieve this goal, the Minister requested to continue to maintain cohesive cooperation with all stakeholders in a spirit of high responsibility in accordance with the "state-private-development partners and community" approach.
The Minister of Agriculture called on the private sector to be able to consider and consider investing in the agricultural sector, especially in the processing of agricultural packaging to jointly reduce the import of raw materials, which is an important factor in increasing value added. Work and improve living standards.
According to the president of Oknha Port Hok Chhuon, Long Met Agricultural Co., Ltd., the banana plantation covers a total area of 1,000 hectares and uses an investment of more than $ 32 million. More than 400 hectares are currently being harvested, packaged and exported, with more than 22,000 tonnes of fresh bananas expected to be exported in 2019 and more than 30,000 tonnes by 2020.
Mr. Oknha confirmed that the company will cultivate a series of steps to cover an area of 1,000 hectares.
On the opening day of Cambodia's first fresh banana processing, packaging and export factory directly to the Chinese market, Long Met exported 6 containers of bananas, equivalent to 120 tons.
On this occasion, Mr. Chiao Tai, Governor of Kampot Province, on behalf of the local authority, expressed his gratitude to the company that has invested in banana cultivation and export, which has provided many benefits, such as the use of land in this area, which is a former battlefield. Do your best to create jobs for local people, increase family income and reduce poverty.
Mr. Chiao Tai also advised local authorities at all levels to continue to provide better support and cooperation with companies for the development of the family economy and the national economy, both now and in the future.
(Banteay Meanchey): Speaking from Banteay Meanchey Province during the inauguration ceremony of Provincial and Deputy Governors this morning, May 10, 2019, Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior, instructed the authorities to pay more attention to prevention. Citizens cross the border into Thailand illegally to avoid facing action by Thai authorities and to prevent citizens from becoming victims of human trafficking.
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng also reminded the authorities to prevent money laundering crimes and to avoid being involved in this crime, to prevent traffic accidents, to increase the efficiency of management and to protect the safety of foreigners, to continue to implement well. Decentralization and deconcentration policy and some other important work.
In addition, the Chief of the Ministry of Interior recommended that the newly appointed governors and deputy governors, together with the Council of Civil Servants and the Armed Forces, work to maintain peace and political stability through law enforcement, dissemination and education. Citizens about the consequences of overthrowing the legitimate government and the color revolution.
"People are enjoying the benefits of peace and development, and this has led some opposition groups to find ways to persuade people to change their minds by inciting them to engage in illegal activities," he said. Previous voters have stated that the people give justice to the Royal Government.
Samdech Sar Kheng stressed that the opposition has taken the word positive change to commit illegal activities and cover up attempts to carry out a color revolution, but for the Royal Government, the change is aimed at reform efforts in all areas to provide peace to the people. Let the nation have peace and prosperity.
Samdech Krala Hom also recommended that the new Governor and Deputy Governor of Banteay Meanchey Province increase the policy of safe villages and communes to be eliminated in 2019 for drug-related entertainment, prevent and suppress drug distribution and use and conduct. Other crimes in society.
Along with the change of the new provincial governor, Samdech expressed his appreciation to the old provincial governor and the new provincial governor, stating that these two high-ranking officials have done a good job, and Samdech asked the council and civil servants under the administration. The province continues to work together to develop Banteay Meanchey to be more prosperous.
On behalf of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng also thanked Deputy Prime Minister Ke Kem Yan, Chairman of the National Authority for Combating Drugs and Chairman of the National Task Force for Banteay Meanchey Province for his generous support. And special resources in rescuing citizens. Svay Rieng Health Officer Warns of Illegal Private Doctors Who Cause Danger to Citizens
(Svay Rieng): Mr. KER Ratha, Director of Svay Rieng Provincial Health Department, urged ODs, ODs and health center directors in all cities and districts to publish and compile statistics on private medical services "Illegal village doctors" who do not have a degree. Acknowledged by the Ministry of Health, if they refuse to listen to the instructions, the department will continue to publish and file a complaint to the court for legal action.
Mr. Ker Ratha made this statement on May 10, 2019 during a meeting to disseminate information to the ODs and the directors of all health centers in all districts and districts to collect statistics on the private services of village doctors who give injections. No degree from the Ministry of Health.
At the same time, he also reminded all medical teams to continue to pay attention to serve the people, respect the code of ethics and not to charge a lot of money, to have a proper attitude to patients.
He also instructed the ODs and ODs in all cities and districts to disseminate widely to the people about the progress and provision of health services to the people. The Red Cross in Kampong Thom province distributes humanitarian aid to 80 families affected by the typhoon in Stong district.
