(US): Four billion years ago, the surface of Mars (Mars) was claimed by scientists to be able to grow life forms in the presence of rivers, as well as many lakes and even a deep ocean. In fact, some scientists even suspect that life on Earth today may have originated from the rocks of Mars, which shattered into space due to a powerful collision event. .
But things changed as Mars lost its magnetic field. At that time, the particles of radiation emanating from the sun were opened to destroy the dense atmosphere of Mars freely. Because of this, Mars turned into a cold, dry planet, as we all know it today, since 3.7 billion years ago.
Today, life forms that may still be present on Mars are less likely to manifest themselves in the same way as life forms on our planet. If any of the aliens with the most advanced technology could immediately know that the Earth had a life form, it would simply scan our environment.
More than 90 percent of the methane in the Earth's atmosphere comes from microbial life forms and other organisms, so it is possible that this type of gas is a sign of modern life on Mars. But more importantly, methane can also be formed by natural reactions.
On the other hand, if methane on Mars was actually formed by a life form, that form may not have existed for a long time. According to scientists, methane gas on Mars comes from underground, but no one knows for sure how long it lasted before it was released into the surface.
* Scientists will continue to hunt for signs of life on Mars
Sihanoukville Customs and Excise Officers Arrest Nearly 50 Duty Free Cars
(Preah Sihanouk): Mobile Customs Officers in Area 3, National Road 4 of the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia on Friday morning, May 10, 2019, in cooperation with officials of the Sihanoukville Customs and Excise Department, as well as the police and the army. The provincial military police seized another left-hand-drive luxury car that did not have import tax documents, or so-called duty-free smuggled vehicles, which were traveling on public roads in Sihanoukville.
The same customs and excise official said that currently, the above duty-free vehicles were taken by the customs authorities to be stored at the Sihanoukville Customs and Excise Branch to continue the procedure according to the customs law.
In this regard, Mr. Tum No, Head of the Sihanoukville Customs and Excise Department, told the media that the activities of the mobile customs officers and the Sihanoukville Customs Branch officers who seized vehicles without paying taxes were in accordance with the instructions. Two of the leaders of the Royal Government delegation in charge of the Director General of Customs and Excise of Cambodia and follow the instructions of the Unified Command of Sihanoukville Provincial Administration.
Mr. Tum No, Head of Sihanoukville Customs Branch, stated that the above activities of Customs and Excise officials are partly to collect tax revenue and partly to campaign to encourage the relevant departments to turn. Participate in respecting the law properly.
Customs officials also said that for new luxury cars, right-hand drive, Cambodian law prohibits the import. And that this case, the authorities confiscated as state property by allowing the owner of the right-hand drive car to file taxes or no fines at all.
It should be noted that in Sihanoukville, from the end of 2018 until May 10, 2019, there are nearly 50 luxury cars, both left-hand drive and right-hand drive, which Cambodian customs and excise officials have found. There are customs duties and illegal imports.
At this point, Mr. Tum No, Head of Sihanoukville Customs and Excise Branch, said that for the above duty-free vehicles, Sihanoukville Customs and Excise officials cooperated with Customs Officers in Area 3, National Road 4 and cooperated. Along with other authorities, a series of arrests were made in Sihanoukville.
