Minister Vong Soth: Celebrating "International Family Day" to Contribute to Dissemination and Awareness of the Important Role of the Family
Minister Vong Soth said this on the occasion of his and her participation in the celebration of the 25th anniversary of the International Day of the Family on May 15 under the theme "Family well-being as a catalyst in the implementation of the social protection system in Cambodia". On May 10, 2019 in Kampong Cham province, with the participation of civil servants of the Ministry of Social Affairs and a large number of family representatives.
Speaking at the ceremony, Mr. Vong Soth also expressed his appreciation and appreciation to the leaders of all levels of civil servants who have worked hard to fulfill their duties by organizing this day every year, in which Samdech Techo Hun The Prime Minister of Cambodia issued a message to all compatriots, especially the head of the family who has worked hard to raise children to become citizens in society.
Mr. Vong Soth emphasized that the Royal Government of Cambodia under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia has made great efforts and taken many measures to improve the living standards of the people and the well-being of families in order to contribute to social development and Harmonize through the development of laws, policies and regulations related to work to promote family values.
The Royal Government of the sixth mandate has launched a political program for in-depth reform and continued implementation of the fourth phase of the Rectangular Strategy, with a strong focus on social affairs, veterans and youth rehabilitation. In fact, the implementation of the program to support pregnant women and children under 2 years of age in poor families will be implemented from June 2019 to facilitate and solve difficulties for the poor and vulnerable.
