The government assigned the Minister of Water Resources and relevant ministries to study the pumping, restoration and construction of the river bank requested by Try Pheap Company, a senior official of the Ministry of Water Resources came out to explain this case.
(Phnom Penh): The Royal Government of Cambodia has assigned the Minister of Water Resources and Meteorology, Mr. Lim Kean Hor, together with relevant ministries and institutions to study, discuss and provide feedback on the restoration of pumping and riverbanking at Try Company. Proposals were made from the Cambodia-Vietnam border checkpoint (lead pot) to the border area of Kampong Cham, Kratie and along the Bassac River.
This recommendation was made in a letter from Mr. Chrea Sochenda, Secretary of State of the Office of the Council of Ministers on May 7, 2019 to the Minister of Water Resources and Meteorology. The letter confirmed Try Pheap's request to pump and restore the riverbank in accordance with the "Rivers of the River" strategy.
After the letter was leaked, there was a lot of reaction to the project, especially the opposition group accused the government of giving Try Pheap to do business with the river.
Mr. Chan Yutha continued to explain that in order to make sure that this project does not cause any impact, in addition to the Ministry of Water Resources, other relevant ministries may be the Ministry of Mines and Energy and the Ministry of Public Works and Transport may conduct separate studies. Legal as well as licensing as well as related navigation along this river.
The senior official of the Ministry of Water Resources added that when each ministry has completed its study, it will meet to discuss the next step to decide whether it is possible or not. To pass on opinions and opinions to the Royal Government to issue a decision later.
For the second main reason: the river-raising strategy means that if the company is allowed by the government for this work, the company will pay for the riverbank, because now the state only receives money from the payment of taxes from the government. The sand business alone has no plans to build riverbanks or prevent landslides.
In connection with the above project, on behalf of the Ministry of Water Resources, Mr. Chan Yutha appealed to the people not to worry because the company has not yet received official permission to restore the river pump and river bank, and the relevant ministry will study In the most detailed and dense way, make sure that there is no impact and can make the river of Cambodia better water flow as well as avoid landslides.
The official also claimed that the shallow water of the river is also the cause of the river bank collapses every year. Experts explain that when the land is shallow, it causes the water flow to start to change, so the water flows to hit the filter along the bank, causing the river bank to collapse.
The same official said that without the restoration and construction of the river bank in the future, the river will be difficult for ships to travel, as this river is an important transportation system of Cambodia.
In addition to the above officials, if they look at the river in the pot on the Cambodian-Vietnamese border, at present, although the river on the Cambodian side is not pumping, but the Vietnamese side is pumping the other side. Every day, too.
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Sok Touch, President of the Royal Academy of Cambodia, addressed the Phnom Penh Municipal Court this morning, May 10, 2019, in response to the complaint of the Khmer Rouge Party.
Dr. Sok Touch considered this lawsuit strange to him, but nevertheless he was not worried about the lawsuit from the Khmer Rouge party. He claimed that he would take legal action against the Khmer Rouge party in response to his defamation.
It should be noted that in 2018, Mr. Sok Sovann Vathanasarapong, President of the Khmer Rouge Party, filed a lawsuit against Mr. Sok Touch, alleging that this doctor had incited the Royal Government to imprison him for collecting fingerprints in protest of Koh Tral. Fall into Vietnamese rule.
Mr. Sok Touch claimed that the story of Koh Tral, it is a matter of law, if Mr. Patong Patriot Party should put a campaign policy before the election.
(Phnom Penh): A meeting of the National Committee for Environment and Health, with members from nearly 30 ministries and institutions, chaired by Prof. Mam Bunheng, Minister of Health, discussed the work of the National Multilateral Action Plan on Disease Prevention and Control. Not infected 2018-2027, which took place. The meeting was held on May 9, 2019 at the Ministry of Health.
Minister Mam Bunheng said that the purpose of this meeting is for each ministry to review the work that has been implemented and set up another technical working group to further detail the prevention of four non-communicable diseases that stand out in society. These include: cardiovascular disease, cancer, chronic respiratory disease, and diabetes.
These four major non-communicable diseases are caused by unhealthy diet, lack of physical activity, tobacco use, smoking, and harmful alcohol use.
Therefore, in response to the growing problem of non-communicable diseases, members from nearly 30 ministries and institutions with different functions and roles work together to find ways to prevent more Cambodians from contracting non-communicable diseases. Treatment reduces the severity of non-communicable diseases so that they do not become disabled or die early.
