(Phnom Penh): Camcontrol Phnom Penh International Port Branch On May 10, 2019, in cooperation with the officials of the Department of Commerce, the Market Commission brought a mobile test vehicle to inspect food products in 5 markets, including: Chbar Ampov Market, Vegetable Market. Chbar Ampov, Prek Pra Market, Champouk Crow Market and Prek Eang Market.
CamControl officers analyzed 64 samples of food products, including seafood, vegetables, desserts, fruits, a total of 64 samples, but did not find any products containing banned chemicals.
Officials of CamControl Phnom Penh International Port Branch said that all these operations are carried out regularly in the responsible areas of the branch throughout the capital, provinces and cities under the careful guidance of the leadership of the General Department of CamControl and Lead the Ministry of Commerce.
The official said that the work of surveying and monitoring in the market is to continue to be more active and strengthen activities to increase trust and protect the well-being of people across the country, contribute to reducing people's poverty by helping Prevent diseases caused by eating contaminated food and containing toxic chemicals in it.
