African swine fever and prevention methods discussed by health officials and doctors
(Phnom Penh): For the purpose of disseminating awareness on the status of African swine fever (ASF) as well as the effects, precautions and prevention of African swine fever epidemics, Ministry of Health officials and doctors from abroad Come to discuss, find solutions to prevent and prevent.
Kuch Sokkruy, owner of a pig farm in Kandal province, said the workshop provided knowledge on African swine fever (ASF) and how to prevent the virus from spreading from one pig to another. Although the disease occurs in pigs, it is not contagious to humans, which is why he continues to raise pigs and encourages other farmers to do so.
At the same time, Mr. Nin Bora, the owner of the farm in Takeo province, said, "I have gained more in-depth knowledge about this African swine fever, solve some questions and gain knowledge in observing the disease situation and how to prevent it." .
Dr. Roongroje added that the best way to prevent this disease is for people to understand the technical management, know how to prevent the implementation of biosecurity of the farm and cooperate in providing information to animal health agencies.
Symptoms: High fever, red skin, rash and bruises on the ears, abdomen and hind legs, difficulty breathing, digestive problems, diarrhea, mixed blood, pigs, miscarriage or sudden birth. Pigs can die suddenly without any symptoms.
It should be noted that if pigs are infected with the African swine fever virus, it will cause a large number of pigs to die (possibly with a mortality rate of 100%), for which there is no vaccine or cure yet, but it is a disease that is not transmitted to humans. .
