WASHINGTON (Reuters) - The administration of US President Donald Trump will raise tariffs on Chinese imports to $ 325 billion, but the United States has said it will resume trade talks between the two countries on Friday. This Friday. This was released by Fox News on Friday morning, May 10, 2019.
The decision to raise tariffs on "$ 325 billion" on Chinese products comes after talks between US and Chinese officials failed to reach an agreement on Thursday. The tariff increase includes a $ 200 billion tariff on imports from China, which is set to increase from 10 to 25 percent by 12:01 a.m. Friday (US time).
