According to the South Korean military, a total of two missiles were tested by North Korea on Thursday, one of which was fired at 4:29 p.m., with a range of 420 km and one. Another was fired 20 minutes later, with a range of 270 km, with both missiles flying at an altitude of about 50 km and heading east and crashing into the East Sea (Sea of Japan).
