World Bank Executive Board Appreciates Cambodia's Achievements
It should be noted that the composition of the Executive Board that is currently on mission is from the representative offices of 63 countries and has a total of 41.14%, which is the group with the most votes in decision-making. Important in the WB.
The delegation of the WB Executive Board expressed appreciation for the many outstanding achievements that Cambodia has made in socio-economic development, especially the achievement of high economic growth for many years in a row, poverty reduction. Good control of low inflation and the achievement of other development goals, such as education and health.
Moreover, Cambodia's good public debt management is becoming a case study and learning experience of major international institutions and some countries. The delegation added that on the basis of this success, the WB is ready to continue to support and travel more vigorously with the Royal Government in the mission of economic and social development of Cambodia.
Today's discussion will enable the Executive Board to verify the information that the delegation has received in the past compared to what is actually happening in Cambodia. At the end of May, the WB Board of Directors will review and approve a partnership framework with Cambodia for the next five years (2019-2023), which is scheduled to provide approximately $ 1 billion in financing.
Mr. Vongsey Visoth, Acting Minister of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, stated that although the cooperation and partnership between Cambodia and the WB has been experiencing problems and setbacks for some time, this partnership has begun to recover in recent years. The latter will gradually improve to the present.
He also mentioned the remarkable progress made in raising fiscal revenue, which makes the Royal Government more able to increase expenditures on priority sectors and sectors to improve economic efficiency and productivity. In fact, from 2013 to 2018, spending on education increased 3.2 times, health increased 2.5 times and agriculture increased 3 times, as well as public investment funded by the national budget. An increase of 3.5%.
As a way forward, maintaining high and healthy economic growth leads to achieving the vision of 2050 to become a high-income country. The Royal Government needs to increase its efforts to diversify its economy and enhance its economic competitiveness. National.
Mr. Vongsey Visoth and the delegation of WB Executive Board also exchanged views on some practical topics. Regarding the public debt situation in Cambodia, he said that the public debt situation in Cambodia is stable and low risk, and large international financial institutions are considered as a model country in managing public debt in the region.
The reason why Cambodia achieved this result is because Cambodia adheres to the four principles of Samdech Techo Prime Minister: First: Borrowing loans in a reasonable amount that the financial and economic situation can withstand, Second: Borrowing only loans with a high level of concessions Third, borrow only for priority sectors to sustain sustainable growth and increase economic productivity, and fourth: use credit in a transparent manner.
He stressed that although more and more partners and countries now want Cambodia to borrow money, Cambodia will not borrow if it is not necessary and does not meet Cambodia's needs and priorities. The delegation also exchanged views on environmental and urban issues in urban areas, as well as secondary education, which, despite high enrollment rates, is still a challenge. No.
At the same time, continuing to improve the quality of higher education, especially the support of study and research in the field of science (STEM) is an indispensable basis for supporting the digital economy in Cambodia. Finally, Mr. Vongsey Visoth also wished the team success and fruitfulness for the mission in Cambodia.
