Chip Mong Co., Ltd. organizes third year life-saving blood donation program
(Phnom Penh): Chip Mong Company led staff at all levels to donate blood voluntarily on May 9, 2019 at its headquarters.
Chip Mong has partnered with the National Blood Transfusion Center to organize this event to contribute to meeting the demand for blood in Phnom Penh as well as throughout the country, as this voluntary blood donation accounts for only about 20% of the total demand.
This is the third year that Chip Mong has organized a blood donation program with the participation of company executives and staff at all levels who have volunteered their time to donate blood to contribute to the mission of saving lives and giving hope to you. There is an urgent need for blood. Discover the history of the Prime Minister of Nepal Sama Oli who will visit Cambodia (Video inside)
Samaoli was arrested for a second time in 1973 and sentenced to 14 years in prison. But after his release in 1987, he became a member of the Standing Committee of the Communist Party of Nepal. Moreover, he became increasingly popular after his democratic movement overthrew the Panchayat regime established by King Mahendra in 1990 through the creation of a new constitution.
Later, despite losing the 2008 parliamentary elections, Samaoli continued his political career until he was elected to parliament and served as interior minister from 1994 to 1995. Both Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Foreign Affairs from 2006 to 2007.
