National and provincial joint commissions set up border posts at Phnom Doh Kramom Cultural Center to end encroachment
(Mondulkiri): Mr. Thai Norak Satya, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts and Mr. Svay Sam Eang, Governor of Mondulkiri Province, together with the relevant units and the Phnom Doh Kramom Mountain Management Committee, on May 9, 2019, set up a border demarcation post at Phnom Doh Kramom Cultural Center is located in Sen Monorom after more than 10 years.
Mr. Thai Norak Satya said that the current mission of the Joint Committee is a good sign because the land issue in the Phnom Doh Kramom area has been going on for many years.
He stated that the joint decision to set up the border demarcation post will accelerate the work of cultural skills to make a practical report to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia. This should be completed as soon as possible to avoid further illegal encroachment.
Mr. Svay Sam Eang, Provincial Governor, said that the land of Phnom Doh Kramom was established by the Royal Government of Cambodia in 2004 to be considered as public property, but at that time, the land in this area has not been properly demarcated. There were also acts of land grabbing by people living along the hillside.
It should be noted that on the afternoon of February 28, 2019, Samdech Techo Hun Sen ordered the Mondulkiri provincial authorities to confiscate the land of Phnom Doh Kramom as state property, which was encroached upon by a handful of people.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen orders the Governor of Mondulkiri Province to immediately prevent any person from encroaching on the land at Phnom Doh Kramom. Remember what Samdech used to go there in 2012 there.
More than 100 hectares of land in Phnom Doh Kramom, or Indigenous Cultural Center, has been gradually lost since 2005, with part of the land being traded from one person to another. Karaoke and guesthouse. The remaining land is currently only about 80 hectares. Nationwide Traffic Law Enforcement Campaign on May 9: 868 Illegal Vehicles Found and 578 Fineed
