The official announcement of the export of yellow bananas to China today was presided over by Mr. Veng Sakhon, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries and Mr. Li An, Economic Adviser at the Embassy of the People's Republic of China.
Five Cambodian companies that grow and package yellow bananas get permission from the Chinese side to export to the Chinese market.
Speaking at the inauguration of the direct export of yellow bananas to China, Mr. Ngin Chhay, the Royal Government of Cambodia delegate in charge of the Director General of the General Department of Agriculture, confirmed that the results of yellow bananas are in high demand in the international market and bananas. Of Cambodia is continuously exporting.
He also mentioned the efforts to negotiate with the Chinese side in terms of procedures, technical documents and especially sanitary and phytosanitary documents to achieve banana exports to China.
Before being allowed to export yellow bananas directly to the Chinese market, the yellow bananas grown and packaged in Cambodia had to be exported through Vietnam before continuing to China.
Speaking on that occasion, Minister of Agriculture Veng Sakhon stated that in order to implement the Strategic Plan for Agricultural Development and the Rectangular Strategy Phase 4 of the Royal Government, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Ministry has made every effort to bring Cambodian agricultural products to market. International. Apparently, the export of yellow bananas directly to China today.
"Indeed, this result is inseparable from the excellent cooperation between the two sides in negotiating legal and technical support from the Chinese side to bring fresh bananas into Cambodia," he said. "Finally, the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries and the Ambassador of the People's Republic of China to Cambodia have reached a protocol to allow Cambodia to export bananas to China."
