Khmer Breweries Continues Campaign to Distribute Cambodian Pure Water in Hospitals
(Phnom Penh): Khmer Breweries will launch a four-month campaign to distribute Cambodian fresh water at the National Children's Hospital from May 9 to August 8, 2019.
4,500 cases of Cambodian drinking water and 1.5 liters of milk will be distributed to all patients treated at the National Children's Hospital.
Distribution of Cambodian Pure Water at the National Children's Hospital is part of Khmer Breweries' large-scale charity campaign, which was initiated with the aim of improving the well-being of children and mothers at children's hospitals in Phnom Penh and in some provinces through Distribute Cambodian pure water to patients for drinking during hospitalization.
In addition to Cambodian pure water for distribution to patients, Khmer Breweries also donated 120 cases of Cambodian pure water for 4 months to the medical team for daily consumption.
Recently, Khmer Breweries brought Cambodian pure water to distribute to patients treated at Kuntha Bopha IV Hospital. Khmer Breweries will continue its campaign to distribute Cambodian fresh water in provincial hospitals in the near future.
