(Phnom Penh): It is unfortunate and outrageous that a group of people only think of fabricating stories and creating false information to pollute society. After many stories were fabricated and spread on social media, now back to "Noodles".
I have observed and noticed that the same group that has been slandering and distorting the case that the Battambang Provincial Court summoned 26 former officials and activists of the former CNRP to come in to clarify the suspicion of violating the verdict. The Supreme Court turned it into a case of eating noodles instead.
The conspiracy theorists, many of whom are hiding abroad to escape the law, are inciting the public to believe that the court summoned them because they ate noodles. They used the word "eating noodles" to ridicule the authorities and the court that they just ate noodles and were summoned for questioning.
In fact, the noodle story is a scenario of an extremist opposition group. Following the dissolution of the former opposition party by a Supreme Court ruling and the banning of 118 party officials and activists, most of the banned politicians suspended their activities in accordance with the Supreme Court ruling.
But at the same time, a group of law-abiding gangs led by foreign activists continued to break the law as they always have. The activists have developed various scenarios for their local networks to secretly follow in order to carry out political activities, hoping to hide from the authorities.
That is why now they are trying to distort the story to mislead the public that just eating noodles was summoned by the court. But they know very well that the noodles are just a loaf of bread. So let the extremists not distort the situation! The truth can not be distorted.
In Cambodia, people have all kinds of freedom to do business and choose a job or eat freely. Who wants to eat noodles, noodles, millet, fried rice, fried duck eggs, baby until all the delicious food in the store is complete freedom without hindrance. But no matter what you eat, as long as you do something illegal or do something that the law forbids, you will be punished. So, I come up with ideas, and to see them flush it out, it's really fun.
For this reason, all the secret plans that have been put out of the country can not be overlooked by the authorities, no matter what the image and form, including the image of a gathering to eat noodles. Also. Noodle eaters are innocent and legitimate politicians are innocent. But you take the noodles to make a shield to cover up illegal activities, is that a crime?
So please do not turn the law into a noodle story. Misrepresentation, incitement to pollute society with the intent to commit a crime is also a crime.
