(Phnom Penh): Ms. Rona Smith, UN Special Rapporteur on Human Rights in Cambodia, expressed her pleasure at the Royal Government of Cambodia for taking the opportunity to share information on progress in response to its past recommendations. Like updating the evolving situation since her previous mission.
On May 9, 2019, Ms. Rona Smith issued a statement concluding her mission on the human rights situation in Cambodia following the completion of her seventh mission as UN Special Rapporteur.
She thanked the government for inviting her to visit and for the willingness of many government officials to agree to meet with her and openly discuss human rights and sustainable development in Cambodia.
"I am pleased to see that many senior government ministers have taken the opportunity to share information on progress in response to my past recommendations, as well as to update the situation since My previous mission. I also met with many other stakeholders, including representatives of civil society, the diplomatic community and the United Nations in Cambodia.
Please be informed that Ms. Rona Smith arrived in Cambodia on April 28 for an 11-day visit from April 29 to May 9, 2019 at the invitation of the Royal Government of Cambodia.
The UN Special Rapporteur regularly completes official missions to Cambodia and reports annually to the Human Rights Council, which appointed her in March 2015.
In October 2018, Ms. Rona Smith also paid an 11-day visit to Cambodia, during which she met with senior government officials, civil society representatives and members of the diplomatic community. She will present a report to the Human Rights Council in September 2019.
