Nationwide Traffic Law Enforcement Campaign, May 08: 774 illegal vehicles were found and 551 fines were imposed.
(Phnom Penh): Nationwide Traffic Law Enforcement Campaign For May 08, 2019, the traffic police force inspected 4,201 vehicles and found 774 vehicles violating the law (36% motorcycles), 223 education vehicles and 551 fines. This is according to the official report of the Traffic Police and Public Order Department of the General Commission of the National Police.
According to the report, 2,392 helmets and goggles were inspected on May 8, 156 education helmets and 475 glasses were fined.
For the results of the 8-day inspection from May 1 to 8, 2019, the police inspected 23,309 vehicles and found 4,954 offending vehicles (36% motorcycles), including education 1,662 units and fines of 3,292 units. Battambang Provincial Administrative Unity Command holds meeting to pass the April 2019 report and raise the direction
