(Phnom Penh): The United Nations Special Rapporteur on Human Rights in Cambodia, Rona Smith, has promised in front of Senior Minister and Minister of Planning Chhay Thorn that she will help spread the word about the Royal Government. The Cambodian government urges the Cambodian people to ensure that no one is left behind by 2030.
The expert's promise was made during a meeting with the Minister of Planning at the Ministry of Planning on the morning of May 7, 2019 yesterday. This is according to the press release of the Ministry of Planning on May 08, which was received by Fresh News.
At this stage, the Royal Government has been in the process of preparing the National Strategic Development Plan (NDPC) 2019-2023, which is a tool for the implementation of the fourth phase of the Rectangular Strategy and to achieve the CSDGs and the vision of Cambodia 2030. Become a high middle income country and Cambodia Vision 2050 as a developed country.
Currently, this document (PYC) 2019-2023 has been reviewed and approved by the Economic and Financial Policy Committee and will be forwarded to the Supreme National Council for consultation and advice before it is reviewed and approved by the committee. Minister from the National Assembly and the hand of the King, which Mr. Chhay Thorn is very confident that will be officially announced at the end of the first half or the beginning of the third quarter of 2019.
Ms. Rona Smith also commended and highly appreciated the efforts and high commitment of the Ministry of Planning, especially the Royal Government of Cambodia in achieving the Sustainable Development Goals of Cambodia 2016-2030, and she promised to help promote Provide a comprehensive understanding of the Royal Government of Cambodia's policies and activities to the general Cambodian people to ensure that no one is left behind by 2030.
Mr. Chhay Thorn also expressed his warm welcome to her most precious mission to Cambodia and expressed his deep gratitude for the indispensable development partnership with her family. The United Nations, in particular UNDP, has contributed to achieving most of the Millennium Development Goals of Cambodia until the United Nations selected Cambodia as one of the six model countries in the world.
Banteay Meanchey Provincial Governor Change Ceremony will be held on the morning of May 10
(Phnom Penh): The change ceremony of Banteay Meanchey Provincial Governor, replacing Mr. Ou Rathrey, Deputy Provincial Governor, will be held on the morning of May 10, 2019, presided over by Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior. This is according to the letter from the Director General of Administration of the Ministry of Interior, Mr. Prak Sam Oeun, sent to the Banteay Meanchey Provincial Administration.
It should be noted that His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, King of Cambodia, on May 08, 2019, issued a Royal Decree appointing Mr. Ou Rathrey as Governor of Banteay Meanchey Province to replace Mr. Suon Bovor, who was transferred to work at Ministry of Interior.
The Royal Decree was issued after a request from the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, to request the transfer of Mr. Suon Bavor to the Ministry of Interior and the appointment of a Deputy Provincial Governor, Mr. Ou Rath. Provinces instead.
It is noteworthy that the change of duties of the Banteay Meanchey provincial governor came after Mr. Suon Bavor was sued by a woman claiming to be a mistress in connection with their love affair.
