Preah Sihanouk Provincial CamControl Branch Continues Food Inspection for Prohibited Chemicals
(Preah Sihanouk): Officials from CamControl Preah Sihanouk Branch continued to inspect fresh food or fresh seafood, pre-packaged food and inspected the dates of various kinds of goods that traders put up for sale at Crab Market. At home and in the supermarket of a Chinese boss in Sihanoukville.
Mr. Chea Pech, Deputy Chief of CamControl Preah Sihanouk Branch, who led the team to inspect the quality of goods or food on May 08, 2019, emphasized that the purpose of the inspection of goods of CamControl officials to research and prevent the traffic of defective goods. Fake labels, expiration dates and contain banned chemicals that harm the health of consumers.
Mr. Chea Pech said that during the inspection of food and other goods, officials took some food samples for preliminary testing, including shrimp, squid, fish, fresh fish, steamed fish and beans to find banned chemicals. May affect people's health.
At the same time, professional officers inspected for non-compliance on the packaging of various food products.
As a result, there were no banned chemicals on the food products, but some expired and defective products were found on display, including: 12 bottles of snail oil or 3.12 kg at the Mart Market Han Ji-koo, who has a Chinese boss.
Mr. Chea Pech said that after the expiration date, the professional officers made a note and confiscated the goods and stored them at the Sihanoukville branch for destruction and instructed the traders to understand. And follow the law on quality control, safety of products, goods and services to avoid affecting the health of people will be able to face the law.
