Chinese Ambassador to Cambodia Wang Winthean considers this action plan to be the most important achievement in Prime Minister Hun Sen's invitation to attend the 2nd "Belt and Road" International Cooperation Summit.
The Ambassador considered the signing of the China-Cambodia Joint Destiny Community Action Plan as one of the most meaningful official documents to guide the development of China-China comprehensive strategic partnership cooperation. And Cambodia.
In a message expressing views on building a common destiny between China and Cambodia posted on Facebook on May 8, 2019, the Ambassador reminded that China and Cambodia are good neighbors. The two countries formally established diplomatic relations in July 1958 and established a comprehensive strategic partnership and cooperation in December 2010.
Only three months later, this meaningful cross-sectoral action plan emerged, signaling a step to a new level in the history of all relations, cooperation, strategic partnership. Corner between China and Cambodia.
1. Fullness: The content of the action plan is formulated on the basis of extensive consultations and recommendations from party and government institutions, the legislature and the administration at all levels of both parties, including clear goals and measures. In fact, 31 projects on cooperation in five major areas: politics, security, economy, people and multilateralism.
At the same time, deepen cooperation in law enforcement and security, ensure the smooth construction process of the Belt and Road Strategy, safeguard security, stability and development benefits of the two countries.
The Ambassador also stated that the signing of the Action Plan for Building a Common Destiny Community will help China-Cambodia relations go further and more stable and will be a catalyst for promoting Sino-Cambodian relations. , As a link between inspiring confidence in cooperation with neighboring countries and as an experimental task in building a community of common destiny of mankind.
