(Phnom Penh): On the morning of Wednesday, May 8, 2019, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, presided over the celebration of the 156th anniversary of the World Day. Red Cross and Red Crescent, May 8, held at the Cambodian Red Cross headquarters in Phnom Penh.
The celebration of this solemn day was led by Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross, and was attended by about 4,000 dignitaries, national and international leaders, philanthropists and students.
World Red Cross Red Crescent Day is celebrated annually with the aim of promoting achievements and raising funds to continue humanitarian operations to help the most vulnerable people across Cambodia, regardless of political affiliation, race, religion or caste. Any color.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the theme "I love the Cambodian Red Cross" for the celebration of the 156th World Red Cross Red Crescent Day is a permanent theme of the Cambodian Red Cross.
* Samdech Techo emphasized that without love, there would be no support for the Cambodian Red Cross.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that it was fortunate for Cambodia that Samdech Preah Borom Rattanakoth Norodom Sihanouk moved to establish the Cambodian Red Cross.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that nearly 140,000 Cambodian families have been rescued by the Cambodian Red Cross.
* Samdech Techo assessed that this charitable activity is a brave action of the Red Cross.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the humanitarian activities of the Cambodian Red Cross have made a special contribution to the social protection policy of the Royal Government of Cambodia.
* Samdech Techo also commended the Cambodian Red Cross Youth Volunteers across the country for their timely response to natural disasters.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen also thanked all local authorities for their efforts to help the victims.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the actions of the authorities and the Red Cross are complementary to help the victims.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen expressed his gratitude to the King of Cambodia and His Majesty the Queen Mother of Cambodia, who have always cared about the Cambodian Red Cross and have always visited the Cambodian people everywhere. .
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen thanked all the philanthropists who have contributed to the Cambodian Red Cross.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the art and culture of sharing is very meaningful for the people of Cambodia.
* Samdech Techo emphasized that if the Cambodian people do not have the art to share, it is very difficult.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the shared culture of the people is in all fields, in which the Buddhist sector can not build temples without the sharing of the Buddhists. In the field of education in the past, without the participation of the people, it would not have been possible to build school buildings.
* Samdech Techo stated that he expects the art of sharing from those who can afford it to those who cannot afford it to continue.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the culture of sharing is not only within the national framework, but also in the global framework, both bilaterally and multilaterally.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen noted that the current situation of the world, especially refugees and internally displaced persons, has created a worrying issue that requires mutual assistance.
* Samdech Techo stated that climate change is becoming a growing concern for Cambodia, just in recent days, the phenomenon of rain and wind has affected the homes of many people.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that due to the rain these days, Cambodia's hydropower can generate about 600 megawatts out of more than 1,400 megawatts.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen called for together to make the president of "I love the Cambodian Red Cross" become a movement, become a reality and become a movement of the whole nation.
* Samdech Techo continues to call for the "I love the Cambodian Red Cross" movement from the leadership to the people.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen expressed the hope that all philanthropists will jointly donate resources to support the Cambodian Red Cross to help vulnerable and vulnerable people.
