"What is the historical legacy of the Cambodian People's Party, as well as myself and other leaders of the party and the Royal Government, is the achievement of national unification, the end of the war through win-win politics, but "The bigger problem is that our country is not trying to bridge the gap between race and religion. What we have done over the last 40 years is to harmonize race and religion."
