Cambodia, Italy agree to keep 8 agencies to provide international adoption services for another 3 years
(Phnom Penh): Cambodia and Italy have decided to maintain the same number of agencies in accordance with the agreement on the number of international adoption agencies allowed to provide services in Cambodia, signed on September 17. 2018 by Minister Vong Soth is automatically valid for another 3 years.
This decision was made during a working meeting between Mr. Nim Thoth, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation, representing Mr. Vong Soth, Minister of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation, met with Mr. Gianni Bardini, Central Member of Italy and Representative of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs. Italy and Ms. Martina represent the Embassy of Italy on the afternoon of May 7, 2019 at the Ministry of Social Affairs.
On that occasion, Mr. Nim Chuot, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Social Affairs, thanked for the invitation of the Italian delegation, represented by Mr. GIANNI BARDINI, Member of the Central Committee for International Adoption of Italy, representing the Central Authority for International Adoption. Italy.
During the meeting that afternoon, in addition to agreeing to maintain eight agencies to provide international adoption services in Cambodia for the next three years, the two sides agreed and decided on a number of points, including:
1. The Cambodian side requested to divide the number of the eight agencies into two groups of four agencies, which were divided by the Internal Authority of Cambodia. At this point, the Italian side agreed. Each agency has the same rights and obligations to be legally responsible for the adoption of children of Cambodia and Italy.
2: Both parties agree after the signing of this memorandum, both parties will report to the Central International Adoption Authority of Cambodia and Italy from the results of the discussions and start to prepare relevant documents, especially short guidelines for guidance. To an accredited agency to conduct an international adoption procedure in accordance with the International Adoption Act of Cambodia.
3. Although the agreement is automatically renewed every three years, the two sides need to set a time and place to meet and discuss, evaluate the results of previous years of cooperation and set directions for the next three years.
He expressed his commitment to further enhance this cooperation and promised that there would be no illegal international adoption in Cambodia.
