Sustainable tourism development and marine environment are the main topics of the ADB Annual Meeting, Cambodia proposes ADB funding for major investment projects
(Fiji): The 52nd Meeting of the Board of Governors or the 2019 Annual Meeting of the Asian Development Bank (ADB) held from 2 to 5 May 2019 in Nadi, Fiji Achieved as planned to achieve environmental prosperity, resilience and sustainability for the Asia-Pacific region.
Mr. Vongsey Visoth, Permanent Secretary of State of the Ministry of Economy and Finance and Cambodia's Deputy Governor for the Asian Development Bank, chaired the meeting on behalf of Cambodia, who was elected Deputy Chairman of the Board of Governors.
It should be noted that tourism has been playing an important role in promoting economic growth and job creation. In fact, the number of international tourist arrivals to the Asia-Pacific region reached about 350 million in 2018, doubling from 2005.
At the same time, Asians are also more tourism, with an increasing middle class population combined with the development of relevant infrastructure to serve tourism. Looking to the future, especially in the context of the Fourth Industrial Revolution with the use of robots and artificial intelligence (AI), tourism will become one of the most widely used sectors.
In this regard, the entire region must continue to promote sustainable tourism development by investing in the development of human resources and skills to serve the tourism sector with consideration for environmental sustainability, cultural heritage and local communities.
In a transcript of the minutes of the 52nd Annual Meeting of the ADB Board of Governors, Mr. Vongsey Visoth, Permanent Secretary of the Ministry of Economy and Finance and Deputy Governor of Cambodia, led the Cambodian delegation. This highlights the progress that Cambodia has made in the past, highlighting key economic achievements in the last five years.
The Secretary of State also mentioned that significant progress has been made in raising revenue, making the Royal Government more able to increase expenditures on priority sectors and areas to improve economic efficiency and productivity. In addition, he mentioned the key policy priorities of the Royal Government of the 6th legislature of the National Assembly in promoting economic diversification and enhancing Cambodia's competitiveness.
In this meeting, he highly appreciated the cooperation and close and sincere partnership between the Royal Government of Cambodia and ADB, especially the achievement of the Strategic Framework for the Partnership for Development of Cambodia 2019-2023.
