(Phnom Penh): The Korea Agency for International Cooperation (KICA) in Cambodia on May 6, 2019 organized a orientation program for 12 Cambodian government officials from the Supreme Court Prosecutor General for a training course on "Capacity Building on Prevent crime and justice ASEAN crime. The course will run from 12 to 25 May 2019 for 14 days at the Yongin Institute of Justice in the Republic of Korea.
The pre-departure orientation program is designed to facilitate Cambodian officials adapting to Korean culture while studying in the Republic of Korea. In this orientation program, KOICA officials in Cambodia presented important information in Korea, the Cambodian-Korean Alumni Association (CAMKAA), ethics of training programs and information on measles.
According to Kang Hwang Wook, Deputy Chief Representative of KICA in Cambodia, KICA provides training to ASEAN on crime prevention and justice in Cambodia to increase the capacity of the criminal justice system to prevent crime.
The purpose of the course is to train participants in a variety of knowledge programs, including: First: Understanding cybercrime and Korea's criminal policy, Second: Finding appropriate solutions to problem solving and policy development. Highly effective criminal offenses based on the criminal justice system; third, the development of practical plans to respond to local situations; and fourth, the implementation of cooperative measures on international crimes.
Mr. Kang Hwang Wook welcomed and congratulated the participants who received this training and also asked the participants to use this great opportunity to learn about the development of Korea and to share their experiences in Cambodia for Sustainable development.
Finally, the shortlisted candidates expressed their gratitude to KOICA and the Government of Korea for their support of the training and their high commitment to participate in capacity building for comprehensive understanding of development projects, especially in the prevention of Offenses and Justice Offenses for ASEAN (Cambodia). Satellite captures North Korea test-fire missile on east coast (Photo inside)
