(Phnom Penh): Dr. O Vandin, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Health, urges the relevant officials to continue to pay attention to clear and targeted work activities in order to effectively eradicate malaria in accordance with the set strategy. .
Dr. O Vandin said that the Ministry of Health pays special attention to Professor Mam Bunheng, the Minister of Health, who is always concerned about the effective implementation of malaria eradication in accordance with the strategy given to the Ministry of Health by Samdech Techo. Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia. The National Malaria Eradication Strategy 2011-2025 also has the full support of Samdech Techo.
Moreover, she said that it was the eradication of the common malaria that sent a message to guide and show political and technical support for the efforts to eradicate malaria.
At the same time, the doctor made some important recommendations, such as:
Call on people to take care to prevent mosquito bites, especially children and mobile people.
* Health officials and all relevant partner organizations must contribute most actively to achieve the National Strategic Plan for Malaria Eradication 2011-2025, especially in the first phase to eradicate falciparum malaria by 2020. .
* Focus on malaria testing and timely treatment of high-risk populations (foresters) in areas with high malaria incidence, such as Preah Vihear and Stung Treng in Siem Pang district.
* May health officials and all relevant partner organizations continue to work better to ensure the smooth implementation of the program towards success.
* Health officials and all relevant partner organizations are asked to jointly review the progress of work, risk factors and opportunities related to the implementation of the RAI2E project to discuss solutions, actions and implement together successfully according to the goals of the elimination strategy. Malaria.
Further strengthen the malaria service system and call for the broad participation of the community. The Ministry of Environment believes that the tram of the international racing team is a message urging the public to take care of the environment and natural resources in Prey Lang.
(Phnom Penh): After the success of organizing a series of motor racing events, in May 2019, the Ministry of Environment together with the Motor Sports Federation of Cambodia, KARA and some other partners will organize a motor racing event through a new obstacle by Pass through the "Prey Lang" wildlife sanctuary and some other wildlife sanctuaries.
Mr. Ho Sithikun said that the motocross race in Prey Lang Wildlife Sanctuary was held under the theme "Together to protect the environment and natural resources", starting from May 17 and ending. On May 20, 2019, it will pass through four provinces, including Kampong Thom, Preah Vihear and Siem Reap, especially through the Prey Lang Wildlife Sanctuary.
He said that the vehicles participating in this international motor racing event include 20 motorcycle racing teams. The team has a total of 21 cars, including 15 national team race cars, 4 international team race cars and 2 spare vehicles.
Mr. Neth Pheaktra said that not only through Prey Lang Wildlife Sanctuary, the team will also pass through some other wildlife sanctuaries such as Boeung Pe Wildlife Sanctuary and Prey Preah Roka Wildlife Sanctuary. In Preah Vihear, on arrival in Siem Reap, the team will pass through Phnom Kulen National Park and other protected areas.
The Secretary of State for the Ministry of Environment expressed his belief that this event is also a part of drawing the public's attention to the protection of the environment and natural resources, especially the prevention of deforestation.
