(Phnom Penh): Mr. Veng Sakhon, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, in the afternoon of Monday, May 3, 2019, chaired a meeting to monitor and evaluate the progress. Of the implementation of projects that the Ministry has been cooperating with various development partners in the framework of the agricultural sector. The meeting was held at the Ministry.
The meeting was also attended by the Secretary of State, Undersecretary of State, Head of Unit and Project Implementation Officer.
The keynote speakers made a series of presentations to the meeting on the progress of the project: First, the project to improve the infrastructure of the agricultural value chain, second: the progress of the production chain project by the environmental brotherhood, third: the project to promote food production, 4: Food production and rice export project. The four projects highlighted the main points to inform the meeting about:
Objectives, budgets, expenditures, sources, budgets, implementation time, provincial projects, project implementation partners, transition results, expected results, challenges, questions and answers of members, and especially the interpretation of good ideas and strategies of the Minister for project implementation officers Make improvements to make the implementation of the project more successful.
Attached to the results, the Minister stated that the achievements of the project so far are inseparable from the merits of the Royal Government of Cambodia through the Ministry of Economy and Finance, international development agencies and development partners who have supported both financial resources. And techniques to implement internal projects.
He thanked the Royal Government, ministries, institutions and relevant authorities at all levels for their cooperation in implementing the projects until they achieved good results and hoped and believed that this wonderful cooperation would continue to strengthen and expand. Better in the context of deepening positions for economic growth.
After grasping all the main points of the presentation
The Minister confirmed to the meeting that we generally recognize that the implementation of practical projects at the local level always produces good results and also meet the shortcomings, so to increase the capacity to manage the project and continue to innovate all action plans. To make the project a success as planned, he made the following important recommendations:
1: Project officials must be willing to stand on clear criteria in negotiating the budget to implement the project to ensure that the project covers a wide range of agriculture. In addition, the project must select subjects in accordance with the agricultural development policy plan for 2019-2023 to meet the needs of the actual beneficiaries, especially the expected results are to meet the will and indicators of the Royal Government.
2: There must be a plan or program to evaluate the results of the project in detail and accurately at each stage to measure the change or change the living standards of the people and the community in a timely manner, especially the budget of the state, development partners, development agencies National and international development spent.
3. The director of the Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries in the target provinces to implement the project must support and increase cooperation in order to develop in a targeted manner and respond to what local people need and want. Yes.
4: The project director or project officer should prepare a short document (video clip) to show the actual project results to the public, especially to improve the living standards of the people after benefiting from the project.
6: To increase the ability and intelligence to lead the implementation of the project to increase efficiency and effectiveness, increase value, trust and sustainability.
7: The project should strengthen the capacity of the community to produce seeds, vegetables, rice and fish to ensure community supply, reduce production and import capital. This case can be contracted with a development partner or a private company to produce seeds, guaranteeing the quantity and quality of seeds by implementing contract agricultural production.
8. The project should review the strengths and weaknesses of Good Agricultural Practices (GAP) because the adoption of some modern technologies by farmers is still limited. The first phase of Phnom Penh cycling event has many participants in previous years
