For the upcoming Pisak Bochea, the Capital-Provincial Committees (22 Capital-Provincial Prisons and 3 Correctional Centers) have issued pardon letters to a total of 252 inmates, including 16 women. Make a final decision to submit to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia to the King.
Mr. Soch Sophannara explained that the amnesty focused on those prisoners who had made good changes in the capitals, provinces, and cities he was a role model in the prison and had complied with the prison standards that the prison authorities requested. Mitigation and pardon.
He said the amnesty was based on humanitarian principles, including women, the elderly, 65 years of age and older, inmates in prison, children with mothers with difficulty living.
