Donors Donate Water Purifiers and Study Materials to Children
This charitable aid and humanitarian activity was provided to the children at Se Ametri Village Organization in Chambok Trop Village, Prek Roka Commune, Kandal Steung District, Kandal Province.
Ms. Svay Muy, Director of Komar Se Ametri Village, said that the donation of water purifiers from philanthropists and hydrotic companies is very important for the organization and students. By helping children get clean and safe drinking water, help children stay healthy as well as reduce the cost of buying water.
She added that the study materials provided by Hydro 6 will help alleviate the shortage of study materials in Se Ametri Village School. Not only that, the children gained knowledge about education, health, environment and hygiene, especially receiving love and eating lunch together.
The director of Komar Se Ametri Village thanked the benefactors, management and staff of Hydro 6 for their donations and humanitarian activities here.
Ms. Svay Muy said that Se Ametri Village was first established in 2003 in Phnom Penh and later moved to Kandal Steung District, Kandal Province, with the aim of helping poor children in rural areas. In particular, the income to support the school here comes from philanthropy and the opening of lakeside seating on weekends and other festivals.
She added, however, that the school still lacks and appeals to philanthropists to help the children here.
Please be informed that Se Ametri Village has 225 students studying at Se Ametri Village. The school accepts poor students from the age of 3 and offers Khmer language training through the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, as well as English, computer, sports, music and dance.
He added that the state-of-the-art technology of the Hydro6 water purifier guarantees 100% quality and safety for the water, making the filtered water a healthy combination of minerals that are most suitable for health. In addition, the company's campaign wants children to understand health, hygiene and the environment.
