A person was sleeping in the car when a power line fell on a parked car.
(Ratanakkiri): A man died while sleeping in a car due to a car fire caused by a fault in the transmission line on the road. The incident happened at 21:10 at the cassava warehouse in Village 1, Sangkat Kachanh, Banlung City, Ratanakkiri Province.
The above accident was claimed by the authorities that before the incident, there was a fault in the transmission line and the fire fell on the tires of a parked car and caused the car to catch fire. The blaze also killed the driver, who was sleeping in the car.
Major General Yin Chamnan, the provincial police commissioner, ordered fire trucks to intervene to prevent the spread of the virus to neighboring houses and other property.
Suon Savuth, chief of the Kachanh Sangkat Administration Post, said that the victim who died in the incident was 20-year-old Tho Ratana, who lived at the scene. At present, the family is arranging the funeral according to the Khmer tradition with compassion.
