Tbong Khmum Governor Tells Workers Not to Believe Incitement to Destroy the Nation
(Tbong Khmum): The Governor of Tbong Khmum Province, Mr. Cheam Chan Sophoan, appealed to the workers in Tbong Khmum Province, which is close to 20,000 people, not to believe in incitement and other activities against the Royal Government, which leads to destruction for National.
The appeal of the provincial governor was made during the celebration of the 133rd anniversary of International Labor Day on May 1, 2019 under the theme "Social protection for productivity" on May 6, 2019 yesterday. The ceremony took place at Top Sewer Limited in Oreang Ov district, Tbong Khmum province.
Mr. Cheam Chansophoan said that the celebration of International Labor Day is possible because the country is peaceful and the high attention from the Royal Government. He said that before January 7, 1979, in the genocidal regime, there was no celebration of the day to respect the rights and values of workers, only oppression, forced to work very hard.
The provincial governor told the workers that under the leadership of the Royal Government of Cambodia, headed by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, under a win-win policy and a rectangular strategy, the country will have full political stability and continuous development, especially under the policy. Samdech Techo's openness to the sky has given young people the opportunity to work to earn a living.
In order to maintain the current achievements, Mr. Cheam Chan Sophoan called on all workers to maintain the necessary peace. "Please, workers and our people, do not believe in the incitement to paint because it caused the disintegration of national unity, making Cambodia fall into the flames of war again with high ambitions, regardless of the well-being of the people. Of some unscrupulous group. ”
Tbong Khmum is one of the last provinces to be separated from Kampong Cham. The province is currently highly favorable for agriculture, especially rubber, and also for industry, providing employment to people in Tbong Khmum with reasonable wages.
In the celebration of International Labor Day yesterday, there was also a raffle to encourage workers who have worked hard in the past, and also to dance to increase the happiness and intimacy between workers. Also.
