Brief biography of King Maha Vijiralongkorn who has just officially ascended the throne in Thailand (Video inside) (Bangkok): King of Thailand King Maha Vijiralongkorn has just ascended the throne in full Thai tradition. A glorious royal wedding ceremony that started last Saturday and will end on Monday, May 6, 2019.
According to the Constitution of the Kingdom of Thailand, King Maha Vijiralongkorn has been the King since 2016, but because Thailand needs time to mourn the former King and organize more general elections, the Royal Ceremony Ascension is postponed until early May. 1: A brief biography of the King of Thailand
At the age of 20, he was appointed heir apparent by his own father.
* After King Bhumibol Adulyadej died on October 13, 2016, he was required to succeed to the throne at that time. But he ordered a delay to continue mourning the Father.
Until the night of December 1, 2016, he also agreed to ascend the throne, but has not yet performed the full royal ceremony.
* Although the body of King Bhumibol Adulyadej was cremated on October 26, 2017, the traditional coronation ceremony of King Maha Vijiralongkorn was postponed further because the Thai nation was still under A time of mourning.
* Until May 4, 2019, the official coronation ceremony according to the tradition of the royal family took place for a total of 3 days.
However, according to the Thai government, the reign of King Maha Vijiralongkorn began on October 13, 2016, when King Bhumibol Adulyadej died. As the 10th King of the Chakri Dynasty of Thailand, King Vijira Longkorn is also known as King Rama X, and he became the oldest Thai King to ascend the throne in 2016. He is up to 64 years old.
2: History of the study of love and works of King Maha Vichiralongkorn
* King Maha Vijiralongkorn was educated at a palace in Bangkok.
* Then, at the age of 13, he was sent to two private schools in the United Kingdom for five years, and for the last year he attended another school in Sydney, Australia.
For the next four years, King Maha Vijiralongkorn spent time training at the Military University in Canberra.
* He continued to receive additional military training both in Thailand and abroad, including the United Kingdom, the United States and Australia, and eventually became a military officer in the Thai Armed Forces.
* In 1972, King Maha Vijiralongkorn was appointed by King Bhumibol Adulyadej as his successor, but he also faced some scandals.
