(Phnom Penh): The General Commission of the National Police and the Cambodian Authority for Mine Action and Mine Action for Disabled People on the morning of May 6, 2019, reaffirmed their joint commitment to achieve the plan. Defined in the Royal Government's policy on demining from Cambodia by 2025.
A joint commitment was made during a working meeting between General Sant Neth Savoeun, National Police Commissioner General, and Mr. Ly Thuch, Senior Minister in Charge of Special Missions and First Deputy Chief of the Mine Authority on the rate of explosive ordnance. .
Speaking to the media after the meeting, Lt. Gen. Chhay Kim Khoeun, Deputy Commissioner General of the National Police, confirmed that "in that meeting, both sides agreed and agreed on some challenges that must be addressed together, especially to push for a clean-up. "By 2025 to clear mines in accordance with government policy."
At the same time, Senior Minister Ly Thuch made a number of suggestions to the General Commission of the National Police, including requesting the National Police to provide additional guidance to the police force at the Capital-Provincial Commission to the Police Administration Post to promote education and dissemination. Citizens are involved in understanding the law as well as understanding the dangers posed by landmines.
In addition, efforts must be made to end the activities of the use of explosive waste for storage by doing business that is different from the instructions that cause accidents and to increase and complete the collection of data related to the explosive ordnance disposal business. As well as disseminating the policy of safe villages and communes.
In response to Senior Minister Ly Thuch's request, General Dr. Neth Savoeun also clarified some additional situations and challenges to continue to work together based on the request of the Mines Authority to set the direction by preparing a plan. Practical action.
The General Commissioner of the National Police also agreed to prepare a memorandum of understanding to increase cooperation between the Mine Authority and the National Police, focusing on the support of the Mine Authority on the Cambodian National Police Force, including training, provision of equipment and Experiences to mobilize more active police forces to clear mines.
