According to the Ministry of Justice, for the Pisak Bochea festival, the Capital-Provincial Committees (22 Capital-Provincial Prisons and 3 Correctional Centers) have issued pardon letters to a total of 252 prisoners, including 16 women.
However, the Minister of Justice will review the qualifications of the prisoners and make a final decision to submit to the head of the Royal Government, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, to request the King to pardon and commute the sentences.
Mr. Eang Sophalleth, Personal Assistant to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, told reporters after the meeting that during the meeting, Ms. Polintha Messiah respectfully informed Samdech Techo Hun Sen that the United Nations would like to congratulate Work carried out in the past year.
Meetings between UN agencies and the Royal Government are held once a year, and this is the fifth time that a group of UN agencies has met with the Royal Government.
In this meeting, the United Nations raised three points: First: related to social protection, second: data for sustainable development, and third: the issue of participation in reviewing national reports on the implementation of development goals. Sustainable in the coming New York City.
Regarding the first point, social protection In this case, the UN system mentioned three points: first, the coordination between institutions and infrastructure in capacity building, second, social and financial protection, and third, social protection work with Practice with equality.
For this work, Samdech Techo Hun Sen allowed a number of ministries to interpret, including the Ministry of Economy and Finance, the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training, the Ministry of Health, the Ministry of Planning, the Ministry of Women's Affairs and the Ministry of Social Affairs.
The Prime Minister informed the United Nations that in the past, Cambodia was 100% poor and there was a start to provide social protection to pregnant women and then to working women. At the factory. Then to the poor women and also do some work, including reducing electricity prices, building infrastructure, digging wells, ponds, etc., are all social protection.
The second point is related to data for development, in which case Samdech Techo Hun Sen allowed four ministries to interpret, including the Ministry of Planning, the Ministry of Economy and Finance, the Ministry of Women's Affairs and the Ministry of Education. At the same time, Samdech Techo also informed about this case, which the UN system proposed to increase the national budget and strengthen the capacity for data work for this development.
Samdech Techo, the head of the Royal Government, explained that in the past, the Royal Government of Cambodia has pushed for funding, increased the national budget on a regular basis, and agreed to increase the budget for data work for this development.
Regarding the capacity building, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also introduced the promotion of undergraduate and postgraduate studies in this field, and Mr. Hang Chuon Naron, Minister of Education, also introduced Also go to universities to promote education up to bachelor's and master's degrees related to the data program for this education.
Third, in relation to the meeting of the National Volunteer Report on the Implementation of the Sustainable Development Goals, the UN system has requested that Cambodia attend the New York meeting in July and support Get involved with all relevant institutions.
