CSX Holds Fourth Cambodia Stock Exchange Expo to Promote and Boost Investor Confidence
The exhibition was attended by Dr. Hean Sahip, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, Mr. Ham Chonghan, Acting Ambassador of the Embassy of the Republic of Korea to Cambodia, Mr. Sou Socheat, Director General of the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia, Mr. Chong Yung-gil Korea International Cooperation Agency in Cambodia and Mr. Hong Sochua, Director General of the Cambodia Securities Exchange, as well as many distinguished guests.
The fair aims to further promote and enhance the confidence of existing investors in the stock market through face-to-face meetings with listed companies, providing opportunities for the public to gain a broader understanding of investing in the market, such as opening up. Trading accounts, trading methods, market data, review of company financial statements, understanding of dividend distribution, as well as other topics on the market question.
This system allows investors to check cash balances and securities, place trading orders, modify and cancel orders on their own, as well as view past trading orders and data, as well as request withdrawals. In addition, investors can monitor market data, announcements, timely and important for investment decisions.
The system also enables investors to access listed company information faster.
He added that the CSX will also have some changes, such as the extension of trading hours until 3 pm, while currently trading at 11:30 am only. These show another step forward of the stock market.
Mr. Sou Socheat highly appreciated the organization of such exhibition as a promotional campaign in order to promote the growth of the capital market in Cambodia. He said that the securities market in Cambodia is in the context of rapid growth in terms of legal structure, market structure, issuers, as well as the number of national and international investors. Therefore, all stakeholders must work together to develop the market to meet the momentum of market demand.
Dr. Hean Sahip also said that the Cambodia Stock Exchange My First Stock 2019 is a good initiative of the Cambodia Securities Exchange to raise awareness and promote the study of investment opportunities in the stock market. Cambodia by the public. At the same time, strengthening transparency, trust and predictability is essential to allow the Cambodian stock market to move forward and develop sustainably.
He added that all this work will contribute to help increase the efficiency of work in the stock market. Therefore, on behalf of the Ministry of Economy and Finance and the Chairman of the Board of Directors of the Cambodia Securities Exchange, please support such promotional activities, as well as request all stakeholders to participate more in attracting investors and publishers. Discover a brief profile of the new Japanese emperor Naruhito
