Tomorrow, Muslims in Cambodia begin to practice the obligation to fast, why fast?
Ramadan is the ninth month in the Islamic lunar calendar and is considered the lord of the other months. Because the lunar calendar year is 11 days shorter than the solar calendar, Ramadan revolves around each season. Example: Ramadan in 2018 falls on May 17, while Ramadan in 2019 falls on Monday, May 6, and it will continue to decrease every year.
