Legal Awareness: Acquisition of Ownership through Purchase and Sale
(Phnom Penh): In the spirit of the Civil Code, the acquisition of ownership of immovable property may be made by a succession contract and the reasons set forth in Section 4 (Acquisition of Ownership), as well as the provisions of the Civil Code or other laws.
Because: In the current situation, the real estate sector in Cambodia is growing remarkably, and issues related to the acquisition of property ownership are also raised.
For the interpretation of this topic, our program only deals with the acquisition (transfer) of ownership through the purchase and sale of real estate with a certificate of ownership of the property (hard copy).
A contract of sale arising out of the agreement of the parties is a type of private contract to guarantee the exercise of the rights and obligations of the parties to the contract, especially focusing on the obligation to acquire (transfer) ownership or other rights over Real estate to the buyer.
According to the spirit of Article 135 of the Civil Code, the transfer of ownership of immovable property by agreement is not effective if it is not registered in accordance with the registration provisions.
That is, in order to be able to arrange the transfer of ownership, the parties must complete a form called a letter of sale at the Cadastral Administration and fingerprint it in front of the competent officer of the cadastral unit where the immovable property is located.
Documents required to process the transfer of ownership include:
3. The contract prohibiting the distribution of undivided immovable property in the case of undivided property, and the application for registration of the contract prohibiting the distribution of undivided immovable property is made together with one (1) copy of the transfer registration application (original) and 2 (two) legalized copies.
4: Proof of court authorization in the case of immovable property that is the subject of sale, purchase, belonging to a minor, a person under the general guardianship or a dependent person and is using that person's residence (original or copy which Legalized).
5: 3 (three) copies of Khmer Nationality ID card of the person applying for registration:
6: Proof of property of the person who has the right to register as a natural person:
After fulfilling the obligation to pay 4% tax, the Cadastral Administration will then complete the procedure of transfer of ownership from the seller to the buyer by registering the transfer of ownership in the official records and recording the transfer of ownership. Title deed, which is the final procedure for completing the transfer of ownership permanently and in accordance with the law.
