Stung Treng Provincial Governor Visits Siem Pang District
(Stung Treng): On the morning of May 4, 2019, Stung Treng Provincial Governor Mom Saroeun visited people in Siem Pang district, which is a malaria-prone area.
On that occasion, Mr. Mom Saroeun visited and instructed the people to protect their health, especially in that area, which is a malaria area, to be careful and before going to bed to tie mosquito nets.
At the same time, he called on ethnic minorities to take care and take care of their health.
At the same time, Mr. Oum Soviet, Director of the Provincial Health Department, also called on the local authorities to inform the local people, if there is malaria, please go to the hospital and health center.
"If people go to the forest, they have to wear long clothes to protect themselves from mosquitoes, which if they bite, it will cause fever and chills," he said. When going to bed, you must tie a mosquito net and use a mosquito net soaked in medicine to avoid danger.
