The official results of the election of the new Sihanoukville Chamber of Commerce leader end today!
(Preah Sihanouk): A senior official of the Ministry of Commerce of the Kingdom of Cambodia said that Saturday, May 4, is the last official election day of the election of the Sihanoukville Chamber of Commerce for the mandate. Second, second.
The election was held at the Sihanoukville Provincial Department of Commerce and was chaired by Mr. Mao Thora, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Commerce.
On that occasion, Mr. Mao Thora said that this election is the election of 5 Vice Presidents for the second term of the Sihanoukville Chamber of Commerce after the election of the new President of the Chamber of Commerce. This was completed on April 21, 2019.
He said that the results of the election won or received the position of Vice President of Sihanoukville Provincial Chamber of Commerce of the new 5 mandates, including: Mr. Chhun Sarom, Mr. Preap Sopheap, Mrs. Khem Chenda, Mr. Oknha Sok Heng and Lok Chumteav Ghech Muy.
The President of the Sihanoukville Chamber of Commerce for the second term, who has already voted for the second term, went to Mr. Oknha Vann Sokheng, who voted to defeat Mr. Oknha Lao Kaing, the former President of the Preah Sihanouk Provincial Chamber of Commerce for the previous term. Duke Lao Kaing has been appointed as the honorary chairman by the new leadership of the Sihanoukville Chamber of Commerce.
At this point, Mr. Mao Thora, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Commerce, spoke in support of the composition of the head of the Sihanoukville Chamber of Commerce in the new mandate, with two young women to serve as Vice President of the Second Chamber of Commerce for the second term. Now.
