Ratanakkiri Provincial Authority Celebrates the 133rd Anniversary of International Labor Day, May 1, 2019 under the Theme "Social Protection for Productivity"
Rattanakiri Province: Mr. Thong Savun, Governor of Rattanakiri Province and Mr. Nab Bunheng, Chairman of the Provincial Council, presided over the 133rd Anniversary of International Labor Day on May 1, 2019 under the theme " "Social protection for productivity." The ceremony took place at the company "Hang Anh Andong Meas" in Kon Mom district.
The ceremony was also attended by Mr. and Mrs. Deputy Governor, Director-Deputy Director of Departments around the province, Commander, Deputy Commander of the three Armed Forces, government officials, representatives of companies, enterprises, organizations, partners, more than 300 workers.
The provincial governor stated that the Royal Government has continued to pay attention to vocational training to the people to increase the professional capacity of human resources in response to the needs of the labor market and job creation. In addition, the Royal Government has set out a number of policies and strategic plans to accelerate the development and create decent jobs for the people.
Mr. Duch Chanto, Director of the Department of Labor and Vocational Training of Ratanakkiri Province, said that in order to implement the Rectangular Strategy Phase 4 of the Royal Government, the Department has continued to implement the strategic plan for the development of employment and vocational training for the period of 2019-2023, including:
First, promote job creation, ensure better working conditions and strengthen the National Social Security Fund. Second, to develop provincial vocational training centers and provide vocational technical education and training services to the people. Third, strengthen good governance and expand gender equity.
On that occasion, the provincial leaders distributed souvenirs to more than 300 workers who participated. On the morning of the same day, the provincial governor, the chairman of the provincial council and all the accompanying officials inspected the production line of Hang Anh Andong Meas banana banana for export.
It should be noted that Hang Anh Economic Land Concession Company has invested in cultivating many kinds of agricultural crops such as bananas, dragon fruit, grapefruit, and pepper on thousands of hectares. Currently, the export of bananas is 8,000 tons per month. The company also employs more than 2,000 workers.
