Ministry of Interior reveals the results of Prince Sar Kheng's official visit to South Korea
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Interior has issued a press release on the results of the official visit of Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior, from April 30 to May 3, 2019 in the Republic of Korea (Korea). South).
A press release obtained by Fresh News on the morning of May 4, 2019 stated that during his visit, Sar Kheng met with South Korean Minister of Interior and Security Jing Yong and both sides Agreed to set the direction of cooperation on a number of important issues, including:
* First, continue to pay attention to the implementation of the memorandum that the two institutions signed with each other in the past, both on the management of sub-national administration and the work of the National Police to be successful.
* Second, continue to strengthen and expand cooperation and exchange experiences related to decentralization and deconcentration reforms, as well as capacity building of local administrative officials.
* Third: Continue to provide support for the training of human resources in the ranks of the National Police, especially in the areas of police technology and technology, as well as share and exchange experiences on security, public order, especially the fight against terrorism. Technology offenses and drug offenses.
* Fourth: Share and exchange work experience, organize and manage the identification system and population data management system to build an effective national data management center.
