Swords used for the royal wedding of the Thai king were brought from Cambodia in 1784
(Phnom Penh): On Saturday, the 1st day of the month of Pisak, Buddhist era 2562, which is on the 4th of May, 2019, tomorrow, the Royal Palace of Tep Mohanakor or Rattanakosin (Bangkok) of the Kingdom of Thailand will celebrate the royal wedding of the King. The new one is King Maha Vachiralongkorn (Siamese called Maha Vichiralongkorn) officially.
Of these five crops, the royal family was brought from Cambodia in 1784. According to the Thai royal family.
After receiving a beautiful sword from a fisherman and realizing that it was the royal family, Chao Ponhea Aphayvong brought it to the King of Siam, Samdech Preah Buddha Yotfachola Lok or Ramathibodi I.
According to the Thai royal family, during the procession into the Royal Palace of Tep Mohanakor, a miracle occurred, with lightning roaring through the sky and shooting at seven locations of the royal procession. Seems to show the mighty power of the Khmer dynasty since ancient times.
The Khmer emperor, who had left this motherland when he was taken to Thailand at that time, did not have a cane or a condom. Prince Rama I ordered the construction of a cane and a casket made of gold and gems and arranged the wedding to be one of the accessories for the royal wedding of the King of Thailand in 1785. Continue to use until today.
In the Royal Chronicle of Thailand, it is also acknowledged that the Kingdom was brought from the Kingdom of Cambodia and was spread throughout Thailand as well as around the world through one of Thailand's most popular newspapers, the Bangkok Post.
