Of the three days, this Saturday is the most important day because it is the beginning of the coronation of King Vichiralongkorn to become the full monarch of the Kingdom of Thailand. The ceremony will be held in the Buddhist and Brahminical ceremonies, beginning with the purification ceremony, in which sacred water is collected from the provinces of Thailand in early April to sprinkle the body of King Vijaya Longkorn.
It should be informed that King Maha Vijiralongkorn succeeded his father from the end of 2016, when King Bhumibol Adulyadej died. Vijira Longkorn was the second and only son of King Bhumibol Adulyadej and Queen Sirikit and became his successor in 1972.
Cambodia to sign more than $ 30 million financing agreement from France for modernization of transmission and distribution network
(Phnom Penh): The Royal Government of Cambodia will sign a cooperation financing agreement (low interest loan) worth 29.1 million euros (equivalent to about 30 million US dollars) to implement the plan to modernize the transmission system. And distribute electricity.
The signing of the new agreement will take place during the visit of Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Economy and Finance, and a high-level delegation from the Ministry to attend the Summit on "Debt Sustainability for Sustainable Growth: Sustainable Financing for Development »in Paris, France. This is according to the press release of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, which was received by Fresh News on May 4.
The low-interest financing agreement will be signed by Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, General Manager of the French Agency for Development (AFD) Remi Riou.
The summit will be attended by finance ministers, central bank governors, heads of international institutions, research institutions and representatives of major private financial institutions from about 60 countries around the world, including: The French host, the US Treasury Secretary, Japan and the Governor of the Bank of England.
