Minister of Agriculture urges National Aquaculture Research and Development Institute to find partners to increase research techniques
(Central): Mr. Veng Sakhon, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, on Friday morning On May 3, 2019, he visited the National Institute of Aquaculture Research and Development of Samdech Techo Hun Sen in Prek Long Village, Roka Khpos Commune, Saang District, Kandal Province.
On this occasion, the President of the Institute informed him that the Institute was established in 2013 on an area of 30 hectares, divided into administrative buildings, ponds, breeding ponds, reservoirs, hatching buildings, residential buildings and laboratories. The institute has three main responsibilities: first: to purify, breed and preserve endangered fish species; second: to study, breed and disseminate, and thirdly, to provide technical training to farmers, officials and students.
The president of the institute added that he is currently conducting research on breeding fish, which is divided into production fish such as squid, catfish, kanthor, kae, squid, big head, tilapia and research fish such as clams, elephant ears and squid.
After inspecting the institute, the Minister praised and appreciated the leaders and officials who worked hard in a responsible spirit to pay attention to study, research and development of the institute to be worthy of the name. National Institute of Aquaculture Research and Development Samdech Techo Hun Sen.
At the same time, the Minister also instructed the management and officials of the institute, he asked the institute to think about trade, that is, breeding, breeding and doing business to create a source of income to meet the needs of the institute. For the Institute to develop sustainably and sustainably, especially to improve the living standards of the Institute staff.
He said that it is good to find a partner with a private company or a fish farm to cooperate as a supplier of fish fry. To enhance the laboratory capacity and increase the research and conservation work, especially the endangered species of fish, and to jointly maintain the entire institute for the benefit of the research work in the field of fisheries and as a valuable state property. Present and future.
Minister Veng Sakhon added that efforts must be made to find partners to help with both budget and technical work of breeding and breeding to increase the level of research techniques in line with regional and global standards to raise, process and export products. Cambodian fish to international markets in the future.
Nearly 400 Homes Destroyed in Banteay Meanchey and Lightning Strikes
(Banteay Meanchey): As of almost 9 pm on May 3, 2019, strong winds destroyed a total of 361 houses in Banteay Meanchey province, in which one person was killed, one injured and two cows were killed by lightning.
According to the same source, Malai district destroyed 172 houses, Mongkul Borei district destroyed 187 houses, lightning killed two cows, Preah Net Preah district killed one person and injured one, and Svay Chek district.
To solve this problem, hundreds of military forces immediately intervened to rescue the people, under the direction of Major General Seng Thearin, Deputy Commander of the 5th Army Division.
(Phnom Penh): The delegation of Cambodian Women's Association for Peace and Development of Phnom Penh Branch led by Mrs. Chea Sina, wife of Mr. Khuong Sreng, Governor of Phnom Penh this morning, May 3, 2019, accompanied by Mrs. Keo Sok Pisey, Deputy Governor of Phnom Penh. Also, members of the Cambodian Women's Association for Peace and Development visited Ms. Tit Sam On, Chief of Sak Sampov Commune, Dangkor District, who is being treated at Calmette Hospital.
Ms. Tith Sam On, Sangkat Chief, is the outstanding Sangkat Chief of the Cambodian People's Party in Phnom Penh, who was elected for four consecutive terms because she is popular and always takes into account the well-being of the local people.
It should be noted that Samdech Techo Hun Sen once praised the heroism of Mrs. Tith Sam On, the chief of Sak Sampov commune, Dangkor district, Phnom Penh, who was popularly elected as the four-term female commune chief.
It should also be noted that 2019 is the 66th anniversary of diplomatic relations between the two countries, Cambodia and Japan, and now Japan has not only an embassy in Phnom Penh, but also a consulate in Siem Reap Angkor.
In 2018, Cambodia received more than 6.2 million international tourists, an increase of 10.7%, including more than 210,000 Japanese tourists, an increase of 3.5%, and in the first two months of 2019, Cambodia received tourists. More than 1.2 million international tourists, including nearly 40,000 Japanese tourists, an increase of 3.1%. Japanese tourists have always been among Cambodia's top 10 tourism markets. This year, Cambodia expects to receive more than 230,000 Japanese tourists.
(Siem Reap): The European Chamber of Commerce in Cambodia seeks cooperation on solid waste and wastewater management at the Angkor resort with the APSARA Authority.
This intention was expressed on the occasion of the European Chamber of Commerce in Cambodia, led by Mr. Giyum Maltaven, Investment Attraction Officer, met with Mr. Hang Pov, Director General of APSARA Authority to learn about solid waste management and wastewater management in Angkor. May 3, 2019.
At this meeting, the European Chamber of Commerce highlighted a number of key tasks, the priority of which is trade promotion, economic studies, and a focus on solid waste management and wastewater management.
In that, APSARA Authority also presented its work related to the management of solid waste (garbage) wastewater in the Angkor area. The two factors that cause garbage are tourists and local people because people do not have a comprehensive understanding of garbage collection, proper hygiene and so on.
In this regard, APSARA Authority also has a number of activities such as education on heritage value, sanitation management around the house and the impact of burning garbage, throwing plastic bags in the open.
In addition, the APSARA Authority also collects garbage, collects dead leaves, kitchen waste to produce compost, in addition to the work that the APSARA Authority provides to Vigreen to clean regularly.
After discussing and understanding each other, the European Chamber of Commerce in Cambodia also expressed its desire to explore the possibility of institutional and institutional cooperation or any private sector to work together in the field of solid waste management and management. Dirty water at Angkor resort.
Rural Development Bank requests Israel to expand drip irrigation technology to Cambodian farmers to increase production and high yields
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Kao Thach, Director General of the Rural Development Bank, requested Israel to expand drip irrigation technology to more farmers, farming communities in Cambodia to increase production and high yields.
During the meeting, Mr. Kao Thach wanted to know about the experience of ATC Israel from Cambodia, which has been present in Cambodia for the past 10 years on the use of drip technology for agriculture on rubber, sugarcane and corn. Trees, etc., which through this technology give farmers a high yield.
Mr. Kao Thach asked to share his experience in farming practices and assistance to smallholder farmers in Israel, focusing on resource management, community mobilization, and the use of seeds and fertilizers by Israeli farmers. Mr. Kao Thach aims to use these experiences to prepare Cambodian farming communities for success.
At the same time, Mr. Kao Thach requested Israel to help expand the technology of the drip irrigation system to more farmers, agricultural communities in Cambodia to increase production and high yields.
Mr. Kao Thach strongly believes that through the presence of the Rural Development Bank, he will work hard to make agriculture in Cambodia move forward to contribute to the Royal Government to improve farmers' livelihoods and expand the rural economy.
(Phnom Penh): At around 7:30 pm on May 3, 2019, the Prosecutor's Office completed the interrogation of the Deputy Director of the Criminal Department of the Ministry of Interior, Duong Nakri Roch, and sent him to the Phnom Penh Municipal Police for further investigation. Go to the judge tomorrow. This is according to a senior official of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court told Fresh News tonight.
