(Preah Vihear): Traders at An Ses Gate on the Cambodian-Thai border in Preah Vihear Province are earning a considerable amount of daily income by selling more than 1 ton of mushrooms every day. Thai for their popular food.
Meanwhile, a Thai man who came to buy vegetables and other goods in Cambodia in the An Se market gate said that the reason they came to buy mushrooms as well as other wild vegetables from traders. Khmer because in Thailand there are not many of these vegetables. On the other hand, in the forest, their land is rich in mines, so no one goes to find these vegetables to sell.
It should be noted that although this An Se Gate has not yet become an international port, the exchange of goods between the two peoples of Cambodia and Thailand takes place daily, but most visitors are on Tuesdays and Thursdays. .
