(Phnom Penh): Mr. Oeur Sothearoth, Director General of the Credit Bureau (CBC), said that he will launch a credit information system for legal entities (companies) early next month. The launch of the Corporate Credit Information System in Cambodia to make it easier for financial institutions to make informed decisions about lending to a company.
Speaking on the program "Latest Developments in Credit Information to Promote the Financial Environment in Cambodia" on the morning of May 3, 2019, Mr. Oeur Sothearoth stated that in the last two years, CBC has implemented the corporate credit information system with With the support of the National Bank of Cambodia, it plans to officially launch the system early next month.
He added that now banks and financial institutions that provide credit to companies can know the background of those companies, which companies have borrowed money from which banks? How to repay? All of this information will be available in the corporate credit system, which helps financial institutions make informed credit decisions to companies.
He said that all banks with corporate credit are users of the corporate credit information system, with more than 50 banks needing to use the system.
He said that in addition, the CBC will tell the actual credit history of the company. He said, for example, that if the company had a history of receiving credit with five banking institutions, the information system will show the history of these five institutions, how much they borrowed? And what about the company's payback? "The above is the point that all banks want to achieve their credit," he said.
Mr. In Channy, President of the Banking Association of Cambodia (ABC), expressed his support for the establishment of this corporate credit information system. He said that this arrangement really provides convenience to both partners. By facilitating the lender before lending to check all the information. Banks and MFIs find it easier and less time consuming to find information about individual companies.
Ms. Chea Serey, Head of Credit Bureau (CBC), said, “The Credit Bureau of Cambodia just announced the launch of the Corporate Credit Information System in December 2018. "Once the corporate credit information is fully operational, it will help financial institutions and stakeholders access credit information of all legal entities applying for commercial loans in this market."
She added that corporate information is important for the central bank to monitor the entire market to maintain financial stability.
He added that the IFC will work with Cambodian partners to further strengthen the country's financial infrastructure. An efficient real estate financial system, a comprehensive credit information system and an effective bankruptcy regime are essential to promote private sector development and enhance the competitiveness of the Cambodian economy.
