(Siem Reap): Eighty-five Angkor families received permission to renovate their homes by the APSARA Authority during April 2019.
Types of renovations include: repairing or replacing roofs, repairing walls, replacing pillars, replacing stairs, eaves, floors, building toilets, chicken coops, pouring soil, cowsheds, pig pens, etc. and other necessities in daily life.
Out of 85 families who received permission, Prasat Bakong district received 6 permits, Angkor Thom district received 5 permits, Puok district received 7 permits, and Siem Reap received 52 permits. And Banteay Srei district received permission from 15 families.
