Samsung changes the packaging and many parts of every product for the environment!
(Phnom Penh): According to Samsung's announcement on the impact of plastic waste on the environment, we observe that many parts of the product, as well as all packaging, have reduced the use of plastic.
However, by mid-2019, all Samsung products and accessories, such as smartphones, chargers, tablets and all-plastic home appliances, will be replaced by environmentally friendly materials. To the environment and the earth.
With this commitment as well as environmental protection principles, Samsung plans to recycle 500,000 tons of plastic waste by 2030 and collect more than 7.5 million tons of discarded plastic products for production and reuse. .
All of these are the most special points that make all of Samsung products get a lot of praise and love around the world, the company not only focuses on quality and meet the needs of customers, but the company also takes into account The health of all its users, as well as the utmost care for the environment.
Preah Sihanouk Provincial Hospital announces search for relatives of two women who died in a traffic accident
Preah Sihanouk: The director of Preah Sihanouk Provincial Referral Hospital, Dr. Seng Nong, announced the search for the relatives of the bodies of two women who died in a traffic accident on the night of May 2, 2019 in Sihanoukville.
According to the director of the Sihanoukville Provincial Referral Hospital, the bodies of the two women were taken by private ambulances to the Sihanoukville Provincial Referral Hospital or Chamkar Chek Hospital.
Dr. Seng Nong confirmed that as of May 3, the bodies of the two young women have not been accepted by relatives for the ceremony. Therefore, he announced to inform the missing people in the family to hurry to contact to check the bodies of the two women as soon as possible because the bodies were kept at Sihanoukville Provincial Hospital.
