Minister Khieu Kanharith emphasized that the dissemination of false information harms the reputation of professional journalists and destroys society as a whole, so it is the duty of journalists to tell the truth in order to dispel all false information. Injustice.
Minister Khieu Kanharith stated, "I urge the national and international journalists to continue their efforts to combat counterfeiting by releasing factual information in order to neutralize the misrepresentation and loss of professional journalism." "Support from the public as well as chaos in society."
In addition, the Minister of Information called on national and international journalists to continue their efforts to work in accordance with the code of professional ethics, maintain dignity and strive to develop their capacity to keep pace with the development of digital technology today and avoid Committing illegal acts that affect the value of the press, such as taking this role to prevent illegal activities.
Please be informed that Samdech Techo Hun Sen issued a three-page message to celebrate the 26th World Press Freedom Day under the theme "The Potential Role of Journalists in Supporting Peace and Democracy".
In this message, Samdech Techo Prime Minister highlighted the importance of journalists in the cause of society and also called on journalists to work together professionally to contribute to building and developing a better society.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also reminded all journalists to be honest in their profession, brave to speak the truth, criticize in a constructive way and to be a mirror of social reality to help build social justice, maintain peace and develop the nation.
(Battambang): 100 Million Riels of Carabao Energy Drink continues to fall into the hands of another teacher in Battambang province, 33-year-old Tham Sinuon, a teacher at Stung Touch Krom Primary School, Samlot District, Battambang Province. .
In front of the team and company representatives to hand over 100 million Riel, Mr. Tham Sinuon said that he currently has a job as a teacher in Samlot district, Battambang province, but during the traditional Khmer New Year, he came Visiting his hometown in Prey Phav village, Ronam commune, Traing district, Takeo province, and buying carabao from a vendor's house near his house to eat.
He added that today, in terms of family living standards, it is quite difficult because there is no occupation other than having a career as a teacher, and the other hand is disabled. For winning this prize, it is very coincidental, just seeing the prize, he was very excited and shouted to the neighbors to help check and call the company through the number on the earring. .
He said that after receiving the big prize of 100 million riels, he will use some to build debt and buy land to build a house and leave some to support the family life in the future.
Please note: For the real prize, only on the can with the Khmer letters as the mark.
