(Kampong Cham): After last night's strong wind, causing a school building to collapse completely at Prakhnor Primary School, Sramor Commune, Cheung Prey District, Kampong Cham Province, immediately on May 3, 2019, Dr. Ma Chhoeun represented The people of Kampong Cham district and the head of the middle level working group visited Cheung Prey district to inspect immediately and decided to help build a new school building made of stone and tile with 4 rooms immediately.
During the visit to inspect the dilapidated condition of the school building which was attacked by the natural phenomenon, Dr. Ma Chhoeun expressed his regret for the damage to the school building, which caused the lack of education of the students.
At the same time, the deputies of Kampong Cham district advised the school management, teachers and students to be careful if there is rain, thunder or wind like last night, especially when students are studying to bring students. Leave the risk area to a safe place to prevent any accident.
Meanwhile, Mr. Seang Sorn, Acting Director of Prakhnor Primary School, said that at 7:20 pm on May 2, there was a thunderstorm and strong wind that destroyed a wooden school building. 4 rooms built during 1997.
He said that before this school has two school buildings that facilitate the learning of students once a day. But after the building became too dilapidated, the school management decided to suspend teaching at the building for about three years. Today, the school has only one school building with 6 classrooms, which is not suitable for the number of students, which is close to 300 students.
Mr. Sieng Sorn, on behalf of the teachers and students, thanked Dr. Ma Chhoeun, an MP who always connects with the people in all circumstances, especially when people are in trouble. Always visit and help solve people's difficulties.
Especially today, after receiving the news that the storm destroyed a school building, Dr. Ma Chhoeun came to the site to inquire about the situation of the disaster and helped build a new building. Renovation of 1 room with 4 rooms to facilitate students' learning so that they do not face any more difficulties.
