Senior CamControl official calls for filing a lawsuit if any vendor is found to be using banned chemicals or overdosing on goods
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Phan Oun, Deputy Director General of CamControl, called on people to file a complaint if they see any vendors using banned chemicals or using excessive amounts of chemicals to maintain the quality of goods for a long time.
On the occasion of the press conference of the Royal Government of Cambodia held a press conference on "food and chemicals" at the Council of Ministers yesterday, Mr. Phan Oun said that some chemicals are allowed to be used to protect food products, but also Some harmful chemicals are strictly prohibited by the Royal Government as well as the Royal Government.
Mr. Phan Oun stated, "I would like to take this opportunity to call on all business people to make a list to report to the relevant authorities." For example, if there is a stall containing chemicals, you can file a complaint by car through the contact number of the General Department of CamControl or the contact number of the relevant ministries and institutions so that the ministries and institutions can take timely action.
A senior official of the General Department of CamControl said that there are many types of food products, including wine, food, vegetables, fruits, except cosmetics or pharmaceutical products. Substances that are not allowed to be used because they accumulate and cause stones to harm the health of consumers, and those substances are also regulated.
According to the Deputy Director General of the General Department of CamControl, some chemicals are allowed to be used, but if any traders use the substance in excess, it is illegal to take action.
"If some people overuse it, it is a problem that we stop, and some people use it to exchange any chemicals that are not allowed, it is a matter of law," he said. The law on safety and quality control is stated in Articles 18 and 19, and there are also penalties for some people stealing unauthorized or overused chemicals. ”
