(Phnom Penh): International digital money transfer service on mobile phones to more than 200 countries has been launched for the first time for more than 1 million customers of Wing Specialized Bank in Cambodia who are using Wing smartphone app through Collaboration between Western Union, a leading global money transfer company, and Wing Specialized Bank (Cambodia) Limited, a leading mobile banking company in Cambodia.
With just two or three clicks on the Wing smartphone app, customers can instantly transfer money via Western Union to their families and loved ones 24 hours a day, 7 days a week to more than 200 countries around the world.
Convenience through the use of a finger is possible for all Wing customers who have the Wing smartphone app in their mobile phone, both national and international staff. Customers have the option of transferring money directly from a bank account or through a digital wallet in the Wing smartphone app, where they can deposit money at more than 6,000 Wing agents to transfer money.
"Our services provide a solution for the movement of money across countries around the world," said Sohinira Jolly, Vice President for South Asia and Indochina, Western Union. "With the expertise in financial services and technology to connect the digital world and the real world of remittances, we are committed to empowering our customers by providing solutions that meet their financial needs."
"Remittances are an important source of income for many families, which is especially true for families living in Cambodia and for immigrants as well as their relatives living abroad," she said. "Connecting customers with their families is key and it is necessary to provide the most convenience for them."
"With the growing popularity of mobile phones and internet usage, we are excited to expand our services with Wing to provide customers with digital money transfer options to make it easier for them," she said. Customers in remittances the way they want and play an important role in their lives and the global economy.
Jojo Malolos, CEO of Wing Specialized Bank, said: “Last year we announced our partnership with Western Union, which allows clients in Cambodia to receive payments through their Wing agents. "Receive money transferred through Western Union as part of the Wing campaign to our world."
"Our commitment to our customers is unwavering and we will not stop there," Malolo said. "We plan to continue to expand and expand our capabilities to provide a more user-friendly experience."
In addition to local and international money transfer services, customers can make other transactions on the Wing smartphone app, including: top up, pay bills, pay online and scan QR codes and more.
Cambodia celebrates 20th anniversary of ASEAN membership
The ceremony was presided over by Mr. Prak Sokhon, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, and was attended by Mr. Hang Chuon Naron, Minister of Education, Youth and Sports, and Mr. Pan Sosak, Minister of Commerce and civil servants. Students participate in large numbers.
On that occasion, Mr. Prak Sokhon congratulated and expressed his great pleasure that Cambodia celebrates the 20th anniversary of ASEAN membership. He also thanked the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports and the Ministry of Commerce for co-organizing this important event.
At the same time, the Deputy Prime Minister reminded that on April 30, 2019, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, sent a message to all compatriots commemorating the history of Cambodia's participation in regional organizations. Important and highlight the meaning as well as the benefits that Cambodia receives in the fields of politics, security, economy, society and culture from this membership.
The Minister of Foreign Affairs added that the celebration will give him the opportunity to deepen his understanding of the reasons for Cambodia's accession to ASEAN, its role, contributions and benefits. Challenges and Perspectives for Cambodia to Become an Equal Active Member of a Community-Centered Community
ASEAN is a regional organization comprising ten member countries of Southeast Asia established to promote intergovernmental cooperation and facilitate integration among all members.
Article 31 of the ASEAN Charter states that "The ASEAN Chairmanship shall be rotated annually in the alphabetical order of the Member States' English name" and that the Member States holding the ASEAN Chairmanship shall chair the ASEAN Summit and Some more meetings. In the past, Cambodia has chaired ASEAN twice, the first time in 2002 and the second time in 2012.
Toilets for residents and traders in Prey Toteung Market were built after the market had no toilets for more than a year
(Kampong Cham): A group of traders from Prey Toteung Market in Prey Chhor District, Kampong Cham Province have built toilets for people and traders in the market to use after the market has not had a toilet for more than a year.
Heng Seng Hour, Chairman of the Prey Toteung Market Traders 'Committee, said that after the Royal Government handed over the market to the traders' group to manage and reorganize the infrastructure, Prey Toteung Market was rehabilitated, such as drains and toilets.
But when the toilets were built for the people and traders in the market, two traders, Sothon and Sineth, objected to the construction of the toilets.
Heng Seng Hour, chairman of the traders' group, confirmed that the site for the toilet was the old one that the market chairman had handed over to the traders before the government handed over the market. But the old toilet, because the director of the market before the construction of the wrong technical standards, caused a bad smell, clogged the sewer and had to be closed for more than a year.
By the time the vendors started rebuilding the toilets at the same spot, the vendors from the stalls had objections, claiming that the canteen was covering their stalls.
The Chairman of the Board of Traders stated that due to the instability of the old water tank poles, the traders set up a new water tank market and the foot of the water tank was placed at the old tank poles, but the side Two vendors objected to the installation of the water tank pole.
Heng Seng Hour said that the district authorities had helped mediate the dispute several times, but the two sides still refused.
However, since this work is in the public interest and the construction of the toilets is mainly on the old site, the market vendors have decided to install the water tank poles have been completed.
