(Ratanakkiri): Mr. Thong Savun, Governor of Ratanakkiri Province, met with officials of the Provincial Information Department and various journalists in Ratanakkiri Province, requesting that journalists strengthen their professional ethics and knowledge in writing news articles. Accurate and reliable.
Speaking on the night of May 2, 2019, the Provincial Governor praised and appreciated the efforts of all officials of the Department of Information and all journalists who have participated in fulfilling their professional roles as reflectors of the social landscape. An indispensable good messenger.
Mr. Thong Savun continued that on the occasion of the 26th World Press Freedom Day on May 3, he would like to join the congratulations with the media and ask all journalists to strengthen the ethics of the journalism profession, strengthen the capacity. Knowledge of writing articles, producing information accurately, with clear and reliable sources based on information sources.
He added that journalists must not trust the source completely, but must be able to check and verify the information provided by the source before publishing and must not spread false information that can cause social problems, defamation or insult. A competent person is an agent to any person on the basis of factual and accurate and useful information.
The provincial governor further stated that journalists must work together to fight fake news by releasing true information in accordance with the high recommendation of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of the Kingdom of Cambodia.
79-year-old man dies in the middle of a rice field after being dragged by a buffalo in Chey Sen district, Preah Vihear province
(Preah Vihear): An old man lost his life in the middle of a rice field when a buffalo dragged him several meters.
This incident happened on the afternoon of May 2, 2019 at the point of Don Nha rice, 1 km away from Men Reach village in Khyang village, Chey Sen district, Preah Vihear province.
Colonel Tiem Sangkram, Chey Sen District Police Inspector, said this morning, May 3, 2019, that before the incident, the victim drank alcohol and went to herd buffalo at the scene with a handcuff. As usual. But when the buffalo was startled, he ran and dragged the victim back to Trolin, causing his death.
