Ministry of Information Celebrates World Press Freedom Day 2019 on "Potential Role of the Press in Supporting Peace and Democracy"
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Information in collaboration with USAID Cambodia this morning, May 3, 2019, organized the celebration of World Press Freedom Day 2019 under the theme "The Potential Role of the Press in Supporting Peace and Democracy". .
It should be informed that on the occasion of the 26th World Press Freedom Day, May 3, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, reminded all journalists to be honest, professional, brave, dare to speak the truth, criticize in a constructive and correct way. Be a mirror of social reality to help build social justice, maintain peace and develop the nation.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also urged the journalists to continue their efforts to develop their ability to analyze the situation in both national and international events in depth to keep up with the situation in the country in the region and around the world. Currently.
False information is one of the world's most pressing topics in the digital age. Samdech Techo Hun Sen also called on journalists to fight against false information caused by unscrupulous people in order to serve their greedy ambitions that are threatening peace, democracy and development in the whole world.
