In a message celebrating the World Press Freedom Day, Samdech Techo, the head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, said that the opening up of press freedom in Cambodia has led to the rapid growth of the media sector in print, electronic and online media. With different trends in line with the current political situation and the development of modern technology that can quickly disseminate and share information around the world.
In a democratic society, the press is considered the fourth power that has contributed significantly to the strengthening of democracy, respect for human rights and the strengthening of social justice. Samdech Techo Hun Sen reminded the media that in order for the media to have the potential to support peace and democracy, it is necessary for the journalists to work hard to develop their capacity and be honest in their profession and dare to tell the truth.
Two ringleaders convicted of illegally occupying state land sentenced to 18 months in prison
(Preah Sihanouk): Two people accused of masterminding the illegal occupation of state land in the multi-use area of Prek Teuk Sap Kbal Chhay in Preah Sihanouk Province have been found guilty by the Preah Sihanouk Provincial Court. The charges will be handed down to 18 months in prison on the afternoon of May 2, 2019, after a full day of trial.
The two defendants, Chhay Rath and Tep Sopha, were arrested and charged in a criminal case on January 21, 2019, after committing the crime of illegally occupying state land and inciting people. Citizens obstruct law enforcement forces in the multi-use area of Prek Teuk Sap, Kbal Chhay, in Group 18, Village 1, Sangkat 1, Preah Sihanouk Province.
Secretary of State and spokesman for the Ministry of Environment, Mr. Neth Pheaktra, welcomed the decision of the Sihanoukville Provincial Court, stating that this is a practical measure for the mastermind who always uses the theory of winning land, losing money in land grabbing. State forest or land illegally owned.
Secretary of State for the Ministry of Environment Net Pheaktra said that some individuals have used the land use application documents that have already been annulled by the Royal Government as an excuse for clearing, burning, encroaching on state land and forest land in the area. Protect nature and on the legal land location of development investment companies authorized by the Royal Government in principle.
Meanwhile, Secretary of State for the Ministry of Environment, Mr. Net Pheaktra, called on innocent people not to be deceived by corrupt brokers and not to engage in illegal activities that lead to legal confrontation because no one can take state land. Can't go shopping. The Secretary of State reminded the people that before buying or selling land, be careful not to touch the state land or land with the correct title, which will lead to the loss of benefits.
