Ministry of Health launches training on the use of cash support program for poor pregnant women and children under 2 years old
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of April 2, 2019, the Ministry of Health organized a training program on the use of cash support programs for poor pregnant women and children under 2 years old under the chairmanship of Dr. Yok Sambath, Secretary of State, on behalf of Dr. Mam. Bun Heng, Minister of Health.
Speaking on the occasion, Ms. Youk Sambath confirmed that the head of the Royal Government of Cambodia under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen has decided to provide cash to poor women, pregnant women and children under 2 years, for a total of 1,000 days. Must be transferred to a poor woman equal to 760,000 Riels.
According to the Secretary of State, the conditions for this payment are divided into three stages, including: Stage 1: 4 regular pregnancy check-ups during pregnancy (40,000 Riels each time), Stage 2: At the time of delivery, receive a one-time allowance of 200,000 Riel and the third stage: 4 postpartum check-ups for mothers and babies, and 4 more periodic check-ups for children (40,000 Riel at a time).
Ms. Youk Sambath emphasized that in order to make the implementation work, the Ministry will create an app system that can be installed with smart phones and computers that can create and determine the level of use and number of users, input information, recording service recipients. Data Entry Payment data to the cash flow system and report generation.
At the same time, Mr. Sok Sam Ang, Director General of Administration and Finance of the Ministry of Health, said that the creation of this App is to facilitate the difficulties of all local hospital units that meet and examine women directly. Poor pregnant. In addition, the ministry also facilitates data management for poor pregnant women who need to be funded.
