Residents reported that the use of explosives and the chemical potassium yanay for gold mining and processing in Kampong Thom province was reported to be seriously polluting the environment. In particular, forest water resources can lead to the death of people if this chemical flows into the water and people use that water.
Residents also claim that the illegal gold mining business in Sok Chet commune, Sandan district, Kampong Thom province, has been destroying many gold mines from Cambodia. In addition, the business has left behind the devastating effects of natural resources, including deforestation, water pollution and fisheries through the use of chemicals.
The people requested the Ministry of Mines and Energy and relevant authorities to inspect and crack down on illegal gold mining sites in their localities quickly and effectively before the devastation is bigger and more serious than now. .
Regarding this issue, Mr. Yos Monirath confirmed that all those activities are old activities and the Ministry officials with local authorities and law enforcement forces have been cracking down since the end of March and until now there are no more activities.
