(Stung Treng): The Stung Treng Provincial Gendarmerie arrested two Vietnamese nationals after stealing and fishing in the restricted area of the Lower Sesan 2 sluice gate, Phluk village, Phluk commune, Sesan district, Stung Treng province.
The Commander of Stung Treng Provincial Gendarmerie, Brigadier General Ieng Vandy, told Fresh News on the afternoon of May 1, 2019 that the suspect was arrested by the Provincial Gendarmerie in cooperation with the Sesan District Local Forces on the night of May 1, 2019. April 29, 2019 by the first suspect: Chang Yang Hom, alias Yu, 29 years old, and the second suspect: Chang Yang Phi, 22 years old.
In this operation, the Provincial Armed Forces confiscated 400 meters of nets, 7 meters deep, 12 centimeters square, 72 wire ropes, and 20 nets.
The commander confirmed that prior to the incident, two military forces, in cooperation with the Fisheries Administration and boat security patrol, found a group of fishermen with two boats floating when they saw the police drive the boat to escape. Authorities then confiscated the artifact, placed it in a boat and parked it near the dam.
It was not until the morning that it was discovered that the boat and the exhibits were missing, then an investigation was launched to obtain the above results, but the boat of the military police has not been found yet. According to the confession, the suspect actually came to steal the exhibits and hid them at the port in front of their house. As for the police boat, they sank it at the point where the water was very turbulent (currently not yet found).
Presently, the exhibits and the suspects are being detained and kept in the unit for the Office of Case Management to send to the court according to the procedure. Stung Treng Provincial Armed Forces Arrest 6 Vietnamese Nationals for Stealing Fishing in the Prohibited Area at Lower Sesan 2 Hydropower and Involved in Illegal Use of Weapons
