NEC: Khmer Identity Card, Type 2, 3 or Identity Document as the only document to be used for 2019 voter registration
(Phnom Penh): The National Election Committee (NEC) has stated that the second type of valid Khmer identity card or the third type of Khmer identity card or identification document for voter registration is a document. The only one that Cambodians of both sexes must use for the 2019 voter registration.
This was stated by Mr. Hal Sarath, Member of the NEC and Chairman of the meeting with stakeholders on "Commencement of the voter list and voter registration in the commune / sangkat and the voter registration procedure in the commune. Sangkat and the transmission of data to the NEC "at the NEC press conference hall this morning, April 30, 2019 yesterday.
Stakeholders attending the meeting included representatives of the Constitutional Council, the Senate, the Ministry of Interior, the Ministry of Information, nine political parties, nine non-governmental organizations, seven media units and a total of 50 NEC officials.
Pursuant to Article 51 of the Law on the Election of Members of the National Assembly, Commune / Sangkat authorities have the right to issue identification documents for voter registration to citizens who do not yet have a Khmer Nationality ID card or their Khmer Nationality ID card is damaged or Missing upon request to meet the conditions for voter registration.
He added that the procedure for requesting and issuing identification documents for voter registration must be implemented in accordance with Joint Instruction No. 018, dated July 11, 2016 between the Ministry of Interior and the NEC.
