(Phnom Penh): On the morning of May 1, 2019, a shocking case occurred when a Chinese man carrying a bag with a improvised explosive device entered a Chinese shop selling pearl brand "He He »In front of Canadia Market, Street 3, Group 3, Trapeang Thleung 1 Village, Sangkat Choam Chao 1, Khan Por Sen Chey.
Seeing this situation, the owner of the above location shouted and reported to the Po Sen Chey District Police Force, and the District Inspector, Colonel Yim Saran, led the force to intervene and arrest the suspect, 39-year-old Liu Jin, along with exhibits to The CMAC unit inspected immediately.
Phnom Penh Municipal Police Commissioner General 3-Star Sar Thet told Fresh News that the improvised explosive device (IED) that police cracked down on a Chinese man in Por Sen Chey district was an unexploded ordnance because there was no explosive device. There was only sand in the pipe, not ammunition.
The General Commissioner said that according to the inspection of CMAC officials, it was shown that the type of improvised explosive device could not explode, so it did not cause any danger.
After the inspection, CMAC officials concluded that it was not an explosive device, but that the suspect had prepared it like an explosive device to intimidate others, just like the suspect's answer. Currently, the above exhibits are kept by the police force, while the suspect is temporarily detained at the Criminal Division of the Police Inspectorate of Po Sen Chey District, waiting to continue the procedure.
Kampong Cham Provincial Prosecutor Denies Allegations That Authorities tortured a detainee to death, in fact, he rented a bathroom by himself
(Kampong Cham): Kampong Cham Provincial Prosecutor Huot Wutty on May 1, 2019, came out and completely denied the accusation that the police tortured a detainee to death in his cell, but passed Carefully researched and investigated Tit Ron by renting a bathroom and committing suicide.
He said that after a thorough investigation, the police found that Tith Ron was arrested for intentionally causing injuries in Wat village, Tuol Preah Khleang commune, Stung Trang district, Kampong Cham province on November 1. In 2006, he was temporarily detained at the Kampong Cham Provincial Police in the same room with two other suspects.
On April 17, 2019, Tith Ron walked into the bathroom of the temporary detention building, his hands and feet shaking like an alcoholic, causing him to fall and hit the corner of the pool, causing injuries. The right eyelid is bleeding profusely. Until April 18, the detainee died in the health post of Kampong Cham Provincial Prison.
(Phnom Penh): The National Police Commissioner's Office in Phnom Penh on the night of April 30, 2019, cracked down on one of the three suspects who committed motorcycle theft. The victim was in front of a clothing store at 147A, Street 156, Group 5, Village 2, Sangkat Teuk Laak II, Khan Toul Kork.
According to the report of Major General Horm Taing Hoeut, Deputy Director of the Criminal Police Department and Chief of Target Sub-District, Tuol Kork District, the suspect who was apprehended by the police force, named Son Piseth, 18 years old, false occupation, living in a rented house. Street number, Sangkat Toul Tum Poung I, Khan Chamkarmon, Phnom Penh. During the arrest, the police took the suspect's urine and tested it for drugs.
Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany calls on all pregnant women to come for regular health check-ups by professional midwives during pregnancy and after childbirth
Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany stated, "I would like to take this opportunity to call on all women to come and receive regular check-ups from midwives during pregnancy, childbirth and postpartum period." Make an appointment to get better health for both mother and baby. "Give birth control from one child to the next for three years and get all babies and young children vaccinated on time."
At the same time, Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany would like to call on all relevant institutions, national and international organizations to support and invest continuously and regularly on key interventions in the field of midwifery work, because midwives are defenders of women's rights, midwives are protectors. Health and Reproductive Rights Only midwives can help all mothers, babies and children receive care, support and life-saving services during pregnancy, childbirth and postpartum.
Samdech Kittipritthbandit strongly believes that under the wise and wise leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, the Royal Government of Cambodia will continue to provide opportunities to promote employment in the health sector, especially maternal, infant and child health. Succeeded in covering global health services.
Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen also recommended that the professional midwives strive to increase their understanding and experience to provide quality health services with high responsibility, virtue and equity to cooperate to For the benefit of women-infants-children and to promote the midwifery profession in order to achieve new successes for the motherland.
Samdech Kittipritthbandit emphasized that in 2019, the Royal Government has focused on maternal, infant and child health, especially the expansion and implementation of social protection policies have made Cambodia brighter and the National Midwifery Day on May 5 more meaningful. More deep. More than 100 Defenders Receive New Uniforms from Kampong Thom Provincial Governor
