Aung San Suu Kyi arrives in Siem Reap to visit Angkor Khmer temple
(Phnom Penh): At 10:00 am on May 1, 2019, Ms. Aung San Suu Kyi, State Councilor of the Union of Myanmar, arrived in Siem Reap to visit the Angkor Khmer Temple before concluding her three-day visit to Cambodia. .
Please be informed that Ms. Aung San Suu Kyi led the delegation to Cambodia at 3:50 pm on April 29, 2019 for a three-day visit at the invitation of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
Last night, she will also attend a reception hosted by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
(Phnom Penh): A suspect involved in a case of drug trafficking about 2 kg per day was sent to the Phnom Penh Municipal Court this morning, May 1, 2019 for questioning. The suspect is named Tang Srun, male, 36 years old.
On his way to court, he was questioned by Deputy Prosecutor Kuch Kimlong of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court before being charged and sent to an investigating judge for further proceedings.
According to authorities, the suspect claimed that he sold about 2 kg of drugs per day and was arrested by the Anti-Drug Department (A11) on April 25, 2019.
