On April 30, 2019, Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth, Minister of Economy and Finance, and Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, accompanied by the Governor of Preah Sihanouk Province, Mr. Yon Min, and many other officials. Joint inspection and study at the location of the wastewater treatment plant in Sihanoukville, Preah Sihanouk Province.
The visit to the location of the water treatment plant is to examine and study to find ways to increase the capacity of the wastewater treatment plant in Sihanoukville to have a higher capacity and receive more water.
According to Mr. Sun Chanthol, the current wastewater treatment plant has a filtration capacity of only 5,000 cubic meters, while transporting wastewater from homes, restaurants and hotels is up to 25,000 cubic meters. One day.
Mr. Sun Chanthol claimed that in order to filter the wastewater that is growing rapidly, the Ministry has studied to build more wastewater treatment plants, which aims to make the wastewater treatment plant with a capacity of 60,000 cubic meters. One day.
The senior minister pointed out that both the construction of a new water treatment plant as well as the installation of a total sewer system with a total length of 157 km will require about 200 million US dollars.
The issue of sewage into the sea in Sihanoukville is a concern of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia. During the Sea Festival in Koh Kong province at the end of 2018, Samdech Techo Hun Sen confirmed the Coastal Management Committee, chaired by Deputy Prime Minister Chea Sophara, Minister of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction, together with relevant authorities, to eliminate sewage. In the sea.
Following the order of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Deputy Prime Minister Chea Sophara led the construction of four wastewater treatment plants on beaches in Sihanoukville to intercept and pump wastewater from homes, restaurants and hotels into wastewater treatment plants. Large.
The four wastewater treatment plants have already been built and have also helped prevent more wastewater from entering the sea.
(World): On Tuesday, April 30, 2019, many important international events took place, including many interesting political events and global situations. So, if you want to know what these daily photo events are, please visit the following:
Iran considers all US troops in the Middle East "terrorists" (Video inside) (Tehran): Iranian President Hassan Rouhani on Tuesday signed a draft law to make it official. All US troops in the Middle East are considered terrorists, as well as the US government itself as a state sponsor of terrorism. This was released by Reuters on Tuesday, April 30, 2019.
The bill was passed by the Iranian parliament last week in retaliation for US President Donald Trump's decision to designate Iran's Revolutionary Guards as a terrorist organization. But at the same time, it is not yet known to what extent Iran's new law will affect US operations and troops stationed in the Middle East.
Iran's new law also lists the US Central Command (CENTCOM), which is responsible for military operations in Afghanistan and the Middle East, as a terrorist organization.
