Venezuelan opposition leader calls on rebel forces to oust Maduro in video with military
Opposition leader Juan Guaido, who has announced his candidacy for the presidency of Venezuela with the full support of the United States, said on Tuesday he had begun implementing the final phase of plans to oust incumbent Nicolas Sarkozy. Maduro has resigned, calling on the Venezuelan military and people to support him. This was released by Reuters on Tuesday, April 30, 2019.
Speaking in the video, Guaido said: "The army will make the right decision against President Nicolas Maduro ... and I also call on the people to protest and "We want the army to join us against the government."
