Deputy Prime Minister Men Sam An said that Sihanoukville is an important destination for investors of all nationalities.
(Preah Sihanouk): Speaking on the occasion of the inauguration of Tongyuan International Hotel on April 30, 2019, Deputy Prime Minister Men Sam An said that Sihanoukville is an important destination for investors after the opening of the market and welcome. Foreign investment, especially from China, has greatly improved Sihanoukville, especially in the tourism industry.
He pointed out that the Royal Government of Cambodia, through the Rectangular Strategy Phase 4, has considered the private sector as the engine of development and has facilitated and encouraged the private sector to grow to contribute to socio-economic development. She commended Tongyuan for making the right decision to invest in the development of tourism and entertainment services in Sihanoukville.
Deputy Prime Minister Men Sam An strongly believes that the success of the company's services has really contributed to the stability and growth of the Cambodian economy by providing income and employment opportunities to the people, which is a necessary factor in reducing poverty. In addition, it also contributes to the development of Sihanoukville and reduce the migration of people.
She reminded the service owner to provide quality and reasonable service that is acceptable with a long-term interest and do not tarnish the reputation, that is, if the customer comes once and let them go back. By bringing satisfaction and good memories and wish to come again or help spread the word to friends and relatives to visit and stay again.
At the same time, she reminded the leaders of Sihanoukville to continue to pay more attention to security, public order, sanitation and urban beauty to build investor confidence.
At the same time, Mr. Yon Min, Governor of Preah Sihanouk Province, congratulated and supported the Tong Yian International Hotel Investment Company, which was inaugurated today. On behalf of the Sihanoukville Provincial Administration, we welcome and support all investors who have invested in the territory of Sihanoukville, and the province guarantees the safety, security and protection of the assets of companies based on the law.
(Preah Sihanouk): Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, asked all hotel and guesthouse owners in Sihanoukville not to drain sewage into the sea, as it could damage the marine environment and damage it. Damage to the coastal environment.
He urged the business owners to cooperate with the wastewater treatment officials by first draining the wastewater into the wastewater treatment plant before discharging it into the sea, even if it is not 100% neutral.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol said this on the afternoon of April 30, 2019, on the occasion that he accompanied Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth, Minister of Economy and Finance, to inspect the wastewater treatment plant in Sihanoukville.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol also stated that the Ministry of Public Works also accepted responsibility for not preparing the master plan closely, thinking that the 5,700 cubic meters could be sustained only because Cambodia is peaceful and politically stable. Only a lot of people come to invest and a lot of tourists, so the demand for water consumption has increased significantly beyond expectations, so the filtration of wastewater is not yet like this.
The senior minister added that he would take the example of the Sihanoukville master plan to be implemented in other provinces to prevent environmental damage because we did not think about the filtration of wastewater by the country. There is progress and the rate of water use is also high, so we must think about this wastewater treatment to avoid damage to the environment.
According to residents of Sihanoukville, in the last three years, used water in guesthouses, hotels and restaurants has been pumped into the sea through some natural streams in Sihanoukville. This case has caused serious impact on both the environment and the surrounding biodiversity. The seawater turned black after the waste and sewage were used up and dumped into the sea.
"International Labor Day, May 1" This morning, Samdech Techo Hun Sen had a solidarity meal and dancing with nearly 4,000 workers of Yida factory
(Phnom Penh): On the occasion of the 133rd Anniversary of International Labor Day, May 1, this morning, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, went to enjoy solidarity food and dance with about 3,700 workers at Yida factory. Located in Russey village, Chheu Teal commune, Kien Svay district, Kandal province.
In addition to fresh food and dancing, Samdech Techo Hun Sen will also provide financial support to pregnant workers.
Yida factory started operating in 2015 and has a total of 3,700 workers, including 2,803 women. Products made at Yida are exported to Europe and the United States.
The factory pays about 866,570 US dollars a month in wages and allowances to workers. The average wage for each worker ranges from $ 220 to $ 280 per month.
In addition to the benefits set by law, the factory also offers a number of other benefits. Those benefits include:
* Bonus for multi-skilled workers, machines for sewing team captains, seamstresses, seamstresses, quality inspectors and more, calculated based on total monthly percentage, salary, role, working hours and other factors.
Please note that International Labor Day is a holiday celebrated by more than 80 countries around the world in order to commemorate and dedicate the heroic deeds of workers who have worked hard and changed their lives for work. All workers' rights.
Cambodia, after being liberated from the genocidal regime and seeking full peace in late 1998, also regularly celebrates International Labor Day on May 1 to promote workers' labor rights.
In order to encourage workers, which is an important driving force in promoting Cambodia's industrial sector, Samdech Techo Hun Sen in the last two years, from August 20, 2017 to the 28th In March 2019, there were 66 meetings with workers, with a total of nearly 950,000 workers participating in this conversation.
Through a series of meetings with workers, Samdech Techo Hun Sen has solved many of the challenges of workers and brought many benefits to ensure workers' rights and improve their lives.
Through the above activities, it is seen as a high attention of the Head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, on the labor rights and livelihoods of workers and also to promote the industrial sector as a driving force. Cambodia's economy is important.
It should be noted that in 2018, on the occasion of International Labor Day, May 1, Samdech Techo Hun Sen invited workers to eat solidarity and dance with workers in the Phnom Penh Special Economic Zone. Cambodian, Thai drug officials urge specialized units to continue importing and exporting chemicals that could effectively divert drug production
(Phnom Penh): Recently, after a group of unscrupulous people used tricks to import some chemicals from neighboring countries to be used to divert and synthesize drugs, Cambodian-Thai drug officials urged the Ministry. The authorities must continue to pay attention to inspect all import, export, use and storage of chemical compounds of all private enterprises to be more efficient.
Such a push by Lt. Gen. Lay Kimly, Director of the Cabinet, Deputy Prime Minister Ke Kim Yan and Deputy Secretary General of the National Authority for Combating Drugs and Mr. Jarae Pokpa, Senior Officer in Charge of Drug Control of the Thai Embassy in Cambodia in the evening. On April 30, 2019, at the closing ceremony of the training course on "Drug and Chemical Control" at the Cambodiana Hotel, Phnom Penh.
On that occasion, Lt. Gen. Lay Kimly stated that Cambodia is not a country that produces drugs, but a country that suffers from the effects of smuggling, transit and processing of illegal drugs by criminals, as well as Diversion of chemicals from the legal trade to the illegal synthesis, processing and production of illegal drugs.
In addition, the lieutenant general also requested the customs authorities in charge of the first inspection at the gate to focus on the inspection of all documents related to the application of the enterprise issued by the relevant ministries, including the Ministry. The Ministry of Industry and Handicrafts and the Ministry of Health, in order to verify the legality of the import of all those chemicals into Cambodia.
"Without chemicals, there would be no drugs," said Jared Pokpa. Therefore, all specialized units must continue to cooperate more effectively on the import, export and use of certain chemicals that can be diverted and synthesized into illegal drugs at their respective target points. More.
