(Phnom Penh): The General Commission of the National Police, through the Department of Private Security Management as a staff, has confirmed that Cambodia does not allow foreigners to work as private security agents and will immediately stop their activities.
Lt. Gen. Lim Sokharasmey, Director of the Private Security Management Department, on the evening of April 30, 2019, at the Closing Ceremony of the 15th Private Security Agency Training Course, said that Cambodia has a large workforce, so there is no reason to allow it. Foreigners are recruited to work as security agents, which is not allowed under Cambodian law.
Lt. Gen. Lim Sokharasmey said, "Cambodia does not allow any enterprise or company that recruits foreigners to work as a private security agent, and if this happens, it must report to the Department of Private Security Management." "Urgent to take legal action."
He added that private security companies must first obtain permission from the relevant authorities or authorities before starting a business, otherwise they will be held accountable before the law or will be penalized accordingly. Determined by applicable law.
Please be informed that the statement of the Director of the Department of Private Security Management came after it was found that the owner of a hotel and casino in Sihanoukville had recruited a foreign security guard without any rules and was summoned by the competent force. Location to make a contract, stop activities immediately.
However, Lt. Gen. Lim Sokharaksmey stated that private security agencies are an important support force of the authorities and not only have the role of protecting private property or enterprises, but also protecting public property, social security and life. Of the people, and especially the cooperation to prevent and suppress crimes and the dissemination of safe village-commune policies.
Mr. Lim Sokharasmey also explained that the word "auxiliary force" is to remember that it is not the authority, so do not do anything beyond its role and facilitate cooperation with the authorities at all times, and he claimed that any obstruction One or the performance of duties beyond one's duties may result in another offense.
The Director of the Private Security Management Department also encourages all private security agencies to report to the local authorities any incidents that occur at the target they are guarding and all information will be kept confidential and provided. Incentives as well.
Aung San Suu Kyi Meets King and Queen Mother
Aung San Suu Kyi led a delegation to Cambodia at 3:50 pm on April 29, 2019 for a three-day visit at the invitation of the Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen Holds a Dinner Ceremony for Ms. Aung San Suu Kyi and Delegates
(Phnom Penh): After a full day visit to Cambodia on the night of April 30, 2019, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, organized a dinner with many delicious food for Ms. Ong. San Suu Kyi, State Councilor of the Union of Myanmar and Delegation.
The dinner was also attended by many senior officials of the Royal Government of Cambodia in a pleasant and happy atmosphere.
It should be noted that Ms. Aung San Suu Kyi arrived in Cambodia on the afternoon of April 29, 2019 to pay her first official visit to Cambodia at the invitation of Samdech Techo Hun Sen.
Throughout April 30, she laid a wreath at the Independence Monument and laid a wreath at the coffin of King Norodom Sihanouk.
Afterwards, he met with Samdech Techo Hun Sen, paid a courtesy call on Samdech Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin, President of the National Assembly, paid a courtesy call on Samdech Vibol Sena Pheakdey Say Chhum, President of the Senate, invited To pay homage to the King of Cambodia, His Majesty King Norodom Sihanouk, and the Queen Mother of the Nation, Norodom Monineath Sihanouk, at the Royal Palace.
Angkor Wat, one of Cambodia's most famous treasures, was also the site of Aung San Suu Kyi's heartfelt visit during her first visit to Cambodia. Aung San Suu Kyi will visit the Angkor Wat temples in Siem Reap on May 1, 2019. After visiting Angkor Wat, she will fly from Cambodia to her country on the same day.
The presence of the Nobel Peace Prize winner in Cambodia carries thousands of meanings, and this is certainly not a dream as Sam Rainsy and his opponents have always had. Opposition groups, especially Sam Rainsy and Mu Sochua, took political advantage of Aung San Suu Kyi and sometimes compared her as a pseudo-democrat to Aung San Suu Kyi, who was internationally recognized as a true democrat. .
