(Phnom Penh): Mr. Lim Kean Hor, Minister of Water Resources and Meteorology, on April 30, 2019, chaired a meeting with relevant leaders and officials to discuss the Stung Prek Tnaot flood relief project. This is a follow-up meeting after the technical review meeting in March 2019.
Please be informed that Stung Prek Tnaot water during the rainy season always causes floods which always threaten Kampong Speu, Kandal, Takeo and especially Phnom Penh.
Examining the current state of development and existing infrastructure in Stung Prek Tnaot and after discussing the options for flood relief in Stung Prek Tnaot, the meeting considered that the diversion of water from the upper part is connected to The Slago River and into the Bati River, connected to the Hanuman Canal, is a well-deserved project. In this option, when the flood is large, the maximum water flow is 900 to 1,200 cubic meters per second.
This is an immediate measure and a priority project to be implemented and has immediate support to reduce and avoid serious impacts on the capital-province, both now and in the future.
