(Phnom Penh): Forces of Po Sen Chey District Unity Command led by District Governor Hem Darith raided two massage parlors run by Chinese bosses and had sex services embedded in them. Twelve Chinese men and women, including 10 women suspected of being sex workers and two men, were arrested.
The operation took place on the morning of April 30, 2019 in the massage shop brand "E Hong Yan" in Prey Tea village, Sangkat Choam Chao 3, Khan Por Senchey, Phnom Penh.
Authorities said the two massage parlors were branded in Chinese characters and were run by a 50-year-old Chinese woman named Ping Yi, who did not have the proper permits and rules to operate. Outside, there are labels and pictures of massages, but in fact, it is a place where sexual services are provided.
When they arrived, they found several boxes of unused condoms and some used condoms, and then arrested 12 Chinese men and women, including 10 women. Serve sexual services. The other two men were in charge of the two massage parlors, while the female manager, Ping Yi, escaped.
The 12 people were taken to Por Sen Chey district court, waiting to be handed over to the immigration police for legal action.
