In the first quarter of 2019, officials banned 65 cases of inappropriate behavior in Angkor
(Siem Reap): The misconduct of tourists in the Angkor area is still frequent, according to the report of the activities of the Department of Angkor Tourism Development of the APSARA Authority for the first quarter of 2019 shows that in the first quarter This year, travel agencies have banned 65 cases of misconduct.
These include the launch of a drone, defecation in the temple grounds, alien photography, unauthorized wedding photography, inappropriate gestures (fashion photography, inappropriate photography), inappropriate clothing, and performances. The circus in the temple organizes dinners in the temple, uses large-scale cameras, conducts religious ceremonies without permission, takes photographs, advertisements, and draws large-scale paintings without permission.
At the same time, the team also rescued 113 cases of tourists who were injured by slipping or tripping, stumbling, paralysis, paralysis of the limbs, dizziness, abdominal pain, monkey bites and food poisoning.
These problems were sent to the hospital by the travel agency, which has specialized first aid and first aid equipment on time, in case of minor cases and in cooperation with the tourist police and heritage protection police, to the hospital in case of injuries. Serious.
The travel agency also collected 93 items of forgotten or lost items from the temples, of which 85 items were found, including mobile phones, iPads, backpacks, handbags, wallets, visas and cameras. And found and returned to the original owner. Today is the 20th anniversary of Cambodia becoming a member of ASEAN, so find out a brief history of the association.
(Southeast Asia): The Association of Southeast Asian Nations (ASEAN) is a regional organization of ten member countries in Southeast Asia established to promote intergovernmental cooperation and facilitate Integration among all members.
Taking the opportunity to commemorate the 20th anniversary of Cambodia's accession to ASEAN, April 30, 1999 - April 30, 2019, we would like to present the history of the establishment of this regional organization:
2: ASEAN Secretariat
The ASEAN Secretariat is based in Jakarta, Indonesia, with the Secretary-General in charge of coordinating and implementing ASEAN activities. The Secretary-General, appointed by the ASEAN Summit for a five-year term, shall be rotated according to the alphabetical order of the English names of the Member States. The ASEAN Charter stipulates that the selection of the Secretary-General shall be based on conditions such as integrity, work experience, competence and gender equality.
3: ASEAN Chair
Article 31 of the ASEAN Charter states that "The ASEAN Chairmanship shall be rotated annually in the alphabetical order of the Member States' English name" and that the Member States holding the ASEAN Chairmanship shall chair the ASEAN Summit and Some more meetings. Cambodia has twice chaired ASEAN, the first in 2002 and the second in 2012.
4: The purpose of establishing this association
5: ASEAN Meeting
All important decisions related to the fate of ASEAN are to be made by the ASEAN Summit, which takes place annually in the ASEAN Chairmanship. In addition to the summit, there are other meetings, such as ministerial meetings by sector.
The South China Sea issue has tarnished relations between some ASEAN member states, and this issue has been a hot topic at every ASEAN summit in recent years. However, ASEAN economic integration is still a topic that ASEAN is paying close attention to and is one of the three pillars that has achieved the most.
But for some ASEAN researchers, the dream remains elusive, even as ASEAN reports show that ASEAN has achieved 90% of the goals set out in the three pillars.
Initially, a small organization was formed in 1961 called the Association of Southeast Asian Nations (ASA), a group of participating countries such as the Philippines, Malaysia and Thailand. ASEAN was then established on August 8, 1967, when the foreign ministers of five countries - Indonesia, Malaysia, the Philippines, Singapore and Thailand - signed the ASEAN Treaty, commonly known as the Bangkok Treaty.
(Phnom Penh): More than 400 University of Human Resources students in collaboration with the National Blood Transfusion Center, sponsored by NVC Corporation Vital, participated in a voluntary blood donation program under the theme "Youth, Humanity and Hope" Tuesday, April 30, 2019 at the National University of Human Resources.
The University of Human Resources is one of the leading universities that receives the largest number of blood donors almost every year. This year as well, this blood donation program is expected to receive at least 200 blood donations to supplement any shortage of blood in the reserves across the country.
The purpose of this program is to increase the participation of students in humanitarian activities in society through blood donation, also to support the campaign of the National Blood Transfusion Center, which always pays attention to the elimination. Eliminate the deaths of Cambodians from anemia.
This blood donation program can be celebrated with the full support of Vital Drinking Water Company, which has always supported various humanitarian activities in the society. To encourage the students who donated blood, Vital donated 1 Vital Water per person in addition to the water donation for the whole program.
Mr. Ou Vannak, Representative of the National Blood Transfusion Center, also praised the leadership of the University of Human Resources, which always pays attention to the charity program, especially this voluntary blood donation program, which is a strong motivation for private universities. As well as the other public in this campaign more and more across the country.
Dr. Ly Sovit, Vice President of the National Blood Transfusion Center, also thanked the National Human Resources Students for their zeal and welcome to the voluntary blood donation campaign for many years. Get more generous blood vessels to supplement the supply to the growing need every day.
In a message received by Fresh News, Samdech Techo Hun Sen emphasized, "I would like to take this opportunity to call on all Cambodians to learn more about ASEAN and to seek more opportunities." "The other comes from regionalization and globalization."
