Ms. Phoeung Sakona's statement came after it was reported that she had not facilitated the 500 foreign journalists to visit Angkor Wat at the request of the Minister of Information.
Please be reminded that about 500 multinational journalists from all over the world will attend the Asia Press Summit 2019 in Siem Reap from 10 to 15 June 2019. Information Minister Khieu Kanharith plans to bring these foreign journalists to visit Angkor Wat.
On April 2, 2019, Mr. Khieu Kanharith made an official letter to the Minister of Culture and Fine Arts to allow these foreign journalists to visit Angkor Wat. In response to this request, Ms. Phoeung Sakona on April 10 also replied that the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts has no authority to allow these foreign journalists to visit Angkor Wat.
Ms. Phoeung Sakona also requested the Minister of Information to contact the Angkor Institute instead. This letter from Ms. Pheung Sakona led to a public outcry against the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts, as well as Ms. Phoeung Sakona refusing to mediate these foreign journalists.
In addition to this accusation, Ms. Phoeung Sakona on April 29, 2019 confirmed to Fresh News that the Apsara Authority under the jurisdiction of the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts is only responsible for the maintenance of Angkor Wat. There is no authority to sell tickets to Angkor Wat.
According to the Minister, because of this problem, she turned to the Ministry of Information to contact the Angkor Institute to ask for mediation and allow all 500 foreign journalists to visit Angkor Wat.
