Bilateral meeting between Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Aung San Suu Kyi ended
(Phnom Penh): At around 10:20 am on Tuesday, April 30, 2019, the bilateral meeting between Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Ms. Aung San Suu Kyi, State Councilor of the Union of Myanmar ended successfully at the Palace. Peace.
After concluding the meeting with Samdech Techo, Ms. Aung San Suu Kyi will pay a courtesy call and have a working conversation with Samdech Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin, President of the National Assembly.
In the afternoon of the same day, she will pay a courtesy call on Samdech Vibol Sena Pheakdey Say Chhum, President of the Senate, and then the State Councilor of Myanmar will pay homage to His Majesty King Norodom Sihanouk. And Queen Mother Norodom Monineath Sihanouk at the Royal Palace.
Tonight, there will also be a dinner to receive her visit to Cambodia by Samdech Techo Hun Sen at the Peace Palace.
Angkor Wat, one of Cambodia's most famous treasures, was also the site of Aung San Suu Kyi's heartfelt visit during her first visit to Cambodia. Aung San Suu Kyi will visit Angkor Wat in Siem Reap on May 1, 2019. After visiting Angkor Wat, she will fly from Cambodia to her country on the same day.
Aung San Suu Kyi's current visit to Cambodia is seen as a contribution to further improving relations and cooperation between Cambodia and Myanmar.
Cambodian expert unit cooperates with Chinese-Indian companies to sign MoU to boost agricultural exports
(Phnom Penh): Seeing the natural potential in Cambodia for the agricultural sector, on April 29, 2019, Phnom Penh Department of Industry and Handicraft, Entrepreneurs for Society, Sram Energy, Technology and Rice Limited of India and Jimmy Co., Ltd. China's Internet has signed a memorandum of understanding to promote the processing and export of agricultural products to regional and global markets.
Mr. Tum Pen Virakvitou, President of the Association of Entrepreneurs for Society (ASF), said that for the first time, this is a new experience for Cambodian agricultural experts to study together with foreign companies on various information in the market. Both domestically and abroad.
Mr. Tum Pen Virakvitou continued that in particular, the association is committed to the training and development of human resources, finance, technology, jurisdictional support, jurisdiction, digital marketing, ISO quality standards, products, services, packaging and delivery to members who are registered as Members of the association and registered with the relevant ministries. In addition, all trade and cooperation between producers and buyers is coordinated by the association.
Mr. Penny Chun, CEO of GMI International, said that the cooperation with the Association of Entrepreneurs for Society will contribute to boosting the Cambodian economy by investing in existing skills in line with the vision to promote Cambodian agricultural products for export. Traffic in regional and global markets.
He added that in addition, his company will strive to better cooperate with Cambodian entrepreneurial partners in key areas as well. The three main areas to be implemented are the civil society sector, the private sector and the focus on the policy of the Royal Government of Cambodia.
