The Emperor of Japan will ascend the throne in early May, the Embassy of Japan in Cambodia opens the embassy for the public to write a message to congratulate and celebrate the coronation.
(Phnom Penh): The Embassy of Japan in Cambodia on April 29, 2019 announced the opening of the Embassy to welcome the public who wish to write a message of congratulations and congratulations on the coronation of its heir to the throne. Ascend the throne in early May.
The Japanese Embassy said on Facebook that Prince Naruhito, the Crown Prince, will ascend the throne as Emperor of Japan on May 1, 2019. Taking this opportunity, the Embassy of Japan will welcome the public to enter the embassy to write a message of congratulations and congratulations on the coronation.
Members of the public wishing to write a message of congratulations and congratulations, please go to the Embassy of Japan in Cambodia, Multipurpose Hall (behind the entrance to the Consular Section) for only 2 days, May 3 and 6, 2019 from 9:00 a.m. to 11:00 a.m. and 2:00 to 4:00 p.m. According to the embassy broadcast.
At the same time, the Embassy of Japan also stated that: * All members of the public, please bring your ID card. * There is no parking space in the embassy. * The Siem Reap Provincial Consulate will also be open to receive greetings. .
