Cambodia launches national consultation and training on "Promoting Women's Entrepreneurship"
The program is co-organized by the ESPN National Committee of the Royal Government of Cambodia (NCDC) and the United Nations Economic and Social Commission for Asia and the Pacific (UNESCAP) to discuss challenges and processes. Promoting women's entrepreneurship in Cambodia, as well as the role of women's economic empowerment in promoting growth, poverty reduction and sustainable development.
In relation to the purpose of this program, Senior Minister Ly Thuch stated that the promotion of small and medium enterprises is a priority direction of the Royal Government in the development of the private sector, as stated in the Rectangular Strategy Phase 3 and 4. Industrial Development Policy 2015-2025 and other policies and strategies of the Royal Government of Cambodia.
As for women, they also play a very important role in Cambodian society, in fact, women are not only the caretakers of the family, but also play an important role in the economic and social affairs, as well as politics.
On that occasion, Senior Minister Ly Thuch also proudly stated that Cambodia is a country that has been plagued by war, insecurity due to armed conflict and a killing field, and has a declining economy and poverty. But now Cambodia has proudly changed its face and has become a country of complete peace, stability and rapid development in all areas.
The Senior Minister emphasized that this is a great achievement in history achieved under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, which shows the ideals and strong commitment of the Royal Government in striving to serve the nation and the people. The common interests of the people continue to defend and build the motherland towards a glorious future in accordance with the will and aspirations of the people.
(Kep): Nearly 3,000 people in Kep province expressed their excitement and gratitude to Mr. HUN Many, Member of Parliament for Kampong Speu Constituency, who sent a team of more than 400 volunteer doctors to help treat and distribute Provide free medicine to the people.
This thank you from the people in Kep province was made on April 28, 2019 on the occasion of the 451 volunteer doctors of Mr. HUN Many led by Mr. Leang Phaly, the head of the medical team. Mr. Hun Many volunteered to treat 2,989 people at Bun Rany Hun Sen Primary School, Damnak Chang Eur Village, Damnak Chang Eur Village, Sangkat Prey Thom, Kep City, Kep Province.
Free medical check-ups and medicine have become a joy for people living in Kep City, Kep Province. Among them, a woman named Dam Dun, among other citizens, expressed her happiness as never before.
Ms. Dun has gastritis and every day this pain in her stomach, thanks to Mr. Hun Many's team of volunteer doctors who came to treat her as well as other villagers.
Ms. Dam Dun expressed her great satisfaction for the arrival of all the doctors, stating that "I save money because the doctors come to treat patients for free and do not spend time away as usual. Times that lead to loss of time affect work.
Another resident, Sam Chantha, who has a nasal allergy, said: "I feel happy when they come down to check and give me free medicine, it saves me money."
In addition to expressing their happiness, the people asked Mr. Hun Many's team of volunteer doctors to visit and treat them to reduce costs and get a highly effective treatment.
