A bomb blast near the Bangladeshi capital Dhaka has killed at least two people.
Dhaka: A suspected network of two militants has been confirmed dead by Bangladeshi authorities in a series of explosions at their hideout during a security operation. This was quoted from the Chinese news agency Xinhua on Monday afternoon, April 29, 2019.
On Monday, Bangladeshi crime forces surrounded a house in the Bosila area of Dhaka, where authorities suspect a suspected militant group was hiding. Later, repeated explosions occurred in the house.
According to Bangladeshi authorities, at least two suspects exploded into pieces as three legs were found at the scene. Meanwhile, four people were detained for questioning.
Bangladesh has continued to tighten security since a militant attack on a cafe in the Gulshan area of Dhaka on July 1, 2016, which killed 22 people. Most are foreigners. Since the outbreak, Bangladeshi police have often launched large-scale operations against militants.
