(Phnom Penh): Hospital leaders of French-speaking countries in Southeast Asia, including Cambodia, Vietnam and Laos, as well as experts from France, jointly held an international meeting this morning, April 29, 2019. One by discussing "the development of non-hospital surgery procedures." The meeting was held at Calmette Hospital.
Professor Chheang Ra, Director General of Calmette Hospital, stated that this is not really a discussion of surgical techniques, but a set of new developments for the treatment methods that are prevalent in many different fields in the country. Cambodia. Not only that, Cambodia also has the opportunity to understand the main needs and explore ways to develop the institution of the hospital as the living standards of the people have improved and increased significantly.
At the same time, the level of demand of customers is also increasing, as they are aware of the latest medical techniques from various institutional sources and demand to receive treatment as soon as possible to return home. He said that non-hospital surgery is very popular in France as well as in developed countries, which is of great importance for patients, saving both health and time.
"Non-hospitalization surgery means that the operation takes less than 12 hours and does not require an overnight stay," he said. Such surgeries are careful and use the latest technology, combined with the team of highly skilled doctors.
He emphasized that the traditional surgery required patients to be hospitalized for three to five days, but with the help of technology and a team of doctors, we were able to perform the operation in just half a day. Next up.
Please note that this meeting is a good opportunity and a meeting of international conferences between countries in Southeast Asia in French with French experts from France, Cambodia, Laos and Vietnam on a very important topic.
