Before concluding his mission in Beijing, China, on Monday morning, April 29, 2019, Cambodian Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen met with Chinese President Xi Jinping. In this meeting, Samdech Techo Hun Sen and the delegation were warmly welcomed by the President of China.
According to Kao Kim Hourn, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister, during the meeting, Samdech Techo Hun Sen and the Chinese President raised a number of issues related to strengthening political, economic, trade and economic cooperation. National defense between the two countries.
Regarding the defense sector, Mr. Kao Kim Hourn said that the President of China has announced to support and protect the Cambodian defense sector better to protect the integrity and sovereignty of Cambodia.
Regarding trade issues between the two countries, Samdech Techo Hun Sen requested the Chinese President to continue to support about 700 Chinese enterprises doing business in Cambodia to continue doing business in Cambodia and also to encourage new Chinese investors. More to do business in Cambodia.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also raised the issue of the EBA, which the EU plans to withdraw from Cambodia. In response, Samdech Techo Hun Sen told the Chinese President that Cambodia has made a number of reforms to reduce production costs as well as company operations and ensure the competitiveness of Cambodian products in international markets.
To address the EU threat by suspending the EBA, Hun Sen has asked the Chinese president to open up more markets for Cambodian products.
In response to Samdech Techo Hun Sen's request, Xi Jinping said that Cambodia is a loyal friend of China, so China will continue to support Cambodia, especially in the framework of a comprehensive strategic partnership between the two countries.
Regarding the EBA issue, the Chinese President affirmed that China will make efforts to help solve this challenge by encouraging more Chinese investors to come to Cambodia and opening up the Chinese market for more Cambodian products.
Xi Jinping also claimed that through the "Belt and Road" initiative, he would promote the development of special economic zones, the construction of airports and expressways in Cambodia.
