(Svay Rieng): A man who has been a newspaper distributor in Svay Rieng for almost 30 years, who used to sell in various departments in the province and sell newspapers to readers at home, etc., has complained about his family's livelihood. At the moment, newspapers do not sell very well because there is a modern online media technology on customers' phones, making it difficult to sell and distribute because there are no buyers for newspapers like before.
Mr. Pen Min, riding an old motorcycle at Veal Yon Market to distribute newspapers to customers, told Fresh News this morning, April 29, 2019, that he is 54 years old and works as a newspaper distributor. He lives in Kork Pring commune, Svay Chrum district, Svay Rieng province and has been distributing newspapers and magazines since 1993 for more than 20 years.
The newspaper distributor, who has been reading the newspaper for almost 30 years, stated that the reason for the decline in the distribution and sale of newspapers was due to modern media systems such as mobile phones, social media, Facebook and online news. But as he still loves his job of distributing newspapers and magazines, he continues to sell even for a small profit, because in addition to selling newspapers, he also has a farming business to feed his family.
