On the evening of April 28, 2019, on the occasion of the inauguration of the "International Horticultural Exhibition Center 2019" with the leaders of the "Belt and Road" cooperation partners, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia The inauguration of this Cambodian park is also official.
At the International Horticultural Exhibition Center, Chinese leaders have provided land for the construction of a symbolic garden for each of the "Belt and Road" partner countries.
Cambodia established this park for the purpose of promoting the culture and building the reputation of Cambodia to be more famous in the international arena, a land full of beautiful traditional culture in line with the theme "living Better to live in a green environment. ”
Participating in this event, Cambodia will have the opportunity to share experiences related to the daily life of the people, show the culture, traditions, customs and practices of the people, the environment of living through the garden of nature and diverse plants represent National identity and popular with people such as palm trees, palm trees and flowers.
Along with the traditional and modern garden design is beautiful to attract the attention of international tourists. Cambodia will also have the opportunity to build good global cooperation through connectivity and cooperation in the fields of tourism, cultural exchange, traditions, economics, trade, investment and protection of the natural environment in Cambodia.
Cambodia attaches great importance to the protection of the green environment and has the fundamental goal of linking the green environment to the lives of the people and the world for the physical harmony, freshness of life in line with the theme of the exhibition "Living Better to live in a green environment. ”
The Cambodian Garden is built in the post-Angkorian Khmer style, combining nature and culture, Khmer traditions, village decoration and display of tools that serve the daily life of the people. The entrance gates are decorated in the Khmer style, following the pattern of the National Museum gates and have a fence around the garden.
The statue with a soft smile represents the royal splendor of the ancient Khmer kings of ancient times, has compassion, compassion and devotion to cover the territory of Cambodia in all four directions and has given peace to people, animals and plants. Living in peace with nature in accordance with the sub-theme is living in harmony with nature.
The pavilion on the right and left side of the four-faced statue has an octagonal pavilion for a short rest period of national and international guests after visiting the Cambodian National Park and Pavilion. In this workshop, visitors can admire the scenery of the Cambodian Garden and also learn about some of the tools of the ancient Khmer people that are displayed nearby, such as ox carts, plows, rakes and other tools that serve the field. Agriculture.
In this park, Cambodia built three national pavilions in the Khmer style of the Chaktomuk period. At the entrance of the National Pavilion, two stone lion statues in the style of the Longvek stone lion are displayed to show the power of power to protect the earth and nature.
