(Phnom Penh): The Garment Manufacturers Association of Cambodia (GMAC) on the morning of April 27, 2019 held the election of a new chairman, while the old president to end his two-year term and organize a meeting to review the results of 2018. Presided over by Mr. Ith Sam Heng, Minister of Labor and Vocational Training.
Prior to the review process, GMAC held a new presidential election, with the results showing that Van Sou Ieng was re-elected as chairman, along with three vice presidents and 19 other members. Composed from representatives of different factories.
Speaking on that occasion, Mr. Ith Sam Heng praised the Garment Manufacturers Association of Cambodia, which since its inception has played an important role as a representative of the garment and footwear sector in Cambodia.
According to the Minister, until now, GMAC has a clear statute and mechanisms, including the headquarters of vocational training schools. In recent years, GMAC has also been a partner in tripartite mechanisms such as the negotiation of working conditions, the contribution to the drafting of laws and regulations related to the garment sector, and the negotiation of related issues. For the benefit of workers and employers directly.
In addition, Minister Ith Sam Heng also thanked Mr. Van Sou Ieng and the leaders of the Garment Manufacturers Association in Cambodia for their hard work in this field to attract investors, especially investors in the sector. Tailor clothes and shoes to join together.
Mr. Ith Sam Heng also considered that GMAC is one of the largest associations in Cambodia and plays the most active role in the tripartite mechanism, and in recent years he observed the progress of employment and vocational training.
At the same time, Mr. Van Sou Ieng, who has just been elected as the Chairman of GMAC for the new term of 2 years, expressed his excitement that he was elected as the Chairman and made a commitment to work hard. This work is even better for the progress of the garment and footwear sector in Cambodia.
Please note that the Garment Manufacturers Association of Cambodia (GMAC) is recognized by the Royal Government of Cambodia as a representative of garment exporters. Founded in 1996, GMAC has become a major association representing the promotion and protection of the rights and interests of the garment industry.
GMAC's goal is to provide a forum for consultation and discussion among members on common interests and to seek the adoption of sound policies and a favorable legal environment conducive to the growth and development of the Cambodian garment industry.
GMAC also provides value-added services to its members, such as market linkages, market promotion, marketing support, training, legal updates, including government regulations and announcements, business partnerships, general business information, and more. More.
