(Phnom Penh): As planned, the 6th National Robot Competition 2019 was held on April 27, 2019. After a tough competition, a group of students from the National Polytechnic Institute of Cambodia (NPIC) won the first prize.
Today's National Robotics Competition was presided over by the Minister of Information, Mr. Khieu Kanharith, and Mr. Hidehisa Sahiro Noochi, Ambassador of Japan to Cambodia, and was attended by Information Ministry officials, Japanese Embassy officials and more than 1,000 students. People.
The competition consists of nine teams from five institutes and universities, competing under the "Riding a Horse with a License Plate" and following the formula of the competition until a series of winners. Universities and institutes that send students to participate in this competition are: Royal University of Phnom Penh, National University of Management, Institute of Technology of Cambodia, National Polytechnic Institute of Cambodia and Preah Kosomak Polytechnic Institute.
The first place winner received 6 million riels, the second place winner received 3 million riels, the engineering winner received 800,000 riels, the winner won 800,000 riels, the winner Rachana received 800,000 Riels, the winner of the popularity category received 800,000 Riels and the winner of the Toyota Award received 1.2 million Riels.
Mr. Pang Chamnan also said that the national robot competition is organized to provide opportunities for students to demonstrate the ability to apply the theory they are learning in school to sharpen the ability and human resources in the field of robotics. Which may be needed in various fields in Cambodia in the future.
