(Preah Sihanouk): Officials from Preah Sihanouk Provincial CamControl Branch caught fresh shrimp with banned chemicals imported by traders through Prek Chak border crossing on the Cambodia-Vietnam border to sell in Sihanoukville market this Saturday, April 27, 2019. .
Preah Sihanouk Provincial Deputy Chief of CamControl, Mr. Neou Ton, told Fresh News Agency that yesterday, his officials, in cooperation with the Anti-Economic Crime Police of Preah Sihanouk Provincial Police, seized a truck carrying 45 fresh shrimp. Weighing 900 kilograms, it contained banned chemicals that traders imported from Vietnam through the Cambodian-Vietnamese border crossing at Prek Chak, Kampot province, and immediately burned them.
He said that the fresh shrimp products after the Camcontrol branch in Sihanoukville analyzed and found a mixture of chemicals like jelly was mixed in the fresh shrimp.
Mr. Neou Ton said that fresh shrimp with 45 chemicals were immediately destroyed in the Camcontro branch in Sihanoukville this morning, April 27, 2019. The official also required the owner of the truck to transport shrimp and represent the owner of the goods to make a contract to stop importing shrimp containing those chemicals in the future.
Starting from this issue, Mr. Chea Pech, Deputy Director of CamControl Sihanoukville Branch also called on the relevant parties, especially traders to cooperate and stop importing or selling vegetables, fish, meat and other goods that contain banned chemicals. No longer affect human health.
He said that the importation or sale of goods and food spoiled or mixed with chemicals to keep fresh food for sale for a long time is illegal and that those involved in the above activities will face punishment if professional officials find There was a serious mistake.
