The following is the NEC's press release:
Looking back at the work of the government and the Electricity Authority, we have also seen the efforts to solve not only the problems ahead, but also the government has a clear plan for the development of the electricity sector for a long time, and this shortage of electricity. Samdech Techo Hun Sen also announced many times for the understanding of the people.
However, I think this is only a temporary and short-term problem. After the next month or two, things will be normal and better.
So just turn off the power for a few hours, do not complain. Instead, you need to overcome these small issues in order to achieve great things and become strong in the future. Do not forget that today, not only children, even some old people lose patience, struggle to forget their past because they live too comfortably.
So as parents, we should set an example for our children. But it is noteworthy that some parents complain before their children complain at home and then complain on Facebook.
In my opinion, this is not a good example for children. I am not saying this to protect the government, but I want to share this idea because I have read many books and documents about the history of Japanese and Korean nation-building after World War II.
These two nations have endured all kinds of hardships and worked hard and were very patient to build the country as it is today. In this sense, I want our Cambodians to follow the example of the Japanese and Koreans to build our country and our family strong. If we just complain a little bit like this, we are showing our weakness in front of our descendants.
