(Beijing): Video of the speech of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, at the opening ceremony of the 2nd Belt and Road Forum in Beijing on the morning of April 26, 2019. Men Sam An Receives Communist Party Secretary of Lao Ninh Province, China
(Phnom Penh) - Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of National Assembly-Senate Relations and Inspection, Ms. Men Sam An, received a delegation from Lao Ninh province led by Mr. Chiu Fa Chen, Secretary of the Communist Party of Lao PDR, People's Republic of China, on April 26. 2019 at Sofitel Hotel, Phnom Penh.
For a start, Ms. Men Sam An welcomed the Lao PDR delegation to visit Cambodia at this time, while Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister, was attending a one-way, one-belt meeting with more than 100 members. Country in Beijing, China.
She added that in the past, the Royal Government of Cambodia has always supported Chinese investment, and China's One Belt One Road policy has really benefited Cambodia as well as the world.
At the same time, Mr. Chin Fa Chen also thanked Ms. Men Sam An for her support for Lao Ninh Province. He added that Lao Ninh and Sihanoukville are sister provinces and are currently establishing special economic zones there. Meanwhile, all the investment of Lao Ninh province has created a lot of job opportunities for the people in Sihanoukville.
The Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of National Assembly-Senate Relations and Inspection also requested Mr. Chin Fa Chen to continue to provide more support to the education and health sectors, especially to help Svay Rieng to join the Royal Government of Cambodia in the development of Cambodia. .
Finally, she also thanked Xi Jinping as well as the delegation for their significant contribution by sending good Chinese investors to Cambodia.
Ministry of Labor calls on factory owners to adhere to the guidelines to combat global warming (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): In response to global warming as Cambodia continues to be affected by El Nino (El Nino), the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training on April 26, 2019 called on factory owners, enterprises, workers to strictly follow the instructions of the relevant ministries.
The call from the Ministry of Labor, received by Fresh News tonight, confirms that as Cambodia continues to be affected by El Nino, which extends the dry season until mid-May and the weather in The Ministry continues to call on workers, owners and directors of enterprises and establishments to pay attention to the following:
* A: For workers, please strictly follow the content of the announcement of the Ministry of Health on the prevention of diseases caused by hot weather, such as:
1: Increase the intake of boiled water as much and as often as possible without waiting until thirsty.
2. Do not drink liquids that contain a lot of alcohol or sugar, because those substances cause more dehydration.
3: Avoid drinking very cold drinks because it can cause stomach upset.
4: Avoid eating hot food and eating too much because it increases body heat.
6: Wear thin or light and loose clothing.
7: Always maintain good hygiene, such as washing hands with soap after leaving the toilet and before and after eating.
The Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training strongly hopes that all workers, owners and directors of enterprises and establishments will comply with this appeal effectively.
The following is the appeal of the Ministry of Labor:
