(Stung Treng): General Sao Sokha, Deputy Commander of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and Commander of the National Gendarmerie, has assigned Stung Treng Provincial Gendarmerie Commander Brigadier General Ieng Vandy to search for and find poor families and daughters. There are serious diseases in Stung Treng district that are distributed in the society to receive donations and help treat diseases.
After receiving this order, Brigadier General Ieng Vandy, on April 26, 2019, assigned Lieutenant Colonel Un Vannan, Director of the Department of Administration and Finance, to conduct a search immediately to hand over the donations and send them to Take to Stung Treng Provincial Hospital to treat the victim.
Sources said that after receiving information shared on Facebook that a family is poor and has a 15-year-old daughter with chickenpox, called chickenpox and severe gastrointestinal disease. General Sao Sokha assigned him to search for the family in order to hand over the gifts and rescue them.
This family lives in Kham Phan village, Samaki commune, Stung Treng district, they are really poor and the mother is just 4 months old. In addition, it was observed that the military officers sent the patient to the Provincial Referral Hospital for treatment, and the doctors promised to treat the patient very carefully so that he could recover as soon as possible.
At the same time, the family expressed their deep gratitude to General Sao Sokha through Brigadier General Ieng Vandy for rescuing them who are in great distress.
