A modern polyclinic building in Chamkarmon district officially opened!
(Phnom Penh): Arianda Polyclinic and Maternity Hospital this morning, April 26, 2019, officially inaugurated in front of its modern polyclinic, located at Building 9A, Street 430, Sangkat Tonle Bassac, Khan Chamkarmon, Phnom Penh.
The ceremony was presided over by the Honorable Dr. Men Sam An, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of National Assembly Senate Relations and Inspection, Dr. Yok Sambath, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Health, Mr. MICHAEL TAN, Ambassador of the Republic of Singapore to Cambodia, and Ms. Neak Oknha, Mr. Oknha and Large number of national and international guests.
Arinda Polyclinic and Maternity Hospital evolved from a small clinic called Sokha, which started its operations in 2015.
Supporting the quality of treatment over the past four years and seeing the need for high quality and standard treatment services, the shareholders, including Ms. Kuon Thida, Ms. Kry Vouchchon and two other doctors, decided to expand the scope. And services from a small clinic to Ariana Polyclinic and Maternity.
This update makes this hospital a private health institution that provides the leading medical services in Cambodia, providing consultation and treatment in many areas such as:
* Obstetrics & Gynecology * Obstetrics * Pediatrics * General Diseases * Heart Disease * Emergency Services * 24-hour inpatient and in-flight special services, all of which are designed to respond To the needs of current patients.
Ariana Polyclinic has well-known doctors working in national and international institutions with many years of specialization and experience, combined with modern medical equipment imported from abroad, laboratories, operating theaters, laboratories and labs, designed by foreign medical engineers. To provide comfort and quality of treatment to international standards.
Speaking at the ceremony, Ms. KUON Thida, Director General of Ariana Polyclinic and Maternity Hospital, said that the decision to establish Ariana Polyclinic and Maternity Hospital with the vision to reduce the number of Cambodian patients seeking medical services abroad and improve the quality of services. Treat the country like any other developed country in the region and in the world.
Ms. Kuon Thida stated that the mission of Arinda Polyclinic is to provide effective, quality and affordable medical services to the people living in Cambodia.
(Phnom Penh): The Chroy Changvar Satellite City Development Project is developing rapidly by transforming from a flooded lake land into an area with the development of infrastructure, roads, bridges, sewers, power lines and growing buildings to enhance the beauty of Phnom Penh, the heart of Cambodia. .
After receiving the right to develop the Chroy Changvar satellite city from the Royal Government in 2011, OCIC has cooperated with the Phnom Penh authorities to address the impact on the people very carefully, so that the people benefit. Much of this development will not bring tears to the eyes of the people.
Authorities and developers have implemented policies to address the impact by accepting funding, relocating houses and market stalls in Borey Rong Roeung, receiving 10 percent of the land, and evicting old villages. As for the impact solution, it is almost completely solved and there is very little left.
The policy of exchanging old houses for new ones in Borey Rong Roeung is a policy that has received a lot of support from the people, who are very happy and satisfied because they have moved people living in slums, no order, small houses. Flooded to live in a stone house in a beautiful Borey Rong Roeung.
Speaking on the occasion of distributing gifts to the people who volunteered to live in Borey Rong Roeung, Duke Pong Kheav Se claimed that he will take the people who volunteer to live in Borey Rong Roeung as a model for Cambodia to live in Borey Rong Roeung Have a better life. And he believes that the people who live in Borey Rong will be better than the people who decide to leave Borey Rong Roeung.
Duke Pung Kheav Se expressed his belief that Borey Rong Roeung is a good example in Cambodia that develops projects with care and understanding of the difficulties of the people, favorable, attentive And take care to make the people who live in Borey Rong Roeung have a better life.
"I believe that Borey Rong Roeung is a good example in the Kingdom of Cambodia, where the developers of the project have the attention and suffering of the people to be an example," said OCIC CEO. We have the favor and we have the care and we have our care to enter the prosperous city is the one who can predict the future in the prosperous city.
Please be informed that Chroy Changvar Satellite City Development Company (OCIC) has already exchanged houses for people living in slums five times, which has already reached 339 families, including 164 families from Svay Chuor village. 147 families in Dey Meas community and 28 families in Doeum Kor village.
In addition to exchanging houses for the people, the company also does not leave them, but regularly pays attention and offers regular gifts every year. Dealing with the impact of such OCIC development projects has been done to hundreds of families, and they have been happily accepted by some, some of whom have 2-by-2-meter wooden houses. Meters or 3 meters came to live in a beautiful apartment in Borey.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol: China does not speak in vain, but cooperates with countries around the world to bring prosperity
(Beijing, China): Accompanying Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, to the 2nd "Belt and Road" Forum in Beijing, China, Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, was invited to deliver a speech. A key point in the forum on infrastructure connectivity on April 26, 2019.
In front of the leaders of relevant ministries of China and more than 100 member countries and partners, Senior Minister Sun Chanthol highlighted and highly appreciated China's role in contributing to the construction of infrastructure in Cambodia and other countries. Member both locally and globally.
In his speech, Senior Minister Sun Chanthol highlighted the Chinese proverb "If you want to be rich, build the road first" and the Khmer proverb "There is a way, there is hope", both of which value construction. Road and bridge infrastructure.
The Minister said that the development of Cambodia's infrastructure supported by China is to promote both physical and people-to-people connections. This development has significantly improved Cambodia and other participating countries, and Cambodia is proud to be a founding member of the AIIB, a supporter and beneficiary of this initiative.
In his speech, Senior Minister Sun Chanthol also praised Chinese President Xi Jinping's "Belt and Road" initiative.
To date, with concessional loans and grants from China, Cambodia has built more than 3,000 km of roads, eight major bridges and a Mekong River port.
Through the "Belt and Road" initiative, Cambodia held a groundbreaking ceremony for the construction of the Phnom Penh-Sihanoukville Expressway under the BOT (Transaction Execution) investment of approximately US $ 2 billion in investment. One of the largest recent infrastructure investments as part of the Belt and Road Initiative.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol praised the Chinese people, saying that China does not speak in vain, but has a good spirit of cooperation with other countries to support the development of practical infrastructure that brings prosperity based on global principles. .
The Senior Minister concluded his speech by expressing his deep gratitude to the Chinese Government and people for their generous support and assistance to Cambodia's socio-economic growth and development.
