The Royal Government is promoting the educational growth of children with disabilities from kindergarten to high school
(Siem Reap): The Royal Government is promoting the educational growth of children with disabilities by establishing special education institutes and environmental education classes to teach children with disabilities from kindergarten to high school.
In addition, there is physical rehabilitation for children with disabilities in the state rehabilitation centers and community rehabilitation work in the community is continuing to be fruitful to help children with disabilities to be mentally and physically capable. Life skills lessons in daily life.
The Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation will continue to promote activities to promote and protect the interests of children with disabilities. The welfare of people with disabilities and children with disabilities is also taken care of by all circles.
This was stated by Mr. Nhek Vannara, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation, representing Mr. Vong Soth, Minister of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation, speaking at a workshop on identifying and collecting data on children with disabilities living in child care centers. State and child care center of the organization organized on April 26, 2019 in Siem Reap.
Speaking at the seminar, Mr. Nhek Vannara added that the Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation was also actively working to fulfill its role and responsibilities to effectively address the issue of children with disabilities, promoting a society without Barriers to preventing children with disabilities to live in equity without discrimination.
In the past as well as now, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, has also increased his attention to consider the interests and improve the living standards of children with disabilities appropriately, as well as inspiring citizens, philanthropists, the private sector and Civil society organizations to support children with disabilities as well.
