Samdech Techo stated that in the digital age, the whole world is no longer divided into continents, and we all live in harmony, and I understand that there is only an effort to build a common destiny. Will sustain the whole of humanity can continue to live together in harmony and peace. This is what I value most in terms of belt and road initiatives.
In front of Chinese President Xi Jinping and leaders from more than 100 other countries, Samdech Techo Hun Sen said, "The fact that an economic power has the ideals and conscience to build a community of destiny together with other countries "Other economies, both large and small, are a heroic example of heroism and a gentle gesture worthy of admiration."
Samdech Techo Hun Sen expected that countries and economies that are prosperous and prosperous will adhere to the common vision and philosophy, that is, strong countries help weak countries, rich countries help the needy in the same goal and help each other. To have the same glorious future destiny.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also said that the Belt and Road Initiative is a framework for regional and global economic and development cooperation and a mechanism that provides resources to countries in the world, especially countries. Developing to fill gaps in financing needs to increase connectivity.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen made the remarks in front of the Chinese President, together with leaders and representatives from more than 100 countries around the world, at the opening ceremony of the second "Belt and Road" forum. On April 26, 2019 in Beijing, China.
During the forum, Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the development of Sihanoukville Special Economic Zone, a major Chinese investment project, is a clear testament to the construction of a "Belt and Road" cooperation plan between the two countries. Samdech Techo continued that these projects have been very successful and currently 161 companies are cooperating. There are 148 Chinese companies and create more than 20,000 jobs for Cambodians.
The Prime Minister also said that the two-step economic development of Sihanoukville could create jobs for an additional 80,000 people.
The construction of the Phnom Penh-Sihanoukville Expressway, which will be a driving force to change the dimensions of the Cambodian economy and improve regional connectivity, is also an important achievement resulting from the "Belt and Road" initiative. This too. This is according to Samdech Techo Hun Sen.
China's "Belt and Road" initiative has been viewed negatively by both the world's largest economy, the United States and European countries. These countries have always warned member countries of the "Belt and Road" initiative that the financing under the initiative is a debt trap.
The head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, said that this initiative was not a debt trap like the ones mentioned above.
Samdech Techo, Head of the Royal Government, also emphasized that Cambodia can not only negotiate and prepare projects based on the spirit of protecting the interests of its nation and its people fairly and equitably. But also achieve a financial engineering that does not create financial burden and public debt to the state. Two big rice buying companies in China are interested in wanting to buy rice from Cambodia without going through a Chinese state company!
The Secretary-General further stated that if the talks reach an agreement, the process of buying and selling rice in Cambodia will start from September 2019 onwards.
The Secretary-General stated that the two companies currently buy rice from Cambodia's neighboring countries, but because of the quality of Cambodian rice is good, they are interested in Cambodian rice.
"The Cambodian Rice Federation will continue to work with the members and negotiate with the above companies on the price and quantity of rice, if any, we will be able to start trading from September 2019 onwards," he said. "Both sides will continue to deepen cooperation in the near future."
Agriculture: People in Kampong Svay district, Kampong Thom province earn 8 to 9 million Riel per season without migration
(Kampong Thom): While many Cambodians have migrated to neighboring countries, but people living in Kork Nguon village, Trapeang Russey commune, Kampong Svay district, Kampong Thom province, it is easy to increase vegetable growing to increase income in Families will reduce migration by earning from 8 to 9 million riels per season.
Not only that, vegetables grown by people naturally are an essential food for people to eat daily and protect health, and growing vegetables is also a big source of income for people living in rural areas. .
Today's vegetable growing business is simplified by the use of modern irrigation techniques and systems, reducing manpower and saving time by using machines as auxiliary to irrigate crops using drip irrigation and irrigation systems.
Meanwhile, Mr. Horn Sophal, a resident of Kork Nguon village, Trapeang Russey commune, Kampong Svay district, Kampong Thom province, said that he now grows vegetables, tomatoes, cucumbers, beans to sell at the market in Kampong Thom at a price he can accept. Tomatoes are a crop that he mentioned that it takes a month and a half to plant and a month and a half to harvest the same.
He planted in a 13-acre plot, harvested a total of between 8 million and 9 million riels, per kilogram he can sell from 2,000 to 3,000 riels, and the cost of this tomato crop For only about 2 million riels, in total, he earned more than 6 million riels for 3 months. This factor proves that growing vegetables is really lucrative, and it also contributes to reducing the import of vegetables from neighboring countries.
He said that growing vegetables, he uses more natural fertilizers than using chemical fertilizers, and the yield that he gets is easy to sell to people to buy and eat does not affect health because he respects this vegetable growing. According to the principle of health first.
