(Phnom Penh): On April 26, 2019, Chip Mong Retail Co., Ltd. held a groundbreaking ceremony for the construction of Chip Mong 598, a community-style shopping mall in Chip Mong Land's Parkland 598 residential project. In Russey Keo district, Phnom Penh.
Chip Mong 598 Mall has 5 floors and 11,000 square meters and 133 parking spaces. The construction of this community-style shopping center will be completed and opened in the first quarter of 2021.
Chip Mong 598 Shopping Mall was built in Chip Mong Land's Parkland 598 residential project to serve the people living in this housing project and the people in Russey Keo district as well as nearby areas.
Meanwhile, Leang Henry, CEO of Chip Mong Land, said that Chip Mong 598 will increase traffic in the Park Lane 598 residential area and nearby areas, which will make businesses in the center. The mall is functioning well and in the future will make the housing in this project more affordable.
It should also be noted that the community shopping center in this housing project is the result of a reliable and modern partnership between Chip Mong Land and Chip Mong Retel, which both companies are committed to bringing new experiences in Easy and complete living for the people living in the housing project of Chip Mong Len and the people living in the nearby area.
Cambodia, China hold talks to boost trade between the two countries
Mr. Sam Sereyroth stated that this forum not only provides opportunities for businessmen and investors of the two countries to meet, discuss and learn about trade and investment opportunities in Cambodia, but also to contribute to the strengthening and expansion of cooperation. Bilateral relations between the two countries in all fields such as trade, industry, tourism, culture, investment and other sectors.
The senior official of the Ministry of Commerce emphasized that in the context of promoting the implementation of the Belt and Road Initiative, the comprehensive strategic partnership between Cambodia and China in all fields has also been strengthened and expanded. Stronger, steadily from year to year.
The senior official said that the total trade volume between Cambodia and China in 2018 reached 6.457 million US dollars, with exports from Cambodia to China amounting to 874 million US dollars. An increase of 15% compared to 2017, while imports from China to Cambodia amounted to 5.583 million US dollars, an increase of 16% compared to 2017.
Mr. Sam Sereyroth said, "Based on the results implemented in 2018, the trade of our two countries reached more than 5 billion US dollars, which meets the trade goals set by the leaders of the country. "Both."
