Boy stabbed to death by stepfather and wife seriously injured in Sihanoukville
(Preah Sihanouk): A 6-year-old boy was stabbed to death by his stepfather with a sharp knife, while his wife was seriously injured and sent to the Sihanoukville Provincial Hospital.
The incident happened at 21:30 on April 25, 2019 at Koh Russey in Ong Ream village, Prey Nob district, Preah Sihanouk province.
Preah Sihanouk Provincial Police Commissioner Major General Chuon Narin confirmed that the suspect was a stepfather named Mao Chhoeun, 34 years old, a construction worker staying at the scene. The victim, 6-year-old Khin, was seriously injured and died at the Provincial Referral Hospital, while his wife, Sem Khon, 33, was seriously injured and was being treated at the Sihanoukville Provincial Hospital.
According to the commissioner, the cause of the murder was due to the suspect being drunk and having a verbal dispute in the family that caused the suspect to commit the crime.
After committing the crime, the suspect and the exhibits were immediately detained by the specialized force and the case was sent to the Sihanoukville Provincial Court for legal action. Court detains three Chinese nationals for forcing a Chinese woman to have sex and holding her hostage for money
