Bombings in Sri Lanka: Authorities drop death toll from 359 to 253 (Video inside) (Colombo): The Sri Lankan Ministry of Health has updated the official death toll in last Sunday's bombings. Only 253 people were killed and hundreds more were injured. This was released by the BBC on Friday, April 26, 2019.
According to the Sri Lankan Ministry of Health, the recount took place during the victim identification process, and the previous death toll of 359 was incorrect, with some officials counting duplicate bodies. .
Last Sunday, nine suicide bombers carried out bomb attacks on hotels and churches in Colombo and Batticaloa, most of them Sri Lankans and 39 foreigners. Seventy-four people were arrested for questioning.
