Senior Minister Sun Chanthol said that Cambodia needs to build the necessary infrastructure to boost economic growth and attract investors to Cambodia. The Minister said that the "Belt and Road" initiative is an important part of building infrastructure in Cambodia.
Speaking in an interview with Fresh News before leaving for China, accompanied by Samdech Techo Hun Sen to the "Belt and Road" forum, Senior Minister Sun Chanthol emphasized, "I want our Cambodia to have a good logistics system. Because our country is in the middle of Thailand and Vietnam. Therefore, the transit of goods from Thailand to Vietnam can pass through Cambodia.
The "Belt and Road" initiative is Xi Jinping's ambitious plan to build a large infrastructure network under the direction of linking trade relations between Asia, Europe, the Middle East and Africa via land and sea. China sees the project as the creation of its new Silk Road.
Currently, 126 countries and 29 international organizations have signed cooperation agreements with China to jointly build this project. The West, including the United States, considers the "Belt and Road" initiative a new type of Chinese colonization of its member states.
Mr. Sun Chanthol denied such allegations. "I do not understand what they are saying," he said. This infrastructure benefits Cambodia and the world. Thus, the Belt and Road Initiative is the link between Asia, Africa and Europe. "This connection makes it easier to transport goods, both goods and people, to create jobs for the whole world."
"So China and more than 100 other countries are working together effectively to bring prosperity to the whole world," he added. This is not to oppress any country, but to make the whole world prosper. This is an initiative that we fully support. ” Leng Navattra Apartment for Sale in Sihanoukville for Only $ 9,900
