World's top leaders attend 2nd Belt and Road Forum in Beijing
BEIJING, April 25 (Xinhua) - The second summit of the Belt and Road Forum (BRF) for International Cooperation will be held in Beijing, China from April 25 to 27, 2019. High quality cooperation under the Belt and Road Initiative. This is according to the release by CGTN on the evening of Thursday, April 25, 2019.
Heads of state and government from 37 countries, including Russian President Vladimir Putin and Philippine President Rodrigo Duterte, as well as other top leaders from Austria, Egypt, Italy, Laos and Cambodia, will attend the forum. Ring and Road (BRF). France, Germany, the United Kingdom, Spain, Japan, South Korea and the European Union are also preparing to send delegates to the meeting.
Ahead of the official meeting, Chinese President Xi Jinping also welcomed bilateral meetings with leaders to discuss friendly economic and trade ties between China and the two countries. Beijing now hosts up to 5,000 guests from 150 countries and a total of 90 international organizations.
Australian Insurance Risk Assessment Training Institute Holds First Asian Insurance Compensation Conference 2019 in Cambodia
The Asia Insurance Compensation Conference 2019 was organized with the participation of Dr. Mey Van, Royal Government Delegate in charge of the Director General of the General Department of Financial Industry of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, as well as participants from many countries.
This conference is a great opportunity for insurance professionals to share as well as learn about the latest trends and developments in the insurance industry. The Insurance Association of Cambodia is very pleased to be a partner in promoting this event and recognizes the benefits of a strong insurance sector for rapid economic growth.
The insurance sector plays an important role in providing hedging to emerging projects and businesses as it provides protection to investors. The insurance sector also provides employment opportunities and covers the issuance of insurance policies, insurance brokers and insurance risk assessments.
The delegates shared their experiences, perspectives and construction, focusing on compensation management in their country.
Dr. Mey Van praised the organization of this Asia Insurance Compensation Event, as he participated in an interesting presentation to share his experiences and best practices in compensation management and provide a forum for stakeholders. Relevant to review the ongoing challenges for insurance coverage.
