The first international standard chicken factory to be launched in Kampot, MPs want to expand production and distribution in the domestic market and to foreign markets
(Phnom Penh): The first factory of meat processing and packaging of international standard chicken with high quality, safety and hygiene in Cambodia was opened in Kampot province on April 25, 2019.
For today's inauguration, Dr. Chea Vandeth, Member of Parliament for Takeo Constituency and Chairman of the Investment, Agriculture, Rural Development, Environment and Water Resources Planning Committee of the National Assembly, together with the Governor of Kampot Province, Mr. Chiao Tai and relevant officials paid a study visit. At the factory. The company, named 3 PLE Farm, is located along National Road 41 in Chheu Teal Village, Champou Vann Commune, Chum Kiri District, Kampot Province.
On that occasion, Mr. Chea Vandeth praised the production process and meat hygiene standards in the factory and encouraged the company to expand production and distribution of its products in the domestic market and to foreign markets.
At present, the company has a chicken farm with a capacity of 35,000 chickens and produces about 1.5 million chickens per year, covering an area of 8 hectares in Prey Tnaot village, Prey Thnong commune, Teuk Chhou district, Kampot province. The company will build another farm by the end of 2019.
The chicken packaging factory has a production capacity of up to 1,500 heads per hour, and the building covers an area of 3,000 square meters on 2 hectares of land in Trapeang Veng village, Trapeang Reang commune, Chum Kiri district, Kampot province, for the purpose of producing high quality chicken. Clean and safe for Cambodians to eat.
Leading companies will contribute to the promotion of agriculture in Cambodia, especially chicken farms and slaughterhouses of international standards in line with the development strategy of the Ministry of Labor, Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries under the wise leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia. The processing plant meets European and American standards with quality and in accordance with strict procedures on biosafety and hygiene with the latest technology.
