From 1995 to 2019, Samdech Techo Hun Sen received honorary degrees and honorary medals from a total of 19 universities, including:
1. In 1995, Samdech Techo received an honorary doctorate in political science from the University of Southern California for his major.
On November 15, 2001, Samdech Techo Hun Sen was awarded an honorary doctorate in political science in the field of international relations from the University of Ramkhamhaeng in the Kingdom of Thailand.
7 - On August 6, 2002, Samdech Techo Hun Sen was awarded the full position of a full member of the Academy of Natural Sciences of the Russian Federation and awarded a medal in recognition of his leadership. To bring peace, stability and social and economic development to Cambodia.
On September 4, 2002, the Committee of the ASEAN Federation of Engineers decided to award Samdech Techo Hun Sen his first and highest honorary title, "Honorary Engineer" in recognition of his national conscience and leadership. To end the civil war, to restore and develop all sectors of society and to enable national engineering intellectuals to participate in the national construction and development movement.
On March 21, 2006, during an official visit to the Republic of Korea, Soon Chun Hyang University in Seoul awarded Samdech Techo Hun Sen an honorary doctorate in political science to highlight national leadership. And wholehearted devotion for peace and prosperity for Cambodia and Southeast Asia, especially for the focus on enhancing friendly relations with the Republic of Korea.
January 29, 2007 - Referred to by the Ministry of Education and Training of the Socialist Republic of Vietnam and the University of Cambodia for their invaluable contribution to the rapid social and economic development of Cambodia. The National Assembly of Hanoi presented Samdech Techo Hun Sen with an honorary doctorate in education.
14: September 21, 2007 Once again, the Association of Trade Diplomats conferred on Samdech Techo Hun Sen the honorary title of a supporter of the trade diplomacy profession.
15 January 07, 2009 in Phnom Penh Recognizing and appreciating the precious contribution to the improvement of economic cooperation between the Republic of Korea and the Kingdom of Cambodia, Woosuk University Higher Education Committee decided to hand over Presented Samdech Techo Prime Minister Hun Sen with an honorary doctorate in economics.
17 September 09, 2015 Recognizing and evaluating the wise leaders, peacemakers and leaders of the only nation in the world with a spirit of dedication and great achievements in transforming Cambodia. Senior Leaders and Board of Directors of Limkokwing University of Technology of Malaysia have decided to confer the honorary doctorate degree "Outstanding Leadership" on Samdech Techo Hun Sen.
On October 15, 2015, during his official visit to the People's Republic of China, Samdech Techo Hun Sen was awarded an honorary doctorate in literature by Guangxi University for the Nation in recognition of his outstanding leadership skills. Unite the country and build strong relations between China and Cambodia.
