(Phnom Penh): The Minister of Tourism, Mr. Thong Khon, expressed his expectation and belief that through the 2nd "Belt and Road" Forum held in Beijing, China, Cambodia will have the opportunity to attract Chinese tourists and investors to Cambodia. More and more.
Minister Thong Khon said that through the "Belt and Road" initiative, has pushed for the construction of many infrastructures in Cambodia, including roads, bridges, railways, as well as airports, which are all part of the tourism sector in Cambodia.
Thong Khon said that there are about 130 million Chinese people who can afford to travel abroad at a cost of about 260 billion US dollars, and by 2020, more than 200 Chinese tourists are expected to travel abroad. Million, at a cost of about $ 460 billion.
According to Thong Khon, 29 million Chinese tourists travel to ASEAN. Among the Chinese tourists to ASEAN, Thailand received about 10 million, Vietnam more than 5 million and Cambodia more than 2 million. In particular, in the first three months of 2019, Cambodia received more than 650,000 Chinese tourists, an increase of more than 30 percent compared to the same period in 2018.
"We see that out of 130 million outbound tourists, 29 million come to ASEAN," he said. Of ASEAN's 29 million, Thailand received nearly 10 million Chinese tourists, Vietnam more than 5 million, and Cambodia received 60 percent more Chinese tourists last year than 2.2 million. "Because of this good policy, we have built a lot of infrastructure and built hotels, created a lot of tourist sites." Mr. Thong Khon further confirmed.
The Minister of Tourism also expressed his hope that through the second "Belt and Road" forum in Beijing, China, in the future, more Chinese tourists and investors will come to Cambodia. To attract Chinese tourists, the Ministry of Tourism and the Royal Government of Cambodia are also ready to provide better services, along with efforts to build infrastructure, establish hotels and tourism products.
