He said this during a meeting to open the voter registration office to elect members of the Svay Rieng Provincial Chamber of Commerce for the first and second mandate on April 25, 2019 at the Svay Rieng Provincial Department of Commerce.
The senior official added that Svay Rieng province has already elected the first mandate of the Chamber of Commerce on July 31, 2016, with 15 members. In 2019, the members of the Provincial Chamber of Commerce must hold the second and second term elections to fill the seven members who have completed their term, leaving eight more members to continue their term, as these eight members will have to complete their term in three years. Coming soon.
Mr. Mao Thora also stated that "In order for the Chamber of Commerce to be more successful, it is necessary to learn from countries with experience in both the private sector and the government by helping each other in trade, in which we need to strengthen the implementation of the project. "Our Chamber of Commerce is strong and effective to avoid being under investor control. The Chamber of Commerce is a major political bridge for the development of our country."
"The private sector has made a significant contribution to helping our country's economy as well," he said.
Please note that since the Royal Government allowed the establishment of special economic zones in 2005 until now, Svay Rieng province has 11 special economic zones, of which 8 are operating.
In addition, there are a number of enterprises and establishments operating outside the special economic zone, which not only provide employment to the people and help boost the national economy, promote Cambodian products to international markets through the export of Products such as clothing, footwear, electronics, electrical wiring, bicycles, lamps, umbrellas, curtains, gloves, measuring instruments, packaging materials, photo frames, metal hangers and more.
MOSCOW (Reuters) - North Korean leader Kim Jong Un and Russian President Vladimir Putin have pledged to strengthen ties as relations between Pyongyang and Washington remain strained. After the summit in Vietnam in February failed. This is according to the release by the BBC on the afternoon of Thursday, April 25, 2019.
In response to Putin, Kim Jong Un also expressed hope that a meeting with the Russian president would help strengthen ties between the two countries.
Putin and Kim will discuss the nuclear issue on the Korean Peninsula, but Kim is also said to be seeking assurances and support from Russia after a failed meeting with Donald Trump in Vietnam. This is Kim Jong Un's first visit to Russia, while his father, Kim Jong Il, has visited Russia three times, the last in 2011.
