(Phnom Penh): Senior Minister Him Chhem, Minister of Cults and Religions, stated that religious freedom is taken care of by the Royal Government and promoted, whether it is Buddhism, Islam, Christianity or any other religion, people have the right to choose their religion. Its free, no citizen is forced to believe in any religion.
This statement was made by Senior Minister Him Chhem on April 25, 2019 at the opening ceremony of an international seminar disseminating research results on "Effective management of Theravada Buddhism in the country along the Mekong-Lan. Chang, Cambodia, China, Laos, Myanmar, Thailand and Vietnam ”at the Cambodiana Hotel.
Senior Minister Him Chhem said: "In this sense, religious freedom is really taken care of and promoted by the Royal Government, whether it is Theravada or Mahayana Buddhism or Islam or Christianity or any other religion. "Furthermore, people have the right to choose their religion freely. No citizen is forced to believe in any religion."
In fact, Cambodia considers Buddhism to be the state religion, as stated in Article 43 of the Constitution of the Kingdom of Cambodia: "Citizens of both sexes have full religious rights. Freedom of religion and religious observance are guaranteed by the state under conditions that do not affect other faiths or religions or public order and security. "Buddhism is the state religion."
