(Battambang): Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior, called on all forces to work together to help repair the houses of people affected by natural disasters in the best possible way.
The appeal of Samdech Krala Hom was made on the morning of April 25, 2019 on the occasion of Samdech visited 279 families affected by the typhoon at Chrey Commune Hall, Thmor Kol District, Battambang Province.
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng said that all forces must cooperate with local authorities to help repair the houses of people affected by the strong winds and are always ready to help in time. Samdech claims that if the authorities go to help the disaster area due to natural disasters but still lack any materials, they must report to Samdech and Samdech will intervene immediately.
At the same time, Samdech Krala Hom also expressed his deep regret that all 279 families were affected by the natural disaster, the wind.
It should be noted that according to the report of Thmor Koul district governor, the people affected by the typhoon in 6 out of 10 communes in Thmor Koul district affected 279 families. Of these, 28 families were severely collapsed and 251 families were affected, a total of 279 families.
The houses of 28 families who were severely affected by the collapse of their houses were donated by Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng. Each family received 200,000 Riels, 20 sheets of zinc, 1 box of pure water, 25 kg of rice and 1 box of noodles. For the average victim, 251 families received donations of 200,000 Riels, 10 sheets of zinc, 1 box of pure water, 25 kg of rice and 1 box of noodles.
The Ambassador stressed that the Chinese government intends to shake hands with Cambodia in the spirit of "belt and road", to jointly discuss, build together, share and continue to deepen mutually beneficial cooperation. To achieve common development and prosperity.
