In 1955, Prime Minister Zhou Enlai and His Majesty King Norodom Sihanouk had a cordial meeting in which Ban Dong opened a new page in China-Cambodia friendship. For decades, the leaders of the two countries have communicated like relatives. His Majesty even considered China as his second homeland.
In 2016, President Xi Jinping paid a historic visit to the Kingdom of Cambodia to set a clear direction for the development of Sino-Cambodian relations in the new era and set a roadmap.
China, on the other hand, has always respected Cambodia's sovereignty and independence, and supported Cambodia in pursuing a development path that is in line with its country's realities, and has always provided assistance for Cambodia in economic development and improving the lives of its people as far as possible. China can do it. Mutual support and assistance has become a prominent feature of the steel friendship between China and Cambodia.
China-Cambodia friendship has always been rooted in the hearts of the people of both countries. Over the years, the highly developed humanitarian relations between the two countries have become a major driving force for development in all aspects. In 2018, more than 2 million Chinese tourists visited Cambodia, while more than 100,000 Cambodian tourists visited China, an average increase of more than 60%.
