(Phnom Penh): At around 2:00 pm (Beijing time) on April 25, 2019, the Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen led a high-level Cambodian delegation to Beijing, China. It is safe to attend the Second Belt and Road Forum and other important meetings organized by the Chinese government.
Cambodia's special aircraft, Flight 001, landed safely at Beijing Capital International Airport in the presence of a very warm welcome, a senior Chinese government official and several Cambodian diplomatic dignitaries to the People's Republic of China.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen and his delegation will spend five days in Beijing from April 25 to 29, 2019 to attend the second "Belt and Road" forum and other important meetings.
According to the Cambodian Ministry of Foreign Affairs, during the Second Summit of the Belt and Road Forum on April 26, the Prime Minister will deliver a keynote address on the theme of the "Belt and Road Cooperation Forum". "Create a glorious common destiny." The next day, at the Leaders' Roundtable, the Prime Minister will share his vision on "Promoting Connectivity to Find New Resources for Growth."
After attending the 2nd Belt and Road Forum, Samdech Techo Prime Minister and other Heads of State / Government will attend the opening ceremony of the 2019 International Horticultural Exhibition, on which Samdech Techo, Head of the Royal Government, will inaugurate the Cambodian pavilion. Also.
During his stay in China, the Prime Minister will hold separate bilateral meetings with President Xi Jinping, Premier Li Keqiang, Wang Hunning, a member of the Politburo and secretary of the Communist Party Secretariat. China. The Prime Minister will also meet with Mr. Ly Yong, Director General of the United Nations Industrial Organization, as well as receive courtesy calls from representatives of some Chinese companies.
It should be noted that the "Belt and Road" initiative is Xi Jinping's ambitious plan to build a large infrastructure network under the direction of linking trade relations between Asia, Europe, the Middle East and Africa via land and road. Water.
China sees the project as the creation of its new Silk Road. Xi Jinping announced the strategic plan for the first time during his visits to Kazakhstan and Indonesia in 2013. In just five years, BRI has evolved from a concept to a key platform for building a community with a shared future for humanity and for international public goods.
