(Preah Sihanouk): On the morning of April 25, 2019, the management of Sihanoukville Municipality and the waste collection company KSWM launched a campaign to implement the plan to collect and transport both construction waste and garbage simultaneously in Sihanoukville. The above activities are in response to the results of the meeting on April 24, 2019, held at Sihanoukville City Hall.
Sihanoukville Administration yesterday held a meeting with the participation of Mr. Samuth Sothearith, Director of the Department of Environment, representatives of the Department of Land Management, Urban Planning, Construction and Cadastral Affairs, representatives of the Department of Public Works, Sangkat chiefs and garbage companies and transport contractors. Construction waste with the following two agendas:
* First: Discuss and submit a plan to collect and transport waste at construction sites throughout Sihanoukville. * Second: Discuss and submit a plan to expedite the collection and transportation of garbage.
The results obtained from this meeting show that from 8 am on April 25, 2019, the plan to collect and transport both construction waste and rubbish simultaneously throughout Sihanoukville. Starting from this issue, the people and operators living in Sihanoukville are waiting to see how effective the action of the construction waste contractor under the supervision of the Sihanoukville administration will be.
In this regard, the representative of KSWM, a company that has been awarded the right to invest in garbage collection, showed the consequences that every day, the waste in the city in Sihanoukville has increased by more than 500 percent and the daily amount of garbage is between 600 and 800. Tons per day.
He added that the delay in collecting garbage of the company in the past due to the packaging and storage of garbage of the people are not properly organized, in terms of time for the release of garbage, people have not cooperated with the company. They continue to dump garbage as they remember and do not respect time and so on. In addition, the distance to transport garbage to the landfill is long and there are traffic jams.
Starting from this issue, the KSWM representative requested the authorities to continue to educate the people and relevant parties to participate in packing or storing all kinds of solid and liquid waste properly and bring it to the front of the house at night for convenience. For KSWM staff, it is easy to collect garbage quickly to help promote a clean environment in Sihanoukville as a whole during the day.
In fact, on the morning of April 25, 2019, Mr. I Sok Leng, Governor of Sihanoukville, led a number of government officials and relevant institutions to clean up construction waste and garbage in some locations in Sihanoukville to respond to the results of yesterday's meeting. April 24 yesterday.
