Congratulations! Cambodia gets another dolphin
(Phnom Penh): It is a happy story for the people of Kratie province as well as all Cambodians, now Kampi Dolphin Canyon received another new baby dolphin in mid-April 2019.
The new baby dolphin is the sixth baby dolphin recorded to be born in 2019 from January to April. This is according to the publication of the Organization for the Conservation of Natural Resources of Cambodia (WWF-Cambodia).
WWF has confirmed that a newborn dolphin, about seven days old, was found in a herd of about five large dolphins in Kampi Canyon, Kampi village, Sambok commune, Chit Borei district. Kratie Province on April 18, 2019 at around 14:35 by a joint research team between the Fisheries Administration and WWF-Cambodia in Kratie.
Eng Chea San claims that there are currently more than 100 dolphins in Cambodia's Mekong River. He also expressed his congratulations on the presence of new dolphins, a rare species in Cambodia.
