The book on "Financial Stability of Cambodia" is published for the first time by the National Bank of Cambodia!
(Phnom Penh): After spending almost a year finally, the book on "Financial Stability" prepared by the National Bank of Cambodia was officially launched and released on the afternoon of April 24, 2019.
The book on "Financial Stability 2018" was made with the participation of Ms. Neav Chanthana, Deputy Governor of the National Bank of Cambodia, Ms. Chea Serey, Technical Director General of the National Bank of Cambodia, Mr. Khou Vuthy, Deputy Director General of the National Bank of Cambodia and Many more members of the public.
This is the first time that the National Bank of Cambodia wants to compile a book on "Financial Stability in Cambodia" after the establishment of the Financial Stability Committee for eight years.
Ms. Neav Chanthana said, "This book is designed to disseminate the results of monitoring and analysis of financial stability to ministries, institutions, banking and financial institutions and the public to understand the state of the financial sector, development, challenges. "And the potential risks to financial stability in Cambodia."
"This is the first time that the National Bank of Cambodia has published a book on financial stability after establishing a financial stability committee at the National Bank eight years ago," she said. "I would like to emphasize that the National Bank has strengthened its financial stability monitoring mechanism with the development of professional capacity since 2011 under the technical assistance of the International Monetary Fund."
She said that the book on financial stability has analyzed a number of policies that can be put in place and reduce risks, and this is one of the role of the National Bank of Cambodia to promote the work done to the public, as well as to the Council of Ministers, the National Assembly, etc. to Distribute this information as well as the transparency of the National Bank of Cambodia.
In addition, Mr. Khou Vuthy, Deputy Technical Director of the National Bank of Cambodia, explained in detail the contents of the book on financial stability in Cambodia in detail to the public.
