The 2019 Hanuman Gold Exercise will involve 1595 military personnel and will include 152 mm and 122 mm artillery, 23 mm rifles, 37 mm rifles, BM21 RM70 tanks, armored vehicles, ambulances, fire trucks, transport vehicles, helicopters, etc. Tripartite Consultation on Draft Amendments to Trade Union Law to Meet the Real Needs of Workers
(Phnom Penh): A tripartite consultation with the Royal Government, trade unions and employers' associations was held on April 25, 2019 at the National Tripartite Consultation Workshop on the Draft Amendment of the Law on Trade Unions to Meet the Real Needs of Workers. Employees in the context of current socio-economic developments.
The opening ceremony of the national workshop was presided over by Mr. Ith Sam Heng, Minister of Labor and Vocational Training on April 25, 2019 at the Sunway Hotel, and was also attended by the International Labor Organization (ILO).
He said that the law on trade unions is a legal framework that aims to: 1: Protect the rights and legitimate interests of workers 2: Ensure the right to freedom of collective bargaining between workers and employers 3: Promote harmony in relations Profession 4: Contribute to the development of decent work, increase productivity and investment.
Following the entry into force, the Trade Union Law has made a significant contribution to ensuring harmony in industrial relations and the promotion of freedom of association.
In fact, as of the first quarter of 2019, there were 4,949 professional organizations registered with the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training, including 4,722 local unions, 189 trade unions, 29 unions, and 9 employers' associations. . In addition, the number of collective labor disputes and strikes has also declined significantly due to the effectiveness of the implementation of trade union law and the strengthening of the labor inspection system.
Despite these advances, some unions and international institutions are still unaware of the content of union law provisions, continuing to address some of the concerns on union registration and requests for union representation.
The purpose of this law is to: 1: Promote the rights of professional organizations of domestic workers more broadly 2: Facilitate the procedures and procedures of union registration and record keeping 3: Facilitate the conditions for obtaining the highest representation 4: Promote the rights and roles of unions with minority members more clearly.
