Senior officials of the National Audit Authority: Good civil servants should work with sincerity and professionalism
(Kampong Speu): Mr. Ouk Saravuth, Deputy Auditor General, Representative of Ms. Som Kimsour, Auditor General of the National Audit Authority, said that good civil servants should work with sincerity and professionalism.
Mr. Ouk Saravuth's statement was made on the occasion of the National Audit Authority on the morning of April 24, 2019, which held a seminar to disseminate the Cambodian Law on Auditing and Public Audit Standards to the leaders of civil servants and the Armed Forces under the Provincial Administration. Kampong Speu.
He said that the National Audit Authority is one of the indispensable audit institutions in the country under the rule of law, and therefore all units and departments under the jurisdiction of Kampong Speu Provincial Administration need to cooperate well with the National Audit Authority to expand financial management. Reducing errors and budget fraud aims to promote more efficient implementation.
Mr. Tith Vuthy, Deputy Governor of Kampong Speu Province, welcomed the presence of the delegation of the National Audit Authority who took the time to co-organize this workshop with the purpose of disseminating the Law on Auditing and Cambodian Public Audit Standards in the territory of Kampong Speu Province.
The Deputy Governor emphasized that this workshop was very important for the civil servants and the armed forces under the administration of Kampong Speu to better understand the content of the audit law and the standards of Cambodian public audit. Pay attention to study, listen, record and raise questions to promote practical and successful work.
It should be noted that the Audit Law and Public Audit Standards of Cambodia have identified four main points to be presented in the workshop, including:
1. Background of National Audit Authority 2. Why is there a law on auditing of the Kingdom of Cambodia? Content of the Audit Law and 4. Public Audit Standards of the Kingdom of Cambodia to Civil Servants and the Armed Forces under Kampong Speu Province.
