China claims that Cambodia plays an important role in maintaining regional stability and is a close friend of ASEAN
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Chin Yun, President of the China Association for International Relations, affirmed that Cambodia has played an important role in maintaining stability in the region and that Cambodia is also a close friend of countries in the ASEAN region.
The statement made by the President of the China Association for International Relations during a meeting with Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia at the Peace Palace on April 24, 2019 at the Peace Palace in Cambodia.
According to Mr. Kao Kim Hourn, Minister accompanying the Prime Minister, during the meeting, Mr. Chhin Yun informed Samdech Techo that this was his second visit to Cambodia. He noted that Cambodia has developed economically, especially in Phnom Penh.
Mr. Chhin Yun said that in the past, there have been two Chinese banks that have supported Cambodia's development, both of which have helped Cambodia's economic growth. He said that economics and politics are inseparable and that Cambodia has played an important role in maintaining regional stability and is also a close friend of ASEAN and China in promoting cooperation. Local friendship.
He asked Samdech Techo to make sure that the Royal Government of Cambodia uses the Chinese currency in the Cambodian market as well, which will be able to attract more Chinese and other investors to Cambodia. Chinese companies aim to make the Cambodian economy stronger by supporting and boosting Cambodia's economic growth.
