1st-12th generation students of Tayama Business School gather after success in their respective jobs
(Phnom Penh): Giving Power Training, a company set up to supply Tayama Business School, recently held a student reunion at Koh Pich Center with the participation of students from all generations. Twelfth, about 800 people.
Tayama Business School was established on October 25, 2007 by the Japanese founder, Mr. Yamato Shio, who is now 12 years old.
The course consists of a full-day course focusing on the Japanese language and the Japanese way of working, which enrolls more than 200 students each year, the largest number in Cambodia.
Today, there are many young students who have graduated and become company presidents and leaders in Japanese enterprises across the country. For those who want to work as a trainee to Japan, you can also go through Grove Power.
Please be informed that this gathering is now for all generations of students to create a closer relationship between senior and junior students in helping each other, which is a solid foundation for Cambodia.
