(Phnom Penh): The Royal Cambodian Armed Forces (RCAF) plans to hold a six-day "Hanuman Meas 2019" live-fire test exercise from May 3 to 8, 2019 in Chum Kiri district, Kampot province. Increase the capacity of the Cambodian defense sector.
The opening ceremony of the "Hanuman Meas 2019" will be presided over by Lt. Gen. Hun Manet, Deputy Commander and Commander of the Army, while the closing day will be presided over by General Vong Pisen, Commander-in-Chief of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces. .
Lt. Gen. Mao Phalla, spokesman for the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces (RCAF), confirmed to Fresh News this morning, April 24, 2019, that the exercise involved all units under the Army, and this exercise is Held annually by the Cambodian army itself, there is no participation of the armies of any country.
He said that for the exercise "Hanuman Meas 2019" will have more than 1,000 troops, but for the exercise in 2019 organized by the Army and smaller than 2018, unlike the General. Royal Cambodian Armed Forces Command This exercise is to enhance the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces' ability to defend the motherland from any eventual aggression.
According to the Ministry of National Defense's website, the "Hanuman Gold 2018" live-fire test firing exercise featured a large number of artillery and reaction weapons, and the live-fire training was conducted to Increase the capacity of the army without any threat, as the country is peaceful, the army must take the opportunity to train more to make the army more qualified and capable.
