(Phnom Penh): Emerging businesses in the field of technology in Cambodia are vibrant and full of energy, along with a culture of entrepreneurship and many opportunities for entrepreneurs.
The public and the tech community were highlighted in this report in October 2018 during the Cambodia Technology Summit in Phnom Penh.
"I am pleased that through the Capacity Building and Research and Development Fund of the Ministry of Multidisciplinary, Training Communities, the Private Sector and the Emerging Business Community, Cambodia can present an unprecedented level of growth," he said. "Coming of a newly formed digital business company and a clear understanding of the potential for the future."
The report, which brings together the views of more than 120 stakeholders in the IT technology business, provides an overview of the emerging technology business sector and the evolution of the digital technology sector over the past three to four years. Identify the fundamentals needed to help drive a strong digital entrepreneurship sector.
This report highlights that Cambodia has the potential to create a positive environment for start-ups to grow and address some of the basic needs of the economy, as well as some underdeveloped sectors. Opportunity for innovation and growth.
"Digital technology, a quiet sector, has grown rapidly in recent years," he said. "Despite the positive momentum in this sector, the digital technology sector continues to have potential, which is why this report provides a good foundation for many stakeholders to help push Cambodia into the digital age."
The report also highlights the challenges that emerging digital companies will face, particularly regarding the lack of skills and experience of the workforce, and that experts with in-depth technical knowledge or specific experience remain limited. Still.
Introducing investors to potential companies for investment is also considered to be a major challenge in Cambodia, especially in ensuring that start-ups are safe to invest in.
In conclusion, this report proposes a multilateral solution to set future policies for the technology business, create an optimal business environment and develop talent in the technology business.
(Tbong Khmum): In order to ensure the health of the consumers who consume food products for sale on the market, Mr. Meas Mora, President of Camcontrol Tbong Khmum Branch, on April 23, 2019, led CamControl officials in cooperation with the Provincial Department of Commerce. Inspected and strengthened the quality and safety of goods at two markets: Stung Market in Ponhea Krek District and Chong Cheach Market in Tbong Khmum Province.
On the same day, Mr. Meas Mora, together with professional officers, continued to inspect the quality of goods, labels, packaging and date of use on goods sold in Chong Cheach market in Tambor district, as a result, CamControl officers found and confiscated drinks. Out of date, some can be used for disposal, including 10 bottles of soy sauce and mixed drinks, including orange juice, milk, 62 bottles of lemon tea and 23 cans.
At the same time, Mr. Meas Mora, together with CamControl officers, posted a poster explaining how to select and display food and beverages, as well as educating and instructing traders before selling goods to check and know. Clear sources and display of good quality goods with the correct label and strictly prohibit goods without a specific date, especially after the expiration date, which is contrary to the provisions of the law.
Minister of Education: Cambodia can develop education in the digital context like developed countries, but we lack resources
(Phnom Penh): In front of the National Assembly-Senate Expert Committee, National-International Cooperation Partnership and many national and international guests, Mr. Hang Chuon Naron, Minister of Education, Youth and Sports, affirmed that Cambodia can develop the education sector in the context Digital is like developed countries, but only this country still lacks resources.
The Minister's statement was made on the occasion that the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports has collaborated with the National Assembly's Committee on Education, Youth, Sports, Cult, Religious Affairs, Culture and Tourism or the Seventh Committee to organize a workshop on "Evolution of Education in the Digital Context". In the framework of Global and Cambodia "in the morning of April 22, 2019.
The workshop, which was held at the National Assembly, was an important consultation forum to gain additional input, share experiences, knowledge, ideas for the development of the education sector in Cambodia, and future visions for Cambodia's readiness to respond. Will the new turn of the digital age and the fourth generation industrial revolution within the framework of Buddhist society.
The Minister of Education said that if Cambodia wants to have 21st century schools, it must have 21st century teachers. In this regard, he would like to see all teachers need to strengthen their capacity to be ready to accept the development of education in Cambodia and the vision for the future to respond to the new turn of the digital age and the fourth generation industrial revolution within the framework of Buddhist society.
He added, "We need to make the school a place that teaches students to think and solve problems, no longer a place to teach." "Our move forward is to strengthen the foundations, both capital and solid, and we need to do it step by step and systematically."
However, in order for the development of education in the digital context to work across the country, Hang Chuon Naron did not specify how much it would cost and how long it would take. He only revealed that any location that can work will be put into operation immediately.
Regarding this workshop, Mr. HUN Many, Chairman of the Seventh Committee of the National Assembly, believes that it is a starting point for a comprehensive discussion on the preparation in the field of education for the digital age. The views, knowledge and recommendations in the workshop will be the basis for further consideration for the future direction of education in Cambodia.
According to Mr. HUN Many, he congratulated and highly appreciated the excellent results of the whole workshop, which is the initiative of the National Assembly of the 6th legislature to continue to monitor, promote, cooperate and discuss with the executive branch of the Ministry. Educate Youth and Sports as a staff to contribute to the efficiency and effectiveness of public services in the field of education, as well as to discuss relevant perspectives.
At the same time, Mr. Nguon Nhel, First Vice President of the National Assembly, affirmed that Cambodia is also ready for the transition to the digital age, as the Rectangular Strategy Phase 4 sets out the key priorities in the 6th legislature, which are related to Improving the quality of science and technology education and preparing for the digital economy and responding to the Fourth Industrial Revolution.
From my observations and analysis (having been actively involved in human rights organizations for almost 20 years) on the record of their subsequent actions, I can clearly conclude that they are, in fact, an independent group. And only false democracy. Why do I dare to evaluate so?
The group is well-organized and well-organized, including: independent analysts - independent civil society organizations - independent media and democratic politicians. From the beginning, the Cambodian people, including myself, were confused and gave full confidence to these groups, hoping that they were truly democrats and independent to contribute to the criticism of building society or building national policy. Which the government puts out.
But over the past 20 years, it has shed light on the fact that the group has gradually manifested itself as an independent and fake democracy.
Through their own actions, as well as through their observation and exploration, I have come to understand more clearly that this false independence and democracy group is not simple, that is, they have a well-organized network of organizations. At home and abroad, they have divided their positions into all walks of life to overthrow the CPP-led government headed by Prime Minister Hun Sen.
Why can I say that those politicians are wearing fake democracy labels? The simplest answer is:
First, the character of this political group is extremist, not accepting dissenting voices other than Haier. Anyone who dares to speak out will be automatically painted as a Vietnamese-Chinese puppet, etc. On Facebook, if you dare to criticize a little, it will be blocked immediately.
Second, they have the skills of insulting, inciting, fabricating and manipulating to provoke anger, burn anger and conflict, causing all kinds of destruction. Third, the internal leadership of the party and their various organizations are partisan and partisan. Fourth, there are no principles and policies to help develop the country and the people's livelihood, that is, to blame the government, especially leaders like Prime Minister Hun Sen.
As for analysts, civil society and independent media, they are also fake independent groups. To identify as a fake independent group:
First, they are the backbone of the political group that wears the fake democracy label as mentioned above. Even though the political group made a mistake, they did not see it and never blamed it. Instead, only protect those extremist political groups forever.
Second, this group never dared to face the truth or never stood on legal grounds. They have only tricked the story into saying and analyzing it to mislead the public that it is the government's fault. But the truth is, they never know.
The case of land grabbing is an obvious example. Never have these civil society groups or independent analysts educated citizens to respect the law against illegal land grabbing, but they only have to defend anarchy in order to politically exploit their network politicians.
Third, civil society organizations or journalists who work professionally and are truly independent but not within their network are not considered independent by this group.
Fifth, they always urge the authorities to abide by the law, as if they want the country to have the law and to abide by the law, but when it comes time to live outside the law, considering the law as a tool of persecution. Overall, they have been using this network to stir up the country for decades.
However, lately, these false independence and democracies have lost the odds because their true faces have been continuously exposed through law enforcement and public awareness. The real face of this group.
Politicians wearing fake democracy labels are now increasingly homeless and losing ground, while fake civil society analysts and independent media also seem to be losing ground, not because of persecution. But lost due to:
First, they lost the influence of the rule of law and could no longer function as before when Cambodia was in the process of tightening its law enforcement.
Second, because the general public has seen and known the true nature of groups that like to wear independent labels and fake democracy, especially their actions are not like the theories they often recite.
Thirdly, because the Cambodian people need peace and development of their lives, it is important not to allow themselves to be easily deceived by the masked and want to make the situation chaotic again. In such a situation, some false independent analysts are amazed at their own shadow because their actions can no longer be hidden from view.
