(Phnom Penh): PRASAC, a leading institution in the field of microfinance and one of the five largest banks in Cambodia, is proud to participate in and sponsor the "Financial Literacy in Cambodia" outreach program organized by the National Bank of Cambodia. Cambodia on April 23, 2019 at Aeon Mall Sen Sok City.
This program is designed to disseminate the benefits of financial knowledge to the public, with the participation of senior officials of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, Ministry of Women's Affairs, banking and financial institutions, partner institutions, stakeholders, students and the general public. .
In this program, PRASAC participated in showcasing its financial products and services, the achievements of PRASAC related to financial knowledge and creating a happy atmosphere by providing games, answering questions and winning prizes.
Mr. Say Sony, PRASAC's Chief Marketing Officer, stated, “Seeing the importance of financial literacy, PRASAC has been working closely with the National Bank of Cambodia to support the dissemination of this knowledge widely.
In fact, PRASAC has sponsored the publication of the book “Let! Talk about money ”and spread financial knowledge through its website and social media. We understand that gaining financial knowledge is the most important need to help customers choose the right financial products and services, manage cash well, know how to save and spend properly, which helps to strengthen and improve living standards.
In addition, we have integrated this financial knowledge through the PRASAC Library Project with the provision of books related to finance that allow students to learn on their own. "We also regularly practice customer protection in compliance with the principles of universal consumer protection."
Mr. Sony continued, "PRASAC is very happy to join the National Bank of Cambodia in various campaigns aimed at mainstreaming financial literacy to the people." "We believe that through these contributions, the financial environment and financial literacy will be broadened, which will contribute to the development of the national economy."
Please be informed that PRASAC is a private institution and is licensed to accept deposits from the public from the National Bank of Cambodia and is providing many financial services, including credit, savings, bill payment, water bill payment, electricity bill transfer, money transfer, password transfer. Buy phone cards, mobile banking, ATMs, payroll, quick payment and POS nationwide.
