(Phnom Penh): To promote and promote the dissemination of financial literacy in Cambodia, three government institutions, including the National Bank of Cambodia, the Ministry of Women's Affairs and the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, have pledged to expand financial dissemination. Things in Cambodia to the people.
Financial literacy is a knowledge that helps people to manage their daily expenses and is an important motivator in avoiding debt's debt, meaning that when people know how to manage their expenses will not have No debt.
He added that financial literacy is a key factor in boosting the financial environment and protecting people financially, which will contribute to fostering sustainable economic growth. Therefore, gaining financial knowledge is no longer an option but a necessity.
Please be informed that the three state institutions also signed a Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) on the dissemination of financial knowledge in Cambodia.
With the signing of the MoU, Ms. Chan Sory, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Women's Affairs, stated that "The Ministry of Women's Affairs considers financial awareness for women as an important tool for contributing to the promotion of gender equality, especially on "Increase the economic empowerment of women."
Although access to financial support is not the only way for family business development and daily living, financial capacity is an important part of daily business and family development, she said.
"In Cambodia, women are always considered to be important people in maintaining and managing the family budget, and when women have better financial knowledge, it will help to increase the role of women in managing the family budget," she said. "Important to use and better."
Ms. Neav Chanthana, Deputy Governor of the National Bank of Cambodia, said that financial knowledge refers to knowledge and management skills in managing and working financially properly and intelligently. This knowledge and skill is an important part of people's lives and livelihoods.
"People are generally financially literate and have better decision-making ability than people without financial literacy," she said. "Financial literacy will contribute to raising the level of the financial environment by encouraging more people to have access to and use of formal financial services."
Ms. Chea Serey, Technical Director General of the National Bank of Cambodia, said that the MoU between the National Bank and the Ministry of Women's Affairs to contribute to the promotion of financial awareness to entrepreneurs, women and women to understand financial management. Also.
"Factors that motivate the NBC to focus on women, because many studies show that women, if they have the resources, spend more on their families on their children's education," she said. Men, on the other hand, spend on education and child health, but men spend less than women. "These are the factors that we want to strengthen the ability of women to manage the family economy."
