Cambodian Minister of Commerce attends ASEAN Economic Ministers' Consultation and ASEAN Business Council
April 2019 Participated in the ASEAN Economic Ministers 'Consultation and the ASEAN Business Council (ASEAN BAC) and the ASEAN Economic Ministers' Dinner.
The ASEAN Economic Ministers' Meeting and the ASEAN Business Council were attended by the 10 ASEAN Economic Ministers, the ASEAN Secretary-General, the delegation of ASEAN Member States, the ASEAN Secretariat and representatives of the ASEAN BAC, focusing on strengthening ASEAN 4.0, especially the digital economy. For small and medium enterprises, policies and human resources, trade facilitation and regional trade connections.
On Monday evening, the Minister also attended the ASEAN Economic Ministers' Dinner, chaired by Ms. Chutima Bunyapraphasara, Acting Minister of the Ministry of Commerce of Thailand and attended by the ASEAN Senior Minister and Minister of Economy, Secretary-General. ASEAN and officials of the ASEAN Secretariat.
The ministers reviewed and approved Thailand's priority economic sectors as the chair of ASEAN in 2019 under the theme "Strengthening Partnerships for Sustainability", focusing on preparations for the Industrial Revolution 4.0. ASEAN through trade, investment and tourism and sustainable development in ASEAN.
The meeting also reviewed and agreed on mutual recognition of the vehicle and the revised dispute resolution mechanism. The meeting also discussed proposals for the establishment of the East Asia Community, as well as contributions to the Economic Research Institute for ASEAN and East Asia (ERIA).
