The Donald Trump administration on Monday announced that the United States would not continue to grant exemptions to some countries that had previously been able to buy oil from Iran without sanctions when the concessions expired earlier this month. Coming next May. According to the White House, this is to try to make Iran completely unable to sell oil, as it is Tehran's main source of income.
Since November 2018, three of them, Italy, Greece and Taiwan, have completely stopped oil imports from Iran, while the five countries have not done so and have tried to persuade them to extend the delay. More for their favor.
According to the White House, the United States, Saudi Arabia and the United Arab Emirates have agreed to work together to meet global oil demand once Iran's crude oil is completely eliminated from international markets.
