Cambodia issues statement condemning attack on Christian church in Sri Lanka, killing 290 and injuring more than 500 (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): The Royal Government of Cambodia, through the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, has issued a statement. Strongly condemn the brutal violence against churches and hotels in Sri Lanka on April 21, 2019 that killed 290 people and injured more than 500.
In a statement from the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, the Royal Government of Cambodia, with Samdech Techo Hun Sen as Prime Minister, expresses its deepest condolences to the Government and people of Sri Lanka, especially the families of the victims. In the heinous bomb attack in Sri Lanka on April 21, 2019.
"The Royal Government of Cambodia strongly condemns this heinous violence and shall not tolerate this horrific act of terrorism and extremism," the statement said.
The Kingdom of Cambodia is committed to the fight against terrorism and extremism in all its forms and forms. The Royal Government and the people of Cambodia stand in solidarity with the government and people of Sri Lanka in this difficult time and pray for the speedy recovery of all the injured.
