Cambodian PM asks Thai PM to open four more international ports to boost trade between the two countries (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): In bilateral talks before co-chairing a series of events in Poipet, Samdech Techo The Prime Minister of Cambodia, Hun Sen, has asked Thai Prime Minister Prayuth Chan-o-cha to open four more Cambodian-Thai international border crossings.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen said: "Just before the start of the ceremony, I negotiated with His Excellency Prayuth Chan Ocha, Prime Minister of the Kingdom of Thailand, I proposed to open four other ports, including An Ses checkpoint between Preah Vihear and the province. "O Bun, Chob Koki checkpoint, Oddar Meanchey province to Borei Ram province, Phnom Dey checkpoint and another Thmor Da checkpoint."
The four Cambodian-Thai border crossings are still in the corridor, with Phnom Dey in Cambodia's Battambang province facing Khodin in Thailand's Sa Kaeo province. An Ses Port in Preah Vihear Province, Cambodia vs. An Ma Port, Ubon Ratchathani Province, Thailand. Chob Koki checkpoint in Oddar Meanchey province, Cambodia against Saitaku checkpoint, Borei Ram province, Thailand and Thmor Dar checkpoint in Pursat province and Bantha Sen checkpoint in Trat province.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the opening of these additional channels will facilitate trade between the people of the two countries even better. At the same time, Samdech Techo Hun Sen claimed that he had received a positive response for the opening of these gates from the Thai side.
"Recently, we also received a positive response through my request to the Prime Minister of the Kingdom of Thailand, His Excellency Prayuth Chan Ocha and His Excellency the Minister of Transport of Thailand," he said.
