(Cambodia-Thailand): On the morning of Monday, April 22, 2019, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, presided over three different programs on the territory. Poipet city, Banteay Meanchey province, borders Thailand.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen is pleased to join General Prayuth Chan Ocha to pour concrete to connect the bridge across the Cambodia-Thailand Friendship Border (Stung Bot-Ban Nong Ean) to connect the border posts of our two countries - Thailand now.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen thanked the Royal Government and the Thai people for their continued support in building and restoring infrastructure in Cambodia as a neighboring country and in the ASEAN community as well.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the Cambodian-Thai friendship (Stung Bot - Ban Nong Ean) is a bridge between the people of Banteay Meanchey and the people of Sa Kaeo, especially the bridge between the people of Cambodia and the Thai people. Recorded in the history of our two countries.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the Royal Government of Cambodia has contributed to the impact of demining, unexploded ordnance and other taxes.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Samdech still remembers that in response to Samdech's promise with General Prayuth Chan Ocha, Samdech composed 4 songs that our band will be performing soon to celebrate Cambodian friendship. - Thailand is strong and stable.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen concludes his speech.
* Mr. Prayuth Chan Ocha stated that in September 2017, he and Samdech Techo Hun Sen met at an informal Cambodia-Thailand Joint Council of Ministers meeting in Phnom Penh. During the plenary talks, both sides welcomed the start of construction of the bridge.
* Mr. Prayuth Chan Ocha stated that this bridge across the Thai-Cambodian border is considered to be the first bridge connecting the two countries. This bridge is: a clear demonstration of good relations between the two countries, which are no neighbors A close relationship for a long time.
* Mr. Prayuth Chan Ocha strongly hopes that the two sides will work together to make this bridge fully operational soon.
* Mr. Prayuth Chan Ocha stated that he urged the responsible institutions to start the construction of the second border administration building here as soon as possible, in accordance with the construction of the road connecting the bridge on the Cambodian side.
* Mr. Prayuth Chan Ocha stated that after the ceremony of pouring concrete to connect the bridge and the opening ceremony to cover the bridge signboards, the Prime Minister will organize the groundbreaking ceremony for the construction of the customs gate and the road connecting the bridge on the Cambodian side.
* Mr. Prayuth Chan Ocha stated that this bridge is also a symbol of the success of the joint work between officials on both sides and will continue to link the Thai people and the Cambodian people.
* Mr. Prayuth Chan Ocha stated that through this new bridge will promote the coordination of cooperation in other areas such as economy, transportation (connection), society and culture, education, agriculture and tourism towards development and Simultaneous progress.
* Mr. Prayuth Chan Ocha considered the Thai-Cambodian Friendship Bridge (Ban Nong Ean - Stung Bot) as a great achievement for both countries as a gift that the Royal Governments of both countries are committed to give to the people of both countries, including the ASEAN Community. Take advantage of the interconnectedness of all sections, especially proud that bridges and roads have been started and completed in our two governments.
* Mr. Prayuth Chan Ocha affirmed that the principles of cooperation of the Royal Government of Thailand with the Royal Government of Cambodia will continue in good faith and will last forever, and next year will be the 70th anniversary of diplomatic relations between Thailand and Cambodia, which may coincide with the progress of the construction and opening of this new port.
