On this occasion, Dr. Takke Sikasai, Director-General of the World Health Organization for the Western Pacific, expressed his pleasure that Cambodia, for the first time, achieved no malaria deaths in 2018 and reduced the number of malaria cases. Total loss of 42% between 2012 and 2016.
He said that during his visit to Cambodia, he was very pleased with the Ministry of Health for accelerating its commendable efforts to eradicate malaria. The World Health Organization will continue to provide full support and work closely with the Ministry of Health to develop strategic policies and guidelines, promote investment and efforts to eradicate malaria.
With all these results, he strongly believes that Cambodia will eradicate malaria as planned in the final stages of the final malaria eradication line in front of us. In addition, to ensure that all of you, the World Health Organization will continue to support Cambodia, along with all health partners, in eliminating malaria every step of the way towards achieving its goals in the future.
At the same time, Mr. Svay Sam Eang, Governor of Mondulkiri Province, also urged all departments around the province to cooperate, especially the provincial health department and provincial health partners in implementing the National Strategic Plan for Malaria Eradication. Highly effective to eradicate malaria in Mondulkiri by 2025.
