(Poipet-Banteay Meanchey): The former battlefield full of the flames of war on the territory of Poipet City, Banteay Meanchey Province is changing its face day by day in the Techo Sen era. In fact, on the morning of April 22, 2019, the Stung Bot Bridge was concreted to connect the Cambodia-Thailand link, and a new international border gate building was officially opened for construction.
The groundbreaking ceremony for the construction of the Stung Bot International Border Crossing in Banteay Meanchey Province and the access road to National Road 5 was presided over by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia. The ceremony was also attended by senior dignitaries of the Royal Government and government officials, the Armed Forces, as well as a large crowd.
Speaking at the ceremony, Samdech Techo Hun Sen expressed his excitement to preside over the ceremony and considered today as a historic event in which Cambodia and Thailand connected the bridge across the Stung Bot-Ban Nong Ean border.
The Prime Minister also stressed that the bridge is an important link between Cambodia and Thailand, and he thanked Thailand for helping to build the bridge and financing the construction of buildings and connecting roads that facilitate trade. The karma of the people of both Cambodia and Thailand is even better.
Samdech Techo, the head of the Royal Government, added that Cambodia and Thailand could not take the bridge in Poipet to cross both tourists and goods. That is why it was decided to build a new bridge at Stung Bot for transporting goods and a bridge in Poipet for tourists and residents of both countries.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen considered the achievements in the territory of Stung Bot as the beginning of the season that came from the efforts of the Royal Government of Cambodia a few years ago, while 20 years ago, the war zone has become a market area, a recreation area and an area that There is a service.
At the same time, the Head of the Royal Government of Cambodia also proposed to the Prime Minister of Thailand to open four other international ports, including An Se, Chub Koki, Phnom Dey and Thmor Da in order to facilitate travel and Trade While the trade volume between Cambodia and Thailand is very large, up to 6 billion dollars.
At the same time, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also continued to call on the compatriots to keep the peace, which is difficult to find, if not, the bridge is broken, the infrastructure is gone, the houses are run away like during the coup d'etat, so the duty of the people must be together To maintain this peace. Senior Minister Ly Thuch and Ratanakkiri Provincial Administration Hold a Public Forum with Government Officials and the Armed Forces to Discuss Challenges
