The Chief Bishop of Wat Bakan led the Buddhists to hold a worship ceremony to show the traditional religious beliefs to end the Khmer New Year.
(Pursat): Venerable Lay Kan, Chief Bishop of Bakan Pagoda, on the afternoon of April 21, 2019, led all Buddhists at the foot of the pagoda to celebrate the Buddha image, monks, parents, grandparents, ancestors to show the traditions, beliefs, religions in Opportunity to end the traditional Khmer New Year, Kor Eksak 2563 AD 2019.
The Chief Bishop of Wat Bakan also said that the ceremony was held under the direction of Mr. Mao Thunin, Governor of Pursat Province, and with the cooperation of the district and commune authorities to provide security to preserve the Khmer tradition for a long time. Going forward and uniting to create a happy and friendly atmosphere to welcome the new year of the people in the province and the Buddhists at the foot of the pagoda.
It should be reminded that Wat Bakan is a pagoda located in the western part of Pursat province, about 19 kilometers from Pursat. In the past, this pagoda was called Wat Ban Ka Het, so it was called because people always prayed for success. The pagoda has a temple with a Buddha image facing west and a small temple to the east of the temple, this temple is made of laterite mixed with limestone.
