This morning, the Prime Ministers of Cambodia and Thailand poured concrete to connect the bridge across the border and open the railway across the two countries.
(Banteay Meanchey, Poipet): On the morning of Monday, April 22, 2019, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, presided over three different programs on the territory. Poipet city, Banteay Meanchey province, borders Thailand.
For the program of pouring concrete in front of the Cambodia-Thailand Friendship Bridge (Stung Bot-Ban Nong Ean) and the signing ceremony of the joint operation agreement on cross-border railway transport and the handover ceremony (DMU) will be The invitation was also presided over by the Prime Minister of Thailand, Mr. Prayuth Chan Ocha.
After that, Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Mr. Prayuth Chan Ocha will travel together by train from Ban Klong Lek station of Thailand to the railway station of Cambodia in Poipet. After this program, Samdech Techo and Mr. Prayuth will have lunch together.
Mr. Sun Chanthol said that the construction process of the building at the new border checkpoint is scheduled to take 24 months from April 2019 onwards. The opening of the new Stung Bot-Ban Nong Ian International Border Crossing is the opening of a new page in history to facilitate cross-border trade between Cambodia and Thailand and to promote the logistics system in Cambodia.
Following the construction of the Stung Bot-Ban Nong Ian International Border Gate and the connection to National Road 5, the Poipet area will be transformed into a highly developed area as a warehousing and distribution center and a special economic zone. Establish strong physical potential to support local and national investment projects in the Greater Mekong Subregion.
The 386-kilometer Phnom Penh-Poipet railway on the Cambodian-Thai border was built between 1929 and 1942 during the French colonial period. The section of the railway to Poipet was cut off when Cambodia fell into the abyss of the 1973 war. The railway was continuously rehabilitated until it was completed and reopened in April 2018 before the New Year at a cost of nearly 84 million US dollars.
