Please be informed that this environmental clean-up was carried out in collaboration with the provincial sanitation company by using 3 garbage trucks and 3 fire trucks of the provincial police commission to clean the roads in the provincial town to be beautiful. Again. Legal Awareness: The Benefits of Women in the Workplace
(Phnom Penh): During the last few decades, we have observed that women have been actively involved in the development of the society to a significant increase, in which many sectors have shown the active presence of women. Such as politics, education, health, and especially in the field of employment, which covers industry, agriculture, handicrafts, trade, services and transportation.
For this field of work, the rights and interests of women must be protected to promote and motivate women to have the courage to participate and express their abilities more widely and effectively. Women's participation in employment has given women many rights and benefits.
For this week, Fresh News' Legal Awareness Program, in collaboration with the Cambodian Lawyers for International Cooperation, brings together the topic of "Benefits for Women in the Workplace", excerpted from the Cambodian Labor Law and Regulations. Some other relevant laws to explain to the people, students and especially women workers as follows:
Of course, today's women are capable and knowledgeable enough not to lose to men in the work, but because women are the most vulnerable and abusive, both mentally and physically or discriminated against. Therefore, society pays attention to and protects women from those effects through the following images:
Equality at this point refers to the equality that both male and female workers receive from the enterprise or institution in which they work. Women are paid the same as men for the same jobs and roles as men.
For example, if the male worker in charge of garment quality inspection receives a salary of $ 182 per month, the worker in charge of the same garment shall receive the same salary, and both workers Both sexes have to work eight hours a day, or forty-eight hours a week, not including the same breaks.
* Physical and sexual abuse
Employee women are strictly protected by law against all forms of physical and sexual abuse.
For example, some activities that are considered to be physical abuse of women, such as violence by employers, physical contact or touching for malicious purposes, sexual harassment in return for promotion or avoidance. Out of dismissal, etc., as well as other activities that affect the honor and dignity of women.
In case of any abuse or inappropriate behavior on the body, the affected women have the right to file a complaint to the competent authorities to help find an appropriate and timely solution.
Neither the employer nor the employer can dismiss the employee during childbirth or use this as an excuse. At the same time, to facilitate this stage, women need to get some benefits, such as:
• Women who have worked in the enterprise for one year or more are entitled to half the wage from the employer during the above leave period.
1. Rectangular Strategy Phase 3 of the Royal Government and was established by Sub-Decree No. 01 dated January 6, 2016 on the establishment of a social security system for health care.
• For all female workers who are registered with the National Social Security Fund (NSSF) (obligation to register as an employer or business owner) and give birth at a public health facility, receive an additional allowance. As follows:
In conclusion, all female workers who have contributed to the field of labor should clearly understand the protection of their rights and benefits, as well as be able to continue to share this knowledge for the benefit of themselves, their families and other workers. .
