Sri Lankan authorities have arrested seven suspects as the death toll from a deadly bomb blast in the Sri Lankan city of Colombo has risen to 207 and 450 injured. This is according to the release by the AP on Sunday, April 21, 2019.
* How did the attack happen?
No group has claimed responsibility for the attack, and there have been fears that ISIS fighters returning from the Middle East could be the culprits. The Sri Lankan authorities have not confirmed the attack or how many people were involved in the attack, while an investigation is under way.
How did the Sri Lankan authorities react?
The Sri Lankan Defense Minister on Sunday called the deadly bombings an act of terrorism and ordered people to stay indoors for 12 hours from 6pm on Sunday. Until 6 o'clock this Monday morning.
* Reactions from world leaders
World leaders, including the prime ministers of Britain, Turkey, the United States, France, Germany, Bahrain and the United Arab Emirates, strongly condemned the attack and offered their condolences to the families of the victims.
