This video is made to document the details of traditional Khmer boxing, which is based on three basic points, such as the history of traditional Khmer boxing, the will and sustainability of the name of the owner. Some people are familiar with the traditional Khmer martial arts form but are not sure that they know the history of this ancient martial art.
Apparently, Khmer traditional martial arts originated between 1177 and 1181, which is called Atma Yuth, which means one-on-one combat martial arts, and this martial art was created by Jayavarman VII, which has concrete evidence. Through the carvings on the walls of Angkor Wat.
