Watch the details in the video below: Road maintenance and repair is an important contribution to raising the value of Angkor
(Siem Reap): In the management of Angkor, a World Heritage Site and the soul of the Khmer nation, the APSARA Authority adheres to two main principles: conservation and sustainable development, which need to go hand in hand and serve the interests of the people. Each other.
Focusing on the above principles, many historical achievements have been highlighted through the restoration and conservation of temples, the development of tourism, the improvement of people's livelihoods and the training of human resources.
Similarly, the construction of physical infrastructure such as roads, bridges, canals, etc. also play an important role in contributing to the value of Angkor and facilitate the travel of tourists and local people.
In fact, at the beginning of 2019, APSARA Authority has already improved 10 km of main road and many other roads and is also continuing to repair the Cambodia-Korea Friendship Road from National Road No. 6 to Preah Dak village, Preah Dak commune. Banteay Srei and the road from the airport to Angkor Wat.
At the same time, APSARA Authority plans to improve all roads in the Angkor resort to be completed by 2020.
Mr. Yit Chanda, Deputy Director General of APSARA Authority, said that the construction of roads in the Angkor area is different from other places, must comply with international heritage standards and take care to preserve the cultural landscape and original features. Resorts, in particular, take into account the impact of archeology, environment and nature.
Each road construction is always pre-excavated and the size of the paved road is generally not more than 6 meters.
