Four More Cambodian Children Receive Free Heart Treatment and Surgery from Yunnan Heart Hospital, China
(Phnom Penh): Four more Cambodian children living in Bati district, Takeo province, received free heart treatment and surgery from Yunnan Heart Hospital, China. Four Cambodian children, 11-year-old Rin Dane, 5-year-old Chhay Yu, 8-year-old Pas Ratanak, and 11-year-old Meang Srey Leung.
On April 19, 2019, Dr. DUO LIN, Head of International Affairs of Yunnan Heart Hospital, led a Chinese doctor who specializes in Cardiovascular and Echocardiography to cooperate with the hospital specialists. Cambodia-China Friendship (Lok Sang Hospital or Preah Kosamak Hospital) to monitor the progress of the condition of four children living in Bati District, Takeo Province.
Dr. DUO LIN stated that since 2017, the Institute for Behavior Research and Health Studies (YUNDI) has partnered with NGO hospitals in Battambang, Kampong Chhnang, Takeo and Phnom Penh to find children with heart disease. And provide the children with free surgery and treatment at Yunnan Provincial Heart Hospital.
Mr. Phuon Chhim, Governor of Bati District, commended the support of YUNDI and Yunnan Provincial Heart Hospital on the possibility of treating congenital heart disease in Cambodian children, including children living in the district. Bati.
Mr. Phuon Chim hopes that Yunnan Provincial Heart Hospital will continue to cooperate and encourage YUNDI team of volunteer doctors to diagnose children with congenital heart disease and cooperate with relevant institutions to send them to the province for treatment. Yunnan.
It should be noted that since the end of 2017, through the work mission of YUNDI, Yunnan Heart Hospital has successfully provided free surgery to 29 children in Battambang province. In addition, YUNDI seeks funding to join Battambang municipal authorities in alleviating the suffering of families of children undergoing heart surgery and treatment.
