Mr. Taing Sochetkrisna, Director of Preah Sihanouk Provincial Department of Tourism, said that from April 18, 2019, at Ochheuteal Beach, a variety of garbage such as plastic bags, cloth and plant roots were found floating on the beach. Sand. However, officials from the Department of Tourism claim that the waste is not as much as the rubbish that used to float on the beach like last time.
Mr. Krisna said that in this case, the Sihanoukville Municipal Administrative Authority has asked the vendors along Ochheuteal Beach and Ariston Beach to help clean up the garbage or garbage on the upper beach or at their respective stalls gradually. However, if necessary, the authorities will lead civil servants in some state institutions to clean up the waste.
At this point, Mr. Yon Min, Governor of Preah Sihanouk Province, led the officials to inspect the beach and ordered the relevant parties to cooperate to clean up the garbage from Independence Beach, Ochheuteak Beach and Ariston Beach as necessary to keep Good hygiene and beauty of the beach.
CamControl officers take a mobile test vehicle to inspect food items in 5 markets in Chbar Ampov district, found nearly 15 kg of meatballs out of date
Mr. Bun Chamroeun, President of Camcontrol Phnom Penh International Port Branch, said that in this operation, 67 samples of food products were analyzed, including: Seafood, Shrimp, Squid, Dried Shrimp, Ya Her, Vegetables, Cucumber, Lettuce, Lemongrass, Beetroot Vegetables, tomatoes, plantains, beans, cucumbers, prahok, peppers, blood, pork, pickles, prawns, pickles, cabbage, pickles, etc., no products contain banned chemicals.
During the visit to Chbar Ampov market, his team found nearly 15 kilograms of broken meatballs, damaged and out of date, the team recorded and educated the owners to confiscate and burn in the meatballs of CP. 5 kg and more than 9 kg of Thai meatballs.
At the same time, the traders in the market also requested the relevant authorities to stand and inspect all the border goods for imported goods, asking for more attention to be inspected like the officials who came to inspect the market in order to have Confidence together.
According to the President of Camcontrol Phnom Penh International Port Branch, all these operations are carried out regularly in the responsible areas of the branches throughout the capital, provinces and cities under the careful guidance of the management of the General Department of CamControl and Leaders of the Ministry of Commerce.
In this operation, CamControl officers explained to the traders to display the products properly, maintain hygiene, avoid mixing banned chemicals in food, shopping for resale must know the source clearly. Distribution address, production invoice and contact phone number, as well as explain to citizens and traders how to check the date of manufacture and the date (expiration date).
Citizens as well as traders applaud the attention, supervision and education of CamControl officers who regularly inspect goods for chemicals to protect food safety as well as protect their health.
