According to Mr. Mok Dara, Deputy Secretary General of the NEC, speaking at the opening ceremony of the training course on election campaign, election, counting and summarizing the results of the election on the morning of April 18, 2019 is the campaign. Voting shall take place in each capital, province, city, district, and khan where the political party is registered to stand.
The election campaign will be held from May 17 to 24, 2019 from 6:00 AM to 10:00 PM. Loudspeaker campaigning is prohibited between 12:00 noon and 2:00 pm, and campaigning near hospitals and schools or educational institutions is prohibited during student hours. All election campaign activities must end 24 hours before election day.
For the organization of marches or processions by infantry or by all kinds of vehicles in each capital-province-city-city-district-Khan shall be determined twice during the election campaign.
For the election and vote counting, Mr. Mok Dara explained that the council election is a non-universal election in which commune councilors in their positions are elected by the Capital Council, Provincial Council, Municipal Council, District Council. District Council.
This election is different from previous elections in that each voter has to cast two ballots to elect two different types of councils and two ballot boxes:
* The first type of yellow ballot is used for the election of City Council, District Council, Khan Council to put in a ballot box.
* The second type of white ballot is used for the election of the Capital Council, the Provincial Council for putting in another ballot box.
Ballot counting must be conducted directly at each polling station after the close of voting. The counting of ballots shall be done separately according to each type of council, starting from the counting of the ballots that have been elected by the Municipal Council, District Council, Khan Council, and the Capital Council, Provincial Council ballots are counted as Next.
Please be informed that in the 3rd Mandate Council Election 2019, there are 7 political parties competing.
