Officials: The new Phnom Penh Airport in Kandal and Takeo provinces will take 4 to 6 years to complete (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Mr. Sin Chanserivutha, Deputy Director General of Technical and Spokesman for the Secretariat of State for Civil Aviation, confirmed the airport. Phnom Penh International, which the Royal Government is preparing to build on the territory of Kandal and Takeo provinces, may take 4 to 6 years.
Mr. Sin Chanserivutha believes that for the new airport project, it is not yet known when it will start, depending on the social and environmental settlement committee, especially regarding the land settlement, but he understands that it may take about 1 or 2 years to resolve. Finished.
Speaking in a weekly special interview with Fresh News, Dr. Sin Chanserivutha said, "Concerns related to environmental issues need to be studied thoroughly before starting work, so I can not say when. Do that. "But from the start, according to international experience, such an airport takes four to six years to build."
He said that the construction of the new airport, we have thought long and hard, using a long-term perspective to ensure that the airport is free of worries and problems in the expansion.
He added that there had been rumors in the past that the airport could be relocated, but in reality, through a partnership between OCIC and the commission, there was no presumption that it would be relocated. . The only thing that will be addressed is the social and environmental impact, the location of the airport will remain the same and will not change.
It should be recalled that the new Phnom Penh Airport project was announced during the visit of Chinese Premier Li Keqiang to Cambodia in January 2018. The Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen and the Prime Minister of China also presided over the signing ceremony of the investment project between OCIC Mr. Pung Khieu Se and the Chinese company.
Minister of Agriculture Receives Heifer Cambodia President to Report on Project Progress and Further Strengthen Cooperation
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Veng Sakhon, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, on the afternoon of April 18, 2019, allowed Ms. Keo Kieng, President of Heifer Cambodia and her colleagues to meet to report on the progress of the project and further strengthen cooperation. Better operations with future ministries.
She informed the Minister that Heifer Cambodia has been cooperating well with the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries with funding from the Heifer International Program to implement the "Market Promotion for Smallholder Farmers" project. Among the 11 target provinces are Kampong Speu, Takeo, Kampot, Prey Veng, Svay Rieng, Kampong Chhnang, Pursat, Battambang, Banteay Meanchey, Siem Reap and Kampong Thom.
Minister Veng Sakhon praised the achievements of the organization in the past. These achievements have contributed to the development of agricultural communities, increasing household income by promoting productivity, appropriate agricultural production, producing quality products, safety and high market competitiveness, and especially increasing household income, reducing poverty, in line with the vision. Of the Royal Government.
The minister said that this activity also really responded to the policy of the Ministry, especially on the development of agricultural communities, focusing on improving the productivity of agricultural production, crop and animal breeding, crop change. Use appropriate agricultural technologies and inputs, and especially to meet the needs of both domestic and foreign markets, in order to keep up with the new context of economic growth, population growth and tourism.
On this occasion, in order for the project to be even more successful, the Minister advised Heifer Cambodia and other organizations that are implementing projects related to the agricultural sector to consider and consider the possibility of providing support on:
First, to complete the production cost chain from A to Z, in order to increase the value added, expand and strengthen the processing, packaging, storage, drying, cold storage and transportation with technical skills and warranty. To quality, safety, both hygiene and phytosanitary, and especially to reduce the export of raw materials.
Second, study the design of infrastructure to support the production chain and other supply structures.
Third, the development of a sustainable and sustainable agricultural community through the development of appropriate technical knowledge and modern technology to make a positive change in what is customary or completely dependent on a single income.
Fourth, to help prepare the planting plan for the farming community properly and should cooperate with other organizations that have been implementing the project with the Ministry to ensure that the implementation of the project is cellular.
The Minister said that all these factors require all stakeholders to cooperate, implement with high responsibility with professional institutions and cooperate with relevant ministries to achieve goals for the benefit of farmers. According to the request, the Minister agreed to visit the actual project achievements in the target provinces in the near future.
She expressed her deep gratitude to the Minister for taking the time to allow the working group to meet, report, share experiences and agree to accept recommendations that are useful for the organization to continue to implement new successes. In the future.
