Delegation of Jiangsu Province Department of Industry and Information Technology of China Meets Governor of Preah Sihanouk Province
(Sihanoukville): A delegation from the Department of Industry and Information Technology of Jiangsu Province, China, led by Mr. Xi Jinping, Director of the Department, paid a courtesy call on Mr. Yun Min, Governor of Sihanoukville Province this morning, April 18, 2019. .
During the meeting, Mr. Yun Min informed the Chinese delegation about the potential of Sihanoukville and that in 2018, the people in the province will have a GDP growth of 3,373 US dollars. Mr. Yon Min said that Sihanoukville is the province with the only deep-sea port in Cambodia, and every day, about 73 percent of goods pass through container shipping.
The people living in this area are engaged in occupations such as: tourism, industry and agriculture. According to a report by the Sihanoukville Provincial Department of Tourism, Sihanoukville has 175 kilometers of beaches and was named a member of the World's Most Beautiful Beach Club in 2011 in Senegal.
"With the support of our Chinese friends in implementing the One Belt, One Belt and Sea Silk Road policy, Chinese investors are interested in investing in Sihanoukville," he told the Chinese delegation. The sharp growth, especially in the Sihanoukville Economic Zone, has played an important role in boosting the national economy and providing employment for about 20,000 people.
In front of the Chinese delegation, Yun Min expects more Chinese investment companies to invest in Sihanoukville in the coming days.
Xi Jinping hopes that the Sihanoukville Provincial Administration will send a team to promote the tourism potential of Sihanoukville in Jiangsu Province, China in the future.
