On April 17, the capital of Phnom Penh, where the Khmer people had fled as a result of the war between the Khmer Rouge and Lon Nol's army, was occupied by the Khmer Rouge, surrounded by smoke and shells. People in the early hours of the morning smile and applaud the Khmer Rouge's onslaught because they expect the long war of about five years to end.
But things did not turn out as expected, and the afternoon turned to mourning after the Khmer Rouge announced their departure from Phnom Penh without any belongings or food. All. From the afternoon of April 17, 1975, Phnom Penh began to become a quiet city, not a city of colorful lights and fun.
National roads were crowded with people with very sad faces as they were forced by Khmer Rouge soldiers to leave their homes, away from their families, starving and homeless. Overall, April 17, 44 years ago, was the most miserable time for the Cambodian people.
On the other hand, on April 17, 2019, the main roads into Phnom Penh were crowded with vehicles, Cambodians were rushing back to Phnom Penh to return to their homes in Phnom Penh to work, earn a living, study and so on. After meeting relatives and friends and enjoying the Khmer New Year for the past 3 days.
