BANGKOK, April 16 (Xinhua) - A total of 2,702 traffic accidents occurred during the five days of the New Year celebrations across Thailand, authorities said on Tuesday. 297 people were killed and 2,807 were seriously injured. This was released by the Chinese news agency Xinhua on Tuesday evening, April 16, 2019.
Sankranti festival in Thailand was held from last Thursday to early Monday this week for 5 days, in which traffic accidents occurred across the country, but for the province of Chiang Mai in northeastern Thailand. Traffic accidents are reported to be the highest in any province or city, including Bangkok.
