Cambodian Civil Aviation has identified three key priorities for sustaining growth and launching towards the Industrial Revolution 4.0 (Phnom Penh): Senior Secretary of State for Civil Aviation has confirmed that the Secretariat of State for Civil Aviation has identified key strategies and priorities for This 6th legislature, with three out of six priorities to promote the growth and sustainability of Cambodia's civil aviation sector.
Mr. Sin Chanserivutha, Deputy Director General of Technical and Civil Aviation Spokesperson, confirmed the three priority tasks, namely: 1: Strengthening participation in the private sector partnership, 2: Strengthening and improving Connections and 3: Preparing for the Fourth Generation Industrial Revolution (4.0).
1. Strengthening participation from the private sector: * The private sector is an important partner for the Royal Government to invest in services and physical infrastructure. The private sector brings modern technology, innovation, efficiency, transparency and accountability in line with international best practices to contribute to improving public service delivery and risk management, as well as reducing public spending.
* Participation in private sector partnerships has shown positive signs for promoting the growth and sustainability of Cambodia's long-term economic growth.
2: Strengthening and improving connectivity:
* Preparing for the Digital Economy and Response to the Fourth Industrial Revolution (4.0): We know that the currents of scientific and technological progress called the Fourth Industrial Revolution have become a key determinant. Socio-economic development trends in all aspects, with the emergence of both opportunities and challenges for the whole universe.
* Develop programs to strengthen human resource capacity in the aviation sector by raising the quality of higher education, training related skills in the aviation industry in line with the trends of technological advancement and digitalization.
Promote research and innovation in the aviation industry, strengthen the professional skills and orientation of the future digital economy for the Cambodian aviation industry.
Finally! Court orders the detention of a male driver of a car that used violence against women in Kandal Market to Prey Sar Prison (Phnom Penh): Finally, at around 1:30 pm on April 14, 2019, the Investigating Judge of The Phnom Penh Municipal Court has ordered the detention of 43-year-old Lor Bun Pheak, a truck driver, at Prey Sor Prison, awaiting trial.
The decision comes after Phnom Penh Municipal Court Deputy Prosecutor Soeun Moniroth accused a man of slapping a woman and causing her to fall on the floor in Kandal Market for intentional violence under Article 217 of the Penal Code.
Please be reminded that a man who violently slapped a woman to make her fall on the street was sent to court by the Phnom Penh Military Police on April 12, 2019 after the Phnom Penh Military Police interrogated and finished the case. All.
It should be reminded that on April 9, 2019, at the corner of Street 136 and Street 15, Sangkat Phsar Kandal I, Khan Daun Penh, a violent incident occurred when the victim, a weak woman named Touch Linda, was attacked by a man. Slapped her on the buttocks on the street.
Suddenly, the driver pressed the glass down and cursed her with many inappropriate words, so she cursed back, then the driver came and hit her in the middle of the face, causing her to fall. She then went to file a complaint at the Daun Penh district military police base.
After receiving the complaint, the military launched a search to identify and arrest the suspect on April 11, 2019. In connection with the crackdown on the above case, the public expressed its gratitude and admiration for the Phnom Penh Armed Forces.
After a search by military police, the suspect confessed that he was 43-year-old Lor Bun Pheak, a driver for a company on Mao Tse Tung Road, and that he had only been working for about a month. He pleaded guilty to one count of felony criminal mischief.
Most surprisingly, the suspect confessed that he had previously been imprisoned in Prey Sar for one year in 2007-2008 on charges of vandalism by his parents. Imprisoned.
