Australian PM sends congratulatory message to all Cambodians on the occasion of National New Year
The Prime Minister of Australia sends the following congratulatory message: I would like to extend a warm welcome to all Cambodians, both in the Cambodian community living in Australia and around the world, on the occasion of the traditional Khmer New Year.
Celebrating important festivals after the end of the harvest season and the start of another new year, this is a great opportunity for traditional gatherings with family and friends, as well as preparations for the new year. Next.
Likewise, the Khmer New Year is an opportunity for the Australian community to recognize the importance of this day and to wish Cambodians everywhere happiness on the occasion of the celebration. The whole festival.
As Australians, we are fortunate to live in a land of multiculturalism and the freedom to share and learn about these multicultural cultures.
Our commitment to peace and sharing has become an important foundation around our past prosperity and a permanent source of social welfare.
The Cambodian community in Australia is an important part of the above foundation, and I thank you and your efforts to ensure that this multicultural, multi-ethnic and multi-faith society remains a peaceful and harmonious society. One of the best in the world.
With all these words in my heart, I wish everyone in this wonderful New Year, and I hope it brings peace and happiness to everyone.
