Sihanoukville CamControl Officials Call on People to Visit "Sankrant Samuth" Beware of Buying Fresh Seafood Containing Chemicals
(Preah Sihanouk): Officials of CamControl Sihanoukville Branch called on people as well as multi-ethnic tourists who visit "Sankrant Samut" from April 14 to 16 to be careful when buying Fresh seafood or seafood to cook because there may be some traders stealing banned chemicals and some traders steal jelly into those seafood to keep for sale for a long time, see fresh and heavy.
Sihanoukville CamControl officials confirmed that as a result, they found 5 kilograms of shrimp with jelly-like substance that the market vendors were selling to people or customers.
In addition, CamControl Sihanoukville branch officials also continued to instruct traders at the stalls in the upper market and commercial market to understand the food law and to participate in the implementation of the law on quality control, safety of products and services. To avoid harming the health of the people and may face serious laws.
Regarding this issue for traders selling goods and other items in the upper market, said that the market really has some traders selling fresh seafood, stealing chemicals to keep the seafood for sale for a long time. And always look fresh. There are also some traders who pour jelly into fresh shrimp to make it heavier or keep it for a long time to deceive customers.
In addition, when the bad-minded traders saw the presence of Camcontrol officials in Sihanoukville to inspect the quality of food in the market, some corrupt traders always bring fresh seafood with these irregularities. Take it to another location or evacuate immediately to another location, escape from the professional officer, then bring it out to sell in the same market when the professional officer leaves.
Meanwhile, some housewives in Sihanoukville also acknowledge that the fresh seafood and packaged food that some vendors put in the local markets is partly because some traders have stolen banned chemicals to store. Sells for a long time and looks really fresh.
In the case of fresh shrimp, jelly is poured into the body of the shrimp or the head of the shrimp to be sold fresh and to be heavy, etc. Vendors sell in some markets in Sihanoukville.
In addition, some traders continue to inject jelly into fresh seafood, fresh shrimp, etc. to gain weight and look fresh.
In order to avoid chemical seafood, all citizens and tourists, before deciding to buy fresh seafood and seafood sold in the markets in Sihanoukville, must first check to make sure. Make sure the fresh food is safe and free of harmful chemicals.
