Vietnam's immediate decision is good news and joy for Cambodians who are suffering from a shortage of electricity at home on the occasion of the traditional New Year.
The decision to provide 50 megawatts of electricity from the Vietnamese government was made at the request of Samdech Techo Hun Sen through a message at the end of March 2019.
Currently, Cambodia is short of about 400 megawatts of electricity in the dry season due to lack of water, but according to Electricite du Cambodge, this problem will return to normal by the end of May.
