(Phnom Penh): Following the words of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, the Phnom Penh Municipal Administration has been preparing 120 public buses to transport people from Phnom Penh to the provinces and from the provinces back to Phnom Penh. Including 115 buses and 4 passenger ferries in Phnom Penh for free on the occasion of Khmer New Year.
This free activity to transport people to visit their hometown is held for 7 days from 12 to 18 April 2019, departing from 5:30 am. Roads that provide free public buses include National Road No. 1, National Road No. 2, National Road No. 3, National Road No. 4, National Road No. 4, National Road No. 5, National Road No. 6, National Road No. 7 and National Road No. 8.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the decision to release 120 public buses was because he was tired of talking to private companies, which often raise bus fares during festivals. In addition, Samdech Techo stated that during the 7 days of the New Year, people in Phnom Penh can also take free public bus and ferry transportation.
The Royal Government of Cambodia not only provides free public bus rides during the New Year, but also provides citizens with free train rides to their hometowns during the New Year. Samdech Techo Prime Minister expressed his expectation and belief that this New Year, the people of Cambodia will enjoy traveling because the Royal Government has provided free transportation.
