ACE Toul Tompong Branch will host the 2019 US Study and Scholarship Exhibition on May 8
(Phnom Penh): Representatives of educational institutions and universities from the United States will come to Phnom Penh for the Excellence and Scholarship Exhibition, which will take place on May 08, 2019 at the ACE Gallery, Toul Tompong Branch from 1pm. Until 6 pm. This annual fair is free to attend and is organized by IDP, the world's leading international study and information institution.
Students and parents can meet directly with these US educational institutions to learn about study options for all levels, from vocational high school to university, as well as job opportunities as well as scholarship information.
"The US Scholarship and Exhibition Fair is a special forum for those wishing to continue their studies in the United States to receive more specific and direct information from representatives of educational institutions from the United States." This is according to Mr. Mao Sreng, Director of IDP Education in Cambodia.
Officials from the IELTS test center in Cambodia will come to advise on exam registration and IELTS preparation. Representatives from the Australian Center for Training (ACE) will also be present at the event to provide information related to the study of English to prepare for the requirements of educational institutions from the United States.
"The United States is a great learning destination that provides students with a learning environment with a multicultural environment. In addition, students have the opportunity to work part-time while studying. "These are the factors that make the United States attractive." This is according to Mr. Chheang Vantak, Head of the Department of Sending Students to Study Abroad at IDP Educational Institutions.
