(Tbong Khmum): Mr. Cheam Chansophoan, Governor of Tbong Khmum Province, encouraged young people to study hard and promised to provide a computer to any student who passed the A-level exam for the upcoming high school diploma or Baccalaureate exam in 2019.
The remarks of the Provincial Governor were made at the closing ceremony of the 3rd Tbong Khmum Provincial Youth Camp under the theme "Peace and Development" on the evening of April 11, 2019 at Heng Samrin University, Tbong Khmum in Sralop Commune Ponhea Krek District, Tbong Khmum Province.
Mr. Cheam Chansophoan said that investing in young people is necessary for the country to have enough human resources to build and protect the society now and in the future according to the wise political path of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia. And perpetuate this national cause forever.
Speaking about the camp, Mr. Cheam Chansophoan emphasized that it is an indispensable program to develop and increase youth activities in education, because this camp makes young people observe and consider by increasing the spirit of teamwork. Decide collectively, love, care for and protect the environment and responsible individuals in the spirit of strengthening friendship and solidarity, especially participation in maintaining peace and community development of young people.
He added that all young people must join the Royal Government to prevent any inactivity that hinders the process of national development, with young people setting an example in both education and living by adhering and remembering that young people need to make life better. Transparent on the nursery to study and take courses in the path of self-development, family and society.
Mr. Cheam Chansophoan also encouraged all students across the province who passed the A-level exam by promising to provide one laptop per person and encouraging them to study hard for their future, to honor their families, especially as a quality grape. To succeed, bamboo is suitable as a pillar of the nation.
