(Phnom Penh): An unjust case occurred in which a 65-year-old woman was violently beaten in Chamkar Mon district until her face was cracked, her nose was bleeding, her eyes were bleeding and her face was swollen, but the prosecutor ordered the police to release her. Two suspects were released.
The incident of violence occurred this morning, April 9, 2019, at 23, Street 199, Sangkat Toul Svay Prey II, Khan Chamkarmon, Phnom Penh.
The first suspect, Hour Bunthoeun, 51, a father, and the second suspect, Hour Sun Hour, 19, a child, were immediately detained by the Chamkar Mon District Criminal Police for questioning and to build a case to be sent to court. But after detaining the suspect overnight, Deputy Prosecutor Kong Sam Sareth ordered the police to release the suspect without sending the suspect to court. This is according to the professional police officer of Chamkar Mon District Police Inspectorate.
According to Ms. Hour Chantha, the violence stemmed from the fact that she called a electrician at the electrical shop at her home where the incident took place. Suddenly, the suspect named Hour Bunthoeun came angrily to ask who set the fire? Then he and his son beat the electrician, beat the electrician and beat her.
After the incident, Ms. Hour Chantha filed a complaint at the Tuol Svay Prey II Administrative Police Station and immediately arrested the two suspects and took them to the Chamkar Mon District Police Inspectorate for questioning. But unfortunately, the victim did not even bleed from the wound, the suspect may come out to scare the victim further.
