(Phnom Penh): The Governor of Phnom Penh, Mr. Khuong Sreng, said that the Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen released 120 public buses to transport people to their hometowns for free is a spirit of care to solve difficulties. Of the people by Samdech Techo is not just for the vote, as the accusation of a group of people with biased views.
The above statement was made when Mr. Khuong Sreng went to take the people to take the free public bus ride to their hometown on the morning of April 12, 2019.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen has decided to release 120 public buses to transport people to visit their hometowns during the New Year from 12 to 18 April. The release of this car in order to help solve the difficulties of people who have to spend a lot of money for bus fares every time there are major national holidays such as New Year and Pchum Ben.
Samdech Techo Prime Minister also did this on the occasion of New Year and Pchum Ben in 2018. Samdech Techo's decision in 2018, the year of the national election, led to criticism that Samdech acted to buy hearts and draw votes from the people.
