(Phnom Penh): The management and staff of the Cambodian Hospital on April 12, 2019 organized a traditional dance performance and a traditional game to celebrate the Khmer New Year, which will take place on This coming April 14-15-16.
Trud Dance is a traditional dance that has been inherited from the Samre people for thousands of years and originated in Siem Reap. In the Angkorian era, the Samre people performed this traditional dance for the king on the occasion of the New Year and as a confirmation of the end of the old year and the glorious new year to the King.
Therefore, every year, especially during the traditional Khmer New Year, the traditional dance is always performed at home or at the pagoda to cut off the evil elements of the old year and move to the new year to the present.
