(Phnom Penh): Pursuant to the Royal Government's order on immediate remedial measures for the impact of the transmission line project in Phnom Penh, on the afternoon of April 11, 2019, the Capital Administration held an emergency meeting with relevant authorities, including the Electricity Authority. Local Khan, Sangkat and other stakeholders to review and resolve in accordance with the policy and order of the Royal Government.
During the meeting, relevant officials also highlighted the impact of the 230 kV and 500 kV transmission lines, which are the priority transmission lines that the Royal Government is paying close attention to to transmit power from southern sources to the national grid. Overall, especially in Phnom Penh and must be completed before the end of January 2020.
In order to ensure that the construction of this transmission line project is completed and implemented according to the plan, the Royal Government has issued regulations to the relevant ministries and institutions and the four capital-provincial authorities: Phnom Penh, Kandal, Kampong Speu and Sihanoukville. That is to direct the work to deal with the impact directly.
Pursuant to the above regulations, the Governor of Phnom Penh, Mr. Khuong Sreng, also urged the relevant officials to implement with the utmost care to address the impact of this project, especially the 10 pillars in the capital to be effective as planned.
The Governor requested all implementing officers to work together to be effective, transparent and fair, not biased or inclined to any individual, to study in detail along the 10 transmission lines, inviting all parties involved. Legal consultation, find a mechanism to resolve quickly and in accordance with the policy of the Royal Government.
At the same time, the Governor also called on the people affected above to be kind, understanding, tolerant and cooperate well with officials in all fields, taking into account the common interests rather than private interests, by accepting policy solutions. Of the Royal Government to ensure the successful construction of the plan.
