Tomorrow, 120 public buses will start transporting people to visit their hometowns (there is a schedule and location of departure buses inside)
(Phnom Penh): Following the words of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, the Phnom Penh Municipal Administration has already prepared 120 public buses to transport people from Phnom Penh to the provinces and from the provinces back to Phnom Penh. Including 115 buses and 4 passenger ferries in Phnom Penh for free on the occasion of Khmer New Year.
This free activity to transport people to visit their hometown will start tomorrow for 7 days from 12 to 18 April 2019, departing from 5:30 am. Roads that provide free public buses include National Road No. 1, National Road No. 2, National Road No. 3, National Road No. 4, National Road No. 4, National Road No. 5, National Road No. 6, National Road No. 7 and National Road No. 8.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the decision to release 120 public buses was because he was tired of talking to private companies, which often raise bus fares during the New Year. In addition, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also stated that during the 7 days of the New Year, people in Phnom Penh can also take public bus and ferry transportation free of charge.
The Royal Government of Cambodia not only provides free public bus rides on the occasion of the New Year, the Royal Government also provides people with free train rides to their hometowns during the New Year. Also. Samdech Techo Prime Minister expressed his expectation and belief that this New Year, the people of Cambodia will enjoy traveling because the Royal Government has provided free transportation.
