(Phnom Penh): A spokesman for the US Federal Bureau of Investigation (FBI) has issued a statement saying the FBI is proud to have a good and long-standing relationship with law enforcement partners in Cambodia.
"The FBI is proud of its excellent and long-standing relationship with law enforcement partners in Cambodia," the FBI spokesman said in a statement.
The statement came after the FBI and the Cambodian National Police signed a memorandum of understanding on strengthening cooperation against transnational crime. The memorandum was signed between Christopher Wray, Director of the FBI Office, General Neth Savoeun, National Police Commissioner of Cambodia, and General Kirth Chantharith, Director General of Immigration of the Ministry of Interior, in Washington on April 5, 2019.
It should be noted that on April 4, 2019, General Neth Savoeun, National Police Commissioner, led a delegation to the United States to meet with the FBI and sign a Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) on cooperation. Law enforcement operations between Cambodia and the United States.
Lt. Gen. Chhay Kim Khoeun, Deputy Commissioner General and Spokesman for the National Police, said that in signing the MoU, the United States will provide some equipment for cooperation and training of Cambodian police officers.
The signing of a Memorandum of Understanding between the National Police and the US Bureau of Criminal Investigation (FBI) is the first of its kind in the past. . This is according to the Deputy General Commissioner of the National Police.
