Samdech Techo Hun Sen's 50,000 Riel allowance makes civil servants happier during the New Year (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): To encourage civil servants who have worked hard to serve the motherland and the people of Cambodia Then, Samdech Techo Hun Sen decided to provide 50,000 Riels to each civil servant, ranging from village level officials upwards, even contracted officials and floating staff also received this allowance.
This 50,000 Riel budget has made civil servants happy, because the money comes from the attention of the head of the Royal Government and helps meet their needs. While happy, civil servants also expressed their respect for Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
Mr. Kimuth is a district security officer on January 7 stationed in the park in front of the Council of Ministers. Frankly, Mr. Kimuth expressed that he was very happy to receive the allowance from Samdech Techo Hun Sen, and this is not the first year that he, like other security officials, has received it.
50,000 Riel for the affluent can be a small amount, but for the security officials above is very valuable because it helps reduce costs during the Khmer New Year. Like security officers, military officials are also happy with the allowance.
Mr. Touch Sovannarith, Assistant Public Order of the Ministry of National Defense, described, "I am very excited and happy that the Prince has supported his children every year. I take this money to the pagoda to celebrate our traditional Khmer New Year. At the same time, I would like to thank both princes, wish them good health, long life and continue to lead their children forever.
Taking a break from teaching students, Yin Ieng, a math teacher at Bak Touk High School, said that in addition to receiving additional allowances from the head of the Royal Government, the head of government also pays full salaries for teachers as well as officials. Other government officials use it on the occasion of Khmer New Year, which helps ease the burden of various expenses.
Mr. Yin Ieng said, "It can also help some of our expenses during the Khmer New Year." And this year, for the fourth month, the prince pays his full salary as well as facilitating civil servants. On the occasion of the New Year, I would like to wish the Prince and his family to meet only the four blessings and blessings: age, class and happiness, do not be wasted.
Teacher Chhun Sopheap stated: “Yes, I am very happy because I donated 50,000 Riels during the Khmer New Year, it helped a lot, I got more money, I got more income, because 4 months is a time when I need a lot of money. So thank you very much prince, because it is very valuable and very happy. I wish the prince and his family all the best. ”
As for the traffic police officer, Colonel Meas Sina, said: 50,000 is more than enough money for the family to buy oxygen at the New Year. I would like to thank the Prince for always taking care of his subordinates and wish him good health. I would also like to wish all citizens to be very careful in their travels and wish everyone a safe journey. ”
