(Phnom Penh): After going through the first and only fuel test system from Caltex called Boroscope test in October 2018, made the driver understand the type The fuel they use for their vehicles is very different.
The results of inspections of 162 submersibles from 23 vehicles in Cambodia show that Caltex-fueled vehicles achieved an average score of 9.7 out of 10 on engine cleanliness.
This result is far beyond the competition of competing fuel in Cambodia, which has an average score of only 7.6 out of 10. For regular fuel vehicles, the difference is even greater, with a score of just 7.0 out of 10. The vehicle tested is a 16-year-old vehicle with a range of 200,000 km.
Testing with a Boroscope equipped with a special camera to inspect the interior of the fuel system and see the cleanliness of the main parts of the engine. At the test site at Caltex Bokor gas station, test participants with good or high scores can be seen through modern technology.
"This is the first time I have seen such tangible results, so it is remarkable," said Sorn Pov, a client from Phnom Penh. "When I see this device available in Cambodia, it is very useful and it gives me confidence."
Another customer, Pheng Kith Vattanak, from Phnom Penh, said, "I was surprised because I believed in the fuel I used in the past, but when I saw the actual results, I was very disappointed. "However, I'm happy to know that my vehicle has a problem through Caltex experts."
