The National Police Commissioner General put out four important measures to protect security, order and reduce traffic accidents during the New Year (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): General Dr. Neth Savoeun on April 11, 2019 Four important measures for police officers to implement during the traditional Khmer New Year to maintain security, public order and reduce traffic accidents.
This is according to Lt. Gen. Chhay Kim Khoeun, Deputy Commissioner of the National Police and spokesman for the National Police General Commission, speaking to the media after a meeting to strengthen security and public order on the occasion of the New Year under the chairmanship of General Santepheap. Dr. Neth Savoeun.
The four measures set out by General Dr. Neth Savoeun for effective implementation include:
* First: Strengthening security measures: Efforts must be made to obtain security information in order to take measures to prevent incitement to incite unrest during the New Year or there may be attempts to cause explosions to disturb. New Year or insecurity affects the safety of the people.
* Second: Strengthening crime prevention measures: To ensure the safety of people to enjoy the pagodas, hometowns and public streets, especially resorts with a warm feeling. In addition, there are measures to prevent theft on public roads and village inspections to prevent theft.
* Third: Strengthening safety, order and traffic: Strengthen traffic law enforcement measures, especially early inspection, educating drivers to avoid overcrowding, heavy traffic, strengthen speed checks, check drivers. Drunkenness and some other work related to inspecting the technical characteristics of vehicles and so on.
In addition, to strengthen the main roads, towns, people's entertainment to organize order and help relieve traffic flow from congestion. In addition, fire prevention and fighting work must promote outreach to the people before leaving the house to check the electricity, electricity, electricity and so on.
In case of fire prevention and extinguishing, the competent force must be ready 24 hours a day to intervene to rescue the people when any problem occurs, however, the rescue intervention is not as good as the people themselves prevent .
* Fourth: Prepare the intervention force: In all capital-provincial commissions, it is necessary to strengthen the work of the command, with the command to take turns to intervene in time to ensure the safety and security of the people.
In addition to all these measures, General Dr. Neth Savoeun emphasized in this meeting that the protection of security and order to the people and society is an indispensable duty of the police force and the relevant authorities to implement regulations. Seriously and carefully to get better results.
