(New York-USA): Addressing the Summit of the United Nations General Assembly (UN) to Celebrate the 100th Anniversary of the Establishment of the International Labor Organization (ILO), Mr. Ith Sam Heng, Minister of Labor and Vocational Training Cambodia has stated that it supports future job initiatives to address the challenges posed by technological advances.
The Summit of the United Nations General Assembly was held at the United Nations Headquarters in New York, USA on April 10, 2019.
On that occasion, Minister Ith Sam Heng said that the celebration of the 100th anniversary of the United Nations Special Agent for Labor is a reflection of the ILO's important role in promoting social justice and the rule of law. Create job opportunities for everyone in the past.
On that historic occasion, Minister Ith Sam Heng expressed his strong commitment to cooperation with the ILO. On March 28, Cambodia recently signed a memorandum of understanding with the ILO and other tripartite partners in Implementation of the Appropriate Work Program for 2019-2023, focusing on three main objectives:
First, continue to develop jobs and jobs and enterprises in line with social and technological developments.
Second, strengthening and expanding social support for women, youth and vulnerable groups.
Third, continue to improve industrial relations and labor rights in line with international labor standards, including migrant workers.
