Russey Keo District Governor Orders Deputy Governor and Sangkat Authorities to Take Responses to Receive Citizens' Complaints on the Occasion of New Year
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Chea Pisey, Assistant to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Governor of Russey Keo District, has issued strict orders to Mr. and Mrs. Deputy Governors, on behalf of the sub-national administration officials, to take turns. To receive all complaints from people to participate in resolving in time, even on the occasion of the traditional Khmer New Year for the next 3 days.
Mr. Chea Pisey made this order while presiding over a social gathering to distribute hats, shirts and budget to more than 200 subordinates according to their duties and responsibilities before the traditional Khmer New Year. This evening, April 10, 2019.
Mr. Chea Pisey further stated that Mr. and Mrs. Deputy Governor, Sangkat Chief, on behalf of the sub-national administrative officials, must take turns to receive regular complaints from the people to participate in resolving in a timely manner, even if On the occasion of the traditional Khmer New Year for the next 3 days.
Deputy PM calls on ministries, institutions, national and international organizations to join Economic Council for economic analysis
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Binh Chin, Permanent Deputy Prime Minister and Minister in Charge of the Office of the Council of Ministers, on April 10, 2019, called on ministries, institutions, national and international organizations to cooperate with the Economic, Social and Cultural Council for employment. Analyze the economic, social and cultural situation to perform better.
Deputy Prime Minister Binh Minh made the call as he presided over the closing ceremony of a seminar on disseminating the 10-year achievements of the Economic, Social and Cultural Council and the implementation of a program to assess the impact of legal documents. Held at Sokha Phnom Penh Hotel on the afternoon of April 10, 2019.
"I call on the relevant ministries, institutions, national and international organizations to explore the possibility of cooperating with the Economic, Social and Cultural Council to analyze the socio-economic and cultural situation and conduct research on the topic," said Deputy Prime Minister Binh Chin. "Importantly, it can work even better."
At the same time, Deputy Prime Minister Binh Minh requested all leaders, members and civil servants of the Economic, Social and Cultural Council to continue to work more effectively to contribute to the construction and Develop the nation to be more prosperous.
During the ceremony, the Deputy Prime Minister said that the research conducted by the Council for Economic, Social and Cultural Affairs has been important in relation to integrated crops in agriculture, animal husbandry and animal production, microfinance, etc., which will definitely have an impact. On the development of the nation and on the daily life of the people.
Deputy Prime Minister Binh Minh urges the Economic, Social and Cultural Council to continue this work.
On behalf of the Office of the Council of Ministers, Deputy Prime Minister Binh Minh praised the Economic, Social and Cultural Council for its achievements over the past 10 years from 2009 to the present and thanked the Asian Development Bank (ADB). Sponsored in organizing this workshop.
The Deputy Prime Minister said that in today's workshop, two ministries made a presentation on the implementation of RIA, which has benefited the preparation of regulations for their respective ministries. Ministries and institutions that have not yet established the RIA Working Group should start organizing the RIA Working Group in accordance with Royal Government Decision No. 132 Pillar dated December 26, 2016.
Deputy Prime Minister Binh Chinh asked the ADB to continue to support this program so that the implementation of RIA can be extended to other ministries and institutions, as this work needs to continue to train adequate human resources in ministries and institutions. Nationwide Traffic Law Enforcement Campaign on April 10: 716 illegal vehicles found and 438 fines
