Mr. Hun Many's reaction came after Mr. So Chandet, who was close to Sam Rainsy and was living in Canada, posted a picture of Samdech Techo Hun Sen attached to a picture of Samdech Vibol Panha Sok An, accompanied by the caption: Fate must meet. This message is seen that Mr. So Chandet is insulting the life of Samdech Techo Hun Sen.
As the traditional Khmer New Year approaches, Cambodian families are getting ready to get together and wish each other happiness. Therefore, the insulting message to the life of Samdech Techo Hun Sen was a great attack for the family and children of Samdech Techo Hun Sen.
"I really could not have imagined that such immoral words and actions would be possible," he said. To me, this is not freedom of expression. "Although I do not hate, but for my family and especially for my father and his safety, I can never forget such filthy words and deeds." Mr. Hun Many further emphasized.
With the reaction to the insult to his father's life by Mr. So Chandet, Mr. Hun Many also took an educational message that the Cambodian people will have the dignity not to act immorally and without shame like Mr. So Chandet. Put the interests and future of the nation as a whole without taking different views to destroy the national interest.
Mr. Hun Many added, "Of course, although I am well aware that such immoral, shameless and dignified individuals still exist. I still believe in the maturity of our people and our society that even though we have different ideas, our society really has the right common sense to keep the differences separate when we talk about the interests and future of the nation and the people. Our people.
Please note that Mr. So Chandet always posted insulting messages to the life of Samdech Techo Hun Sen. He is currently awaiting a complaint from a government lawyer regarding his immoral actions. The number of French police officers committing suicide may increase in the face of stress on duty, especially over-demonstrations
PARIS (Reuters) - Police in France have expressed outrage over reports that two French police officers have committed suicide over the weekend, raising concerns about the number of suicides among officials. The police will face increasing stress in their duties. This is according to the release by RT on Wednesday afternoon, April 10, 2019.
According to a report by the French Senate in the summer of 2018, the challenges of law enforcement officials, including the busy schedule, excessive fatigue and tensions caused by terrorist protests, which are considered. That is the reason for some French police to commit suicide.
