Minister Mam Bunheng: Kidney failure is the leading challenge among non-communicable diseases
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Mam Bunheng, Minister of Health, said that kidney failure is currently the leading challenge among non-communicable diseases in the world, as well as in countries in the region with Cambodia. He made the remarks at the opening ceremony of the conference "The Road to Organ Transplantation" at Calmette Hospital on the morning of April 10, 2019.
Mr. Mam Bunheng added that although the rescue of patients with kidney failure is more effective through various skills and the latest method is dialysis, which is mostly in national and provincial hospitals, both public and private in Cambodia. An additional approach that is being done in developed countries such as France is kidney transplantation, a new option for patients where possible.
"The fight against kidney failure has become a major challenge for our government, and a concerted effort to bring this conference together is needed to help address this issue," added Calmette Hospital Director General. In the Kingdom of Cambodia as well as in the region.
He emphasized that the theme of the conference, "Towards Organic Transplantation", was in line with the current focus on health care in the region, which is facing the challenge of prevention. Monitoring and treatment with a focus on more advanced techniques in the treatment of both doctors and patients have received high quality and high efficiency.
