Vital Holds Largest Annual Prayer Ceremony for 300 Elderly, Poor and Disabled in Tbong Khmum Province
Vital's biggest annual celebration has been held since 2016. This large charity event connects the charity program with Buddhism to celebrate the upcoming Khmer New Year. This annual big god ceremony is held at Wat Chhouk, Chhouk commune, Krouch Chhmar district, a poor area of Tbong Khmum province, which is currently experiencing severe drought.
Poor elderly women who come to receive priests from the age of 75 are living in poverty, while others are living in a state of disability and illness, in need of humanitarian assistance. Due to this, the company, which is famous for its Vital charity activities, celebrates the monks and praises the New Year to their grandparents.
Ms. Im Bolika, a member of the Board of Directors of Vital Company, also expressed her happiness at this year's largest devotional program, which was highly praised by the elders of the eight villages, which encouraged Vital to continue its humanitarian program. Extra style for more. Taking this opportunity, she also thanked the team of Chhouk Commune Hall for facilitating the celebration smoothly.
After receiving the revelation of God and changing into beautiful new clothes, an 83-year-old woman named You Ly Heng expressed her happiness, "Today she is very happy because she has a lot of gifts and delicious food. "They are not related to each other, we are really excited."
The program of worshiping the gods has been practiced by the Khmer ancestors since the beginning, believing that this is a way to save a lot of merit in the Buddhist way, because the old man is like a living god for all his children. That's why Vital has brought a 25 R fund to participate in this generous donation to save merit back to Vital customers by participating in the 25 R's success in purchasing a bottle of Vital water.
Vital hopes that Vital will continue to receive support from clients across the country, so that we can continue to fund this annual program of prayer and other humanitarian activities. Another Cane Juice Seller in Kampong Speu Market Wins 100 Million Riel Prize from Echitan Green Tea
(Phnom Penh): A 31-year-old woman named Khat Channary lives in the commercial village of Sangkat Rokar Thom, Chbar Morn City, Kampong Speu Province. Big prize of 100 million Riel from Echitan Green Tea.
The cane juice seller said that she was immediately very excited and shouted to those nearby to come and watch, along with the phone to inform the company through the phone number on the cover. Bottles.
"I never thought I would have such a lot of money before, but now Echitan green tea has improved her life and family," she said. After receiving the big prize money of 100 million Riel, some will be used to build a house for a decent stay and leave the other part to expand more business to support life in the future.
