In addition to the above measures, the district administration will take additional legal action against those who are stubborn and do not commit illegal acts, cause disorderly conduct, and build a case to be sent to court to be punished according to the law in force. Mr. Sok Sokun: Koh Tral was not lost by Samdech Sihanouk or Samdech Techo Hun Sen as alleged by the opposition (Video inside)
To this day, there are still some Cambodians who believe in the interpretation of opposition politicians, cast doubt on this issue, and have a prejudice that Koh Tral was lost by Samdech Techo Hun Sen through the visit. Signing of the Supplementary Treaty between Samdech and the Vietnamese side in the 1985s.
According to the documents he researched, Sok Sokun pointed out that Koh Tral was placed under the control of the Cochinchina administration in 1939 when France colonized Indochina, including Vietnam, Cambodia and Laos. Later, during the reign of Previer, he established a line of administration between Vietnam and Cambodia and established this island in Vietnamese territory.
In addition, Mr. Sok Sokun also quoted the words of the King of Cambodia, His Majesty King Norodom Sihanouk, in response to the "The Daily Mirror" of the Philippines in 1968 to confirm. In the press page, Samdech Norodom Sihanouk emphasized that Cambodia wants peace and stability in Cambodia, abandoning its territorial claims, including Koh Tral, and asking Vietnam to recognize the current Cambodian border only.
Mr. Sok Sokun asserted that the loss of Koh Tral was not due to the death of King Norodom Sihanouk or Samdech Techo Hun Sen, as the island was ceded to France during the colonial period and when Cambodia reclaimed its independence in 1953, France did not. Confirmed the transfer of Koh Tral back to Cambodia.
The social commentator argued that the only way to reclaim Koh Tral was to sue France, which was a colony and the one that divided and demarcated Cambodia and Vietnam at the time.
With an explanation of the reasons for the loss of Koh Tral and how to reclaim it, Mr. Sok Sokun also criticized the opposition, including prisoner Sam Rainsy, that anyone has sued Koh Tral from France? While living in France.
Mr. Sokun claimed that Mr. Rainsy, along with other dissidents, had never complained to the French government about claiming Koh Tral. There are two main reasons for not demanding, the first is the fear of the French expelling them from France and the second is that they leave this issue for political gain from the Cambodian people.
He said that in all countries with territorial disputes such as Vietnam, Thailand, Laos and China, it is often said that this or that region is their territory, but the decision on territorial issues can not be justified. No statement or claim of any country is based on the evidence presented in the relevant historical documents.
