(Kampong Cham): Nokor Bachey Temple is a historical and cultural tourism site located in Ampil Commune, Kampong Siem District, Kampong Cham Province, approximately 122 km from Phnom Penh and 2 km from Kampong Cham Provincial Town.
This temple was built during the reign of Jayavarman VII in order to dedicate to Mahayana Buddhism. However, in later dynasties, the temple suffered the destruction of Buddha statues and parts of the temple to renovate the temple dedicated to Brahmanism.
Until the 16th and 17th centuries, during the late Chaktomuk period during the reign of Queen Srey Sokuntheap and the beginning of the Longvek period during the reign of King Chan Reach, this ancient site was reorganized as a Hinayana Buddhist pagoda, with the central tower dismantled and restored. To a new form with a sharp top shaped like a "stupa".
Despite the war, after Cambodia regained peace, this temple is still a place of peaceful worship by Buddhists and has been turned into a popular cultural and historical tourist destination in Kampong Cham province. Until now, this temple and pagoda Nokorbachey has also become a highlight of the sweet ancient scene for newlyweds who want to go to the pre-wedding shoot before the wedding day.
It is most suitable for people in Kampong Cham and from other provinces to take pictures before the wedding day to show the traditional costumes, such as Chaktomuk, Longvek or Udong, because the people of Kampong Cham consider this Nokor Bachey temple. Like the temples of Angkor Wat in Kampong Cham.
Lieutenant Colonel Moul Daneth, tourist police stationed at Nokor Bachey temple, the number of tourists visiting Nokor Bachey temple resort continues to increase year by year.
Mr. Sok Sophanit, Officer of Kampong Cham Provincial Department of Tourism, said that with the development of tourism, Kampong Cham Provincial Department of Tourism always pays attention to the selling price of traders, especially during big festivals and education. About hygiene issues to the rest of the traders as well as tourists.
Ministry of Public Works and Transport advises all transport operators not to increase transportation costs during the New Year (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Public Works and Transport has advised the Transport Association, Passenger Transport Companies and Traders Transport all passengers do not increase their transportation costs during the upcoming Khmer New Year.
The ministry emphasized that the introduction was aimed at reducing the cost of commuting during the traditional New Year.
In addition to advising not to increase fares, the Ministry of Public Works and Transport has also advised all transport operators not to overcrowd and load bulky goods that are technically unsafe and dangerous.
To avoid possible accidents during the trip, the Ministry has instructed truck drivers to adhere to road traffic laws and understand tolerance while driving.
During the New Year, in addition to the call, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also decided to release 120 public buses to transport people to their hometowns free of charge. Minister Mam Bunheng: We will work together to ensure that no citizen does not have access to health care due to lack of access
(Phnom Penh): The Minister of Health, Prof. Mam Bunheng, said that the health care system must ensure at least essential health services for all people to use, that is, a package that responds to the burden of disease or health problems. Local people, both in health centers and referral hospitals at all levels, both in urban and rural areas, and all services must be quality, safety and efficiency.
At the same time, the health system must ensure that no citizen does not receive health care services during an outbreak due to inability to pay for services. This was confirmed by the Minister on the occasion of closing the third forum on global health coverage in Cambodia at the Phnom Penh Hotel on April 9, 2019.
Minister Mam Bunheng stated that this third forum is an important meeting of health officials at all levels, national and international experts, development partners, stakeholders to reflect on the progress, challenges and opportunities in Cambodia. Its efforts towards achieving global health coverage through the intervention of WHO experts, experts from Thailand and the Philippines.
Moreover, the Royal Government of Cambodia, under the wise and wise leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, has resolutely resisted in the sustainable development of the Cambodian economy, bringing about peaceful economic growth and development. Maximum reduction of population poverty. In particular, improving the health of all citizens has always been considered a priority in investing resources in the social sector.
In addition, the Minister stated, "I note that Cambodia has made great progress in strengthening the operation of the health system on the road to global health coverage, including the expansion of coverage of health services and health interventions." "The public will improve the quality of services and expand the protection mechanisms of health services, such as the Equity Fund program and the National Social Security Fund for health care."
